(window.GAMES = window.GAMES || {})[2005] = [{"t":".hack//frägment","p":["PlayStation 2"],"g":"Role-playing (RPG), Hack and slash/Beat 'em up, Adventure","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/.hack//fr%C3%A4gment","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4r6i.jpg","s":"The commercial success of the Project .Hack franchise led to the production of .hack//frägment.\nThe game uses the same engine as the .hack series with an online multiplayer component."},{"t":"007: From Russia with Love","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube"],"r":"November 1"},{"t":"10,000 Bullets","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Blue Moon Studio, Metro Corporation","u":"Taito","g":"Shooter","r":"February 24, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/10,000_Bullets","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co490o.jpg","s":"10,000 Bullets is an action/third-person shooter in which the gun-wielding player character battles numerous enemies and bosses in different environments. Styled similar to cinematography found in The Wachowskis' The Matrix film franchise and gameplay mechanics in games such as Dead to Rights and Max Payne, the player is given an ability to slow down time and thus dodge multitudes of flying bullets and other obstacles. The first level, \"enhancement\", slows down all action, including the player character. The second level, \"Blitz\", slows down only the enemies, allowing the player to move around at normal speed. The third level, \"frozen time\", halts everything around the player, who again maintains normal speed. By pressing the shoulder buttons, the player can lock-onto and switch aim at the various enemies. Successfully dispatching several foes in a row earns the player bonus points, which can be used at the end of a stage to purchase upgrades like more health, as well as special attacks and acrobatic evasion skills that can be mapped to certain controller buttons. The game features four playable characters (Crow, Alice, Dragon, and Boris), each of which has their own unique set of abilities. Between the action sequences, the player must advance the plot through a graphic adventure-style interface, where certain characters must be spoken to in order to continue."},{"t":"187 Ride or Die","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"August 23","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/187_Ride_or_Die"},{"t":"50 Cent: Bulletproof","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"November 17"},{"t":"7 Sins","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2"],"g":"Action, Indie, Early Access","r":"May 27","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/7_Sins_(video_game)","i":"images/steam-5064890.jpg","s":"7 Sins is a 1-4 player co-op psychological horror game. Search for their items and destroy them in a ritual to stop the creatures. However, whoever touches an item falls victim to the curse of that sin and becomes trapped in mental hallucinations. Resist the curse, solve the mystery, and survive!"},{"t":"80 Days","p":["Windows"],"d":"Frogwares","u":"Focus Home Interactive, Tri Synergy","g":"Adventure","r":"November 4, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/80_Days_(2005_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2fso.jpg","s":"Continuing in the footsteps of his uncle Philias Fogg, Oliver Lavisheart, an adventurous youth, agrees to travel around the world in 80 days or less in order to win a bet made by his uncle. The young man must locate and provide proof of the existence of 4 incredible machines that have been hidden in the four corners the world."},{"t":"Absolute Obedience","p":["Windows"],"d":"Langmaor","u":"Will JP JAST USA/Peach Princess US","g":"BL game, dating sim","r":"April 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Absolute_Obedience"},{"t":"Ace Combat Advance","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ace_Combat_Advance"},{"t":"Act of War: Direct Action","p":["Windows"],"g":"Action","r":"March 15","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/2710","i":"images/steam-2710.jpg","s":"Tomorrow's War Is NOW Ripped from today's headlines, Act of War: Direct Action™ is a frightening tale of suspense, international intrigue and geopolitical military conflict. This real-time strategy experience puts you squarely in control of counterterrorist forces and delivers a first look at tomorrow's war."},{"t":"Adrenalin: Extreme Show","p":["Windows"],"d":"Gaijin Entertainment","u":"1C Company, Frogster Interactive Pictures","g":"Racing","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adrenalin:_Extreme_Show","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2nes.jpg","s":"Adrenalin is a arcade racer/management game published by 1C games.\n\nAdrenalin is a game that successfully blends the genres of thrilling adrenalin-pumping racing and an economic management sim. The aim of a player is to not only become the fastest driver around, but to be a talented manager as well. In the beginning of the game the player has to pick out one of the twelve beautiful young ladies. One of them even exists in reality - she is the winner of Miss Russia contest in 2003."},{"t":"Advance Wars: Dual Strike","p":["Nintendo DS"],"u":"Nintendo","r":"June 23, 2005"},{"t":"Advent Rising","p":["Xbox","Windows"],"g":"Action","r":"May 31","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Advent_Rising","i":"images/steam-3800.jpg","s":"A common legend pervades the galaxy-that of a powerful, highly intelligent ancient race that will one day deliver the universe. They are known as Humans. The Advent of Humanity Begins..."},{"t":"AFL Premiership 2005","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Windows"],"d":"IR Gurus","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment, THQ","g":"Sports","r":"September 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AFL_Premiership_2005","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/obbcfmhqohx5hxkouhlk.jpg","s":"AFL Premiership 2005 is based off the Australian Rules Football game that is quite popular in southern parts of Australia. Based off the official rules and has full licensing from the AFL board. It is a mixture of a few sports, originally developed by a Australian Cricket Coach who wanted to keep his team fit in the off season. It is mainly played throughout the state of Victoria but has now gotten a following in other states.\n\nThe game includes all the 16 teams, 692 AFL players with stats and 8 of the stadiums. The game also includes support for the Cameo Eyetoy (PS2 version) that will allow the player to put his/her head into the game on top of one of the players. Full multiplayer gameplay is supported, using Gamespy for online play, or using the Multi-tap you can have up to 4 players. The PS2 version also comes with a bonus \"100 Years of Australian Football\" DVD.\n\nThe later released Xbox and PC versions do not contain the DVD, but because of the later release changes from the AFL draft have been implemented, even though the overall team score has not been updated."},{"t":"Against All Odds","p":["Browser"],"d":"UNHCR","g":"Educational","r":"May 10, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Against_All_Odds_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3xo6.jpg","s":"Against All Odds is an Adobe Flash video game developed by UNHCR designed to teach players about the plight of refugees."},{"t":"Agatha Christie: And Then There Were None","p":["Windows"],"d":"AWE Productions","u":"The Adventure Company","g":"Adventure","r":"October 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agatha_Christie:_And_Then_There_Were_None","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co25dn.jpg","s":"Agatha Christie's world famous novel, And Then There Were None, is brought to the PC with all of its original baffling suspense!\n\nTen people, strangers to each other, are invited to a lavish estate on an island. Through a recording, their mysterious host accuses each of his 'guests' of murder and proceeds to exact 'justice.' The tension mounts as, one-by-one, the number of people are reduced through the ingenious plotting of the unseen killer. Prepare to play the video game based on the Bestselling Murder Mystery of All-Time!"},{"t":"Age of Empires III","p":["Windows"],"r":"October 18","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Age_of_Empires_III"},{"t":"Alfa Romeo Racing Italiano","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Milestone srl","u":"Black Bean Games, Valcon Games","g":"Racing","r":"May 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa_Romeo_Racing_Italiano","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6pxk.jpg","s":"Alfa Romeo Racing Italiano, known in Europe as SCAR, is a Gran Turismo-style racing game. It is similar to the Gran Turismo series except for the role-playing game elements. The game was lauded for having artificial intelligence superior to Gran Turismo 4. When compared to Gran Turismo 4, Alfa Romeo Racing Italiano has far fewer cars and tracks. All the cars in the game are manufactured by the Alfa Romeo motor company. While most of the tracks are in Italy, a few are in other countries like Germany and the United States. A distinguishing feature of the game is that it models driver development using a system almost identical to a role-playing video game. In addition, cars get damaged, both visibly and in performance, by collisions or by driving off course."},{"t":"Alfa: Antiterror","p":["Windows"],"d":"MiST Land South","u":"GFI/Russobit-M, Russia","g":"Strategy","r":"January 20, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfa:_Antiterror","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/eg1z5dzjcusbnmro2ehh.jpg","s":"Alfa: Antiterror is a strategy video game created by Russian developer MiST Land South and published by Game Factory Interactive in Russia on January 20, 2005. In the same year, the North American company Strategy First published the game as well.\n\nThe story of the game follows a Russian special forces Alpha Group. The player guides the actions of the detachment of an elite squad Alpha Group to fight terrorism. Many jobs in the game are based on historical events."},{"t":"Altered Beast","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Sega Wow, Sega Shanghai","u":"Sega","g":"Beat 'em up","r":"January 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Altered_Beast_(2005_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2iwa.jpg","s":"Altered Beast is a 2005 action-adventure beat 'em up video game for the PlayStation 2. The game is a remake of the 1988 arcade game Altered Beast. While the gameplay still involves the main character transforming into different kinds of beasts like in the original, the story, characters and setting are completely different, along with notable gameplay additions."},{"t":"America's Army: Rise of a Soldier","p":["Xbox"],"d":"Secret Level, Inc.","u":"Ubisoft","g":"First-person shooter","r":"November 15, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/America's_Army:_Rise_of_a_Soldier","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7mzo.jpg","s":"America's Army: Rise of a Soldier is the Xbox version of the tactical first-person shooter developed in conjunction with the US Army. You can create a soldier and advance him or her through an army career from recruit to leader of a Special Forces team. America's Army: Rise of a Soldier also includes online multiplayer, so you can battle up to 16 players over the Internet."},{"t":"American McGee Presents: Scrapland","p":["Xbox"],"r":"February 28","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scrapland"},{"t":"Amped 3","p":["Xbox 360"],"r":"November 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amped_3"},{"t":"Animal Crossing: Wild World","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"December 5"},{"t":"Animaniacs: Lights, Camera, Action!","p":["Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 13"},{"t":"Animaniacs: The Great Edgar Hunt","p":["GameCube","Xbox","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Warthog Games","u":"Ignition Entertainment","g":"Action-adventure","r":"May 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Animaniacs:_The_Great_Edgar_Hunt","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1osq.jpg","s":"Animaniacs: The Great Edgar Hunt is a third-person action adventure, which brings the colourful and hysterical world of the Animaniacs wonderfully to life. Players must guide the Warner brothers and sister Wakko, Yakko and Dot through six levels in a quest to locate the hidden Edgar trophies. Each Animaniac has his or her own special abilities, and each must be used in order to fully explore the luscious landscapes."},{"t":"Ankh","p":["Windows"],"d":"Deck13 Interactive, VIS Games","u":"BHV Software, Xider Games, Daedalic Entertainment","g":"Adventure","r":"November 4, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ankh_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6t3c.jpg","s":"Ankh is a point-and-click 3D adventure game by Deck13 Interactive. It features a fully three-dimensional environment with cineastic camera movement. All content is fully spoken and the soundtrack reflects an authentic Egyptian atmosphere. Humor is an important aspect of the game, and the influence of classic LucasArts adventure games is noticeable.\n\nThe player takes the role of Assil, the son of a respected architect in Cairo. Assil is a party animal but at some point one of his party-nights turned out sour. When he tries to have some fun in the pyramids with two friends of his, he accidentally breaks some urns and thus disturbs the mummy resting in the pyramid. The mummy punishes Assil by placing a death curse on him, and now he has 24 hours to remove the curse and save himself. Later in the game Assil meets the Arabian ambassador's daughter Thara, who is also a playable character.\n\nRequires a game patch which consists of an updated audio .dll file made for Vista to run on Windows Vista or Windows 7."},{"t":"Another Century's Episode","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"FromSoftware","u":"Banpresto","g":"Third-person shooter","r":"January 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Another_Century's_Episode","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co31ad.jpg","s":"Another Century's Episode is the collaboration of Banpresto, best known for their Super Robot Wars franchise, and From Software, the makers behind the Armored Core series. The game is a fast-paced action title featuring characters, mecha and story elements from nine famous Japanese anime. However, while Super Robot Wars is known for combining super robots, like Mazinger Z, and real robots, like Mobile Suit Gundam, A.C.E. exclusively focuses on real robots (later games, however, have include 1-2 Super Robot series in their casts)."},{"t":"Another Code: Two Memories","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"September 26"},{"t":"Anubis II","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows"],"d":"Data Design Interactive","u":"Metro3D Europe, Data Design Interactive, Conspiracy Entertainment","g":"Platform","r":"July 14, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anubis_II","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3isq.jpg","s":"A long time ago, an evil spirit known as Mumm'hotep sank the land of Egypt into eternal darkness. A deadly curse was spread across the once peaceful civilisation. The Gods had to send one man to deal with this threat, the warrior of the sand... Anubis. The player is armed with an arsenal consisting of the scepter of Ra and the Kanopic bombs of fury, with this, Anubis sets off to save Egypt once and for all! In this game, the player will have to face off with legions of evil enemies across nine playable levels of gameplay.\n\nThe player controls Anubis from a third-person perspective through levels with platform puzzles and enemies that are taken out by swinging his staff or locking on to them and shooting energy balls. In each level Anubis needs to find eight pyramids that open up the portal to end the stage. Contrary to the title, this is not the sequel to an earlier game."},{"t":"Ape Academy 2","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Shift, Alvion","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Party","r":"December 15, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ape_Academy_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2ngo.jpg","s":"Ape Academy 2 is the sequel of Ape Escape Academy.\nThe game consists of using a deck of of cards to battle your oponents and reduce their stamina. The cards use a Rock–paper–scissors system in which the winning card will apply a penalty to the oponent. In order to apply the penalty you need to win a minigame. To be able to use cards you need an equal or higher numbers of banana specified in the number of the card.\nYou will be rewarded with a new card whenever you win an opponent. After beating some you can unlock bosses and new islands in which you will find more bosses and oponents until you defeat the antagonist."},{"t":"Arc the Lad: End of Darkness","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"June 14"},{"t":"Archer Maclean's Mercury","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"April 6","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archer_Maclean%27s_Mercury"},{"t":"ArchLord","p":["Windows"],"d":"NHN Corporation, Codemasters Online Gaming","u":"Webzen, Codemasters","g":"Massively multiplayer online role-playing game","r":"March 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ArchLord","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6jvo.jpg","s":"In this massively-multiplayer online game, ArchLord features an advanced player-vs-player combat system, utilizing sprawling free battle areas and special guild battlefields that enables players to battle in fearsome guild versus guild battles. With an ever-evolving storyline of conquest and betrayal, ArchLord presents an epic adventure in which players band together as they quest for the ancient relics of the Archons. Each relic bestows incredible power on those who possess it and when relics are combined they deliver ultimate mastery over the fundamental forces of creation for there can only be one Archlord! Every month, one player will take control of the world, and with it the opportunity to wreak havoc on their cowering enemies as the player gains control of supreme global Archlord powers!"},{"t":"Area 51","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"g":"Action, Adventure, Casual, Indie, Simulation","r":"June 8","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Area_51_(2005_video_game)","i":"images/steam-4423180.jpg","s":"Storm AREA 51 with your friends. Explore the most classified facility on earth. Discover what they've been hiding. Take selfies with aliens and smuggle evidence out before the military arrives."},{"t":"Armored Core: Formula Front","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"December 15"},{"t":"Armored Core: Last Raven","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"FromSoftware","u":"FromSoftware, Agetec, 505 Games","g":"Third-person shooter","r":"August 4, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armored_Core:_Last_Raven","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1w5q.jpg","s":"Two powerful groups, the Alliance and the Vertex, are fighting for world dominance and victory hinges upon the \"Raven\" pilots. You are a Raven, an elite mech warrior who must choose sides between the fighting powers. Ravens face the ultimate decision in the fight for survival, either to fiercely defend their chosen side or fight alone and face the wrath of all Ravens."},{"t":"Armored Core: Nine Breaker","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 13"},{"t":"Asphalt: Urban GT 2","p":["Mobile phone","N-Gage"],"d":"Gameloft Montreal","u":"Gameloft","g":"Racing","r":"November 7, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asphalt:_Urban_GT_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co569c.jpg","s":"Asphalt: Urban GT 2 shifts into gear with six game modes, numerous tuning possibilities, 30 tracks and 36 licensed cars and motorcycles - taking handheld racing simulations to a new level. To keep the action hot, Asphalt: Urban GT 2 features music from Moby and music and appearances from the Pussycat Dolls."},{"t":"Asterix & Obelix XXL 2: Mission: Las Vegum","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Étranges Libellules, OSome Studio","u":"Atari, Microids","g":"Action-adventure","r":"September 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asterix_&_Obelix_XXL_2:_Mission:_Las_Vegum","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5fkx.jpg","s":"Astérix & Obélix XXL 2: Mission: Las Vegum is the sequel of Astérix & Obélix XXL, it was released exclusively in Europe due to the lower popularity of the franchise in the United States and Japan. The game stars the French comic book characters Asterix & Obelix and features spoofs to many classic games, in the same fashion that the comics spoof historical characters and make many cultural references."},{"t":"Atomic Battle Dragons","p":["Windows","Windows Mobile"],"d":"Isotope 244","g":"Jousting/Joust remake","r":"December 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atomic_Battle_Dragons"},{"t":"Atomic Betty","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 25","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atomic_Betty"},{"t":"Atomic Cannon","p":["Windows","macOS","Windows Mobile"],"d":"Isotope 244","g":"Artillery","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atomic_Cannon"},{"t":"ATV Offroad Fury: Blazin' Trails","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"April 19"},{"t":"ATV: Quad Frenzy","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 14"},{"t":"Avalon no Kagi","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Hitmaker","u":"Sega","g":"Board game, digital collectible card game","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avalon_no_Kagi"},{"t":"Ayakashi","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ayakashi_(video_game)"},{"t":"Azumi","p":["PlayStation 2"],"g":"Hack and slash/Beat 'em up","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azumi","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6in8.jpg"},{"t":"Banjo-Pilot","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"January 12","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banjo-Pilot"},{"t":"Bankshot Billiards 2","p":["Xbox 360"],"d":"PixelStorm","u":"PixelStorm","g":"Sports simulation – pool","r":"November 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bankshot_Billiards_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co50jw.jpg","s":"Play nine different styles, from classic 8-Ball to Trick Shots."},{"t":"Batman Begins","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"June 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batman_Begins_(video_game)"},{"t":"Battalion Wars","p":["GameCube"],"r":"September 29","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battalion_Wars"},{"t":"Battle of Britain II: Wings of Victory","p":["Windows"],"d":"Shockwave Productions, Wild Hare Entertainment","u":"Tri Synergy, GMX Media, Wild Hare Entertainment","g":"Combat flight simulation","r":"August 26, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Britain_II:_Wings_of_Victory","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/osyew58ezl1cnmqdhttg.jpg","s":"Battle of Britain II: Wings of Victory simulates the struggle of air warfare over the deadly skies of Britain during July 1940 to September 1940. Options allow playing the game at a strategic role such as supreme air commander controlling at your disposal all of the RAF or Luftwaffe resources at the map campaign level. If fighter pilot instant action is prefer you can also jump into the cockpit of a RAF Spitfire or Luftwaffe Messerschmitt along with many other great airplanes of the Battle of Britain."},{"t":"Battlefield 2","p":["Windows"],"u":"Electronic Arts","r":"June 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battlefield_2"},{"t":"Battlefield 2: Modern Combat","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"October 25"},{"t":"Battlefield 2: Special Forces","p":["Windows"],"r":"November 21"},{"t":"Battles of Prince of Persia","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"December 6","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battles_of_Prince_of_Persia"},{"t":"Beat Down: Fists of Vengeance","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"August 23"},{"t":"Best Student Council","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Best_Student_Council"},{"t":"Bet On Soldier: Blood Sport","p":["Windows"],"d":"Kylotonn","u":"Frogster Interactive, Focus Home Interactive, Digital Jesters","g":"First-person shooter","r":"August 25, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bet_On_Soldier:_Blood_Sport","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3m3l.jpg","s":"Delve into a world where war has become a media frenzy! Survive your battles and bet on your victories!"},{"t":"Big Brain Academy","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"Nintendo EAD","u":"Nintendo","g":"Puzzle, edutainment","r":"June 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Brain_Academy_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co31cc.jpg","s":"Big Brain Academy features 15 activities that test their brain powers in areas like logic, memory, math and analysis. Up to eight people can play with a single game card, and each activity takes less than a minute to complete."},{"t":"Big Mutha Truckers","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 9","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Mutha_Truckers"},{"t":"Big Mutha Truckers 2: Truck Me Harder","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Windows"],"d":"Eutechnyx","u":"Empire Interactive, THQ","g":"Racing","r":"June 24, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Mutha_Truckers_2:_Truck_Me_Harder","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co45vx.jpg","s":"The truckers return and this time you have to get Ma Jackson off the hook after being arrested for tax evasion. Bribe the jurors as you take the roll of Ma's cousin Jacob in a race to make money by trucking and trading. Drive and go almost everywhere at any time in a bigger environment than the original finding shortcuts and new towns to go trucking in. Trading is only a small part of the game and has been simplified to allow more time driving."},{"t":"Billy Blade and the Temple of Time","p":["Windows"],"d":"Iridon Interactive, Nerlaska Studio","u":"Nordic Softsales, Fusion Software","g":"Action-adventure","r":"March 25, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billy_Blade_and_the_Temple_of_Time","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/ahrdufzejr8neap7lzif.jpg","s":"As Billy you'll have to travel to Ancient Persia, The Ice Age, and The Caribbean and hack and slash your way to the top in order to fight The Guardians of Time. Each level challenges the player with platform jumping as well as sword fighting and also simple puzzle solving."},{"t":"Bionicle: Maze of Shadows","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"March 24"},{"t":"Bishi Bashi Champ Online","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bishi_Bashi_Champ_Online"},{"t":"Black & White 2","p":["Windows"],"r":"October 7","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_%26_White_2"},{"t":"Bliss","p":["Linux","macOS","Windows"],"d":"Games for Loving","u":"Games for Loving","g":"Erotic","r":"November 10, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bliss_(video_game)"},{"t":"Blitz: The League","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Midway Games","u":"Midway","g":"Sports","r":"October 17, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blitz:_The_League","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co70pg.jpg","s":"Blitz: The League is an American football game by Midway as an unlicensed extension of their NFL Blitz series. Released after the NFL signed an exclusive licensing deal with Electronic Arts, it was released in October 2005 for the PlayStation 2 and Xbox. This game is the first in the Blitz series to receive an \"M\" rating by the ESRB due to the graphic violence, explicit language, and drug use depicted. Lawrence Taylor, who provides voice acting for the game, serves as its official spokesman. In 2006, a second version of the game was released on the Xbox 360 in October. In December 2006, a portable version was released on the PlayStation Portable (under the title Blitz: Overtime). These versions included the voicework and likeness of former pro linebacker Bill Romanowski. The game was originally intended to be a Wii launch title, but the Wii-version was delayed and eventually canceled.\n\nOn January 22, 2007, the game was refused classificatio by the Office of Film and Literature Classification in Australia, effectively banning the game there. The game was banned as the use of drugs was related to incentives and rewards."},{"t":"Blitzkrieg 2","p":["Windows"],"d":"Nival Interactive","u":"1C Company, CDV Software","g":"Real-time tactics","r":"September 23, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blitzkrieg_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7np7.jpg","s":"As its predecessor and the similar Sudden Strike games, Blitzkrieg 2 focuses on the battles of World War II rather than real-time strategy aspects like base building and resource extraction. The game features many new features and units over its predecessor; the graphics engine is upgraded, allowing for full 3D and the game features over 250 units compared to Blitzkrieg's 200."},{"t":"Blokus Portable: Steambot Championship","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Tomcat System","u":"Irem, Majesco","g":"Puzzle","r":"November 17, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blokus_Portable:_Steambot_Championship","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co70ph.jpg","s":"Blokus Portable: Steambot Championship, known in Japan as Blokus Club with Bumpy Trot, is a 2005 puzzle video game developed and published by Irem Software Engineering for the PlayStation 2 and later ported to the PlayStation Portable in Japan. The PlayStation Portable version was later published outside Japan by Majesco. It is based on the board game Blokus and features characters from Steambot Chronicles (known in Japan as Bumpy Trot). Like in Steambot Chronicles, players are able to customize the appearance of their characters. Each player is given a pile of blocks that resemble Tetrads . Players must place blocks on the board starting at the corners and then extend it from the corners of the pieces they have placed. The game is over when no one can place any more pieces. The player with the fewest pieces remaining wins."},{"t":"BloodRayne 2","p":["Windows"],"r":"August 2","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BloodRayne_2"},{"t":"Bludgeoning Angel Dokuro-chan","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bludgeoning_Angel_Dokuro-chan"},{"t":"Boiling Point: Road to Hell","p":["Windows"],"d":"Deep Shadows","u":"Russobit-M, Atari","g":"First-person shooter, role-playing","r":"May 19, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boiling_Point:_Road_to_Hell","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1mrm.jpg","s":"Boiling Point: Road to Hell combines intense armed combat with exploration and interaction with a vast and seamless open-ended gaming world. In Boiling Point: Road to Hell, gamers travel to the present day jungles of South America and battle competing factions in a brutal guerrilla war. Developer Deep Shadows' innovative game engine streams the beautifully rendered environment, creating a non-linear gameplay experience, with no loading times or separate levels, creating a continuous world spanning hundreds of miles. To make the most of the environment, a massive range of vehicles are at the disposal of the player, as well as a vast array of weapons.\n\nThe wide open game world features an array of different AI factions with which the player can interact, and hundreds of diverse missions to create an original experience each time the game is played. Combined with the vast seamless gaming world, the result is gameplay freedom and replayability on an unprecedented scale."},{"t":"Bokura no Kazoku","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Millennium Kitchen","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Simulation","r":"March 24, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bokura_no_Kazoku","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2fad.jpg","s":"Bokura no Kazoku is a Simulation game, developed by Millennium Kitchen and published by SCEI, which was released in Japan in 2005."},{"t":"Bomberman","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"June 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bomberman_(Nintendo_DS)"},{"t":"Bone: Out from Boneville","p":["Windows"],"d":"Telltale Games","u":"Telltale Games","g":"Adventure","r":"September 15, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bone:_Out_from_Boneville","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1xn1.jpg","s":"After an attack by a swarm of locusts leaves Fone Bone lost in the mountains, he sets out to find his cousins, with a little help from a mysterious red dragon, a couple of talking bugs, and a pretty girl named Thorn. But with hungry rat creatures on his tail, will Fone Bone ever make his way back to Boneville?"},{"t":"Bonez Adventures: Tomb of Fulaos","p":["Windows"],"d":"Bone Artz","u":"Bone Artz","g":"Action-adventure","r":"July 8, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonez_Adventures:_Tomb_of_Fulaos","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1mt1.jpg"},{"t":"Bonnie's Bookstore","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"New Crayon Games","u":"PopCap Games","g":"Puzzle","r":"November 28, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonnie's_Bookstore","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co82uq.jpg","s":"Bonnie needs help updating children's books by linking words together in this clever puzzle game!"},{"t":"Brain Age 2: More Training in Minutes a Day!","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"Nintendo SPD","u":"Nintendo","g":"Puzzle, edutainment","r":"December 29, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brain_Age_2:_More_Training_in_Minutes_a_Day!","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2whx.jpg","s":"Brain Age 2: More Training in Minutes a Day contains all-new activities to challenge a player's gray matter. The title is a series of trainings designed to give the brain a workout. The 17 new, engaging activities are all designed to help work the brain. Whether players are playing simple songs on a piano keyboard or monitoring the photo finish of a footrace, they'll love this new mental workout."},{"t":"Brain Boost","p":[],"d":"Interchannel","u":"Majesco","g":"Puzzle, edutainment","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brain_Boost"},{"t":"Bratz: Rock Angelz","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","GameCube","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 4"},{"t":"Brave: The Search for Spirit Dancer","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"VIS Entertainment","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment, Evolved Games, SouthPeak Games","g":"Action-adventure","r":"September 2, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brave:_The_Search_for_Spirit_Dancer","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7k1h.jpg","s":"Brave: The Search for Spirit Dancer is a 2005 platformer video game of the action-adventure genre originally released by VIS Entertainment for the PlayStation 2."},{"t":"Breeders' Cup World Thoroughbred Championships","p":["Xbox","PlayStation 2"],"d":"4J Studios","u":"Bethesda Softworks","g":"Horse racing","r":"September 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breeders'_Cup_World_Thoroughbred_Championships_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/ozyje5tkhrvj6cipbt9y.jpg","s":"Experience the most realistic horse racing simulation ever created and the only game officially licensed by the NTRA, with Breeders' Cup World Thoroughbred Championships. With thousands of horses, ability to race your own Thoroughbred, play the ponies, and even build your own stable, Breeders' Cup is the horse racing game with something for everyone."},{"t":"Brian Lara International Cricket 2005","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Swordfish Studios","u":"Codemasters","g":"Sports","r":"July 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brian_Lara_International_Cricket_2005","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4rms.jpg","s":"Brian Lara International Cricket 2005 (BLIC) (also known as Ricky Ponting Cricket in Australia and New Zealand) is a cricket video game from Codemasters, available on Xbox, PlayStation 2 and Windows PC platforms. released on 21 July 2005, which was the first day of the 2005 Ashes series."},{"t":"Brigade E5: New Jagged Union","p":["Windows"],"d":"Apeiron","g":"Tactical RPG","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brigade_E5:_New_Jagged_Union","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3mkw.jpg","s":"Brigade E5: New Jagged Union is a tactical game that places gamers in the small tropical nation of Palinero on the verge of a civil war. The mission: hire a band of mercenaries and take control of the deteriorating situation before the country finds itself in complete ruin.\n\nThe story offers players an opportunity to experience three different viewpoints of the conflict or work out the political structure to achieve their own goals in the global domination. Game play for the title is based on an innovative combat system called SPMÂ (Smart Pause Mode) that successfully blends together real-time and turn-based games.\n\nUnlike standard turn-based systems, Brigade E5: New Jagged Union does not use \"action points\" while in turn-based mode, but takes into consideration the character skills and attributes resulting in more natural and diverse behavior of units. Furthermore players can issue a chain of commands that will be carried out automatically.\n\nThe choice of weapons will satisfy even highly demanding fans, with more than 100 accurately modeled firearms, varied ammunition types, grenades, body armor and special equipment. Players will be also able to modify and upgrade weapons by adding various gadgets, sniper scopes, mini grenade launchers, bayonets, etc."},{"t":"Brine Lacrosse","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"SkyZone Entertainment","u":"SkyZone Entertainment","g":"Sports","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brine_Lacrosse"},{"t":"Brothers in Arms: Earned in Blood","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"g":"Action","r":"October 26","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/19800","i":"images/steam-19800.jpg","s":"With its unprecedented combination of authenticity, compelling story and squad-based action, the Brothers in Arms franchise has established itself as a benchmark for military action games, receiving the highest average review scores of any console WWII game to date (www.gamerankings.com)."},{"t":"Brothers in Arms: Road to Hill 30","p":["Xbox","Windows","PlayStation 2"],"g":"Action","r":"March 1","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/15190","i":"images/steam-15190.jpg","s":"Based on a true story. Set during the famous airdrop before the invasion at Normandy, where Sgt. Matt Baker and his squad of 101st Airborne Paratroopers were scattered over the French countryside."},{"t":"Bubble Bobble Revolution","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"Dreams","u":"Taito, Rising Star Games, Codemasters","g":"Platform","r":"November 24, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bubble_Bobble_Revolution","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cocueq.jpg","s":"Originally released as an arcade game by Taito in 1986, Bubble Bobble starred two dinosaurs - Bub and Bob who co-operate to make their way through a hundred levels to rescue their girlfriends. This addictive two player game went on to be released on most console formats. Now the game is reborn on the Nintendo DS with all new graphics, split screen action and the classic gameplay. 100 new exciting levels to explore. All new power bubbles and bubble attacks. Microphone activated challenges and Bubble mini-games. Includes a perfect re-creation of the original Bubble Bobble arcade machine game."},{"t":"Burnout Legends","p":["PlayStation Portable","Nintendo DS"],"r":"September 13","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burnout_Legends"},{"t":"Burnout Revenge","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"u":"Electronic Arts","r":"September 13, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burnout_Revenge"},{"t":"Bust-a-Move DS","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"December 6","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bust-a-Move_DS"},{"t":"Buzz!: The Music Quiz","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Relentless Software","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Party, quiz, music","r":"October 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buzz!:_The_Music_Quiz"},{"t":"Cabal Online","p":["Windows"],"d":"ESTsoft Corp.","u":"ESTsoft Inc.","g":"Massively multiplayer online role-playing game","r":"October 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabal_Online","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6j7z.jpg","s":"Long ago, a powerful group known as the CABAL used their powers to transform the continent of Nevareth into a utopia, ruled by the strong. Constant abuse of power, coupled with in-fighting between members, ultimately led to their downfall, leaving the continent in ruins. During this massive upheaval, nearly every member of the group perished, sparing only seven, including their leader, Faust.\n\nUsing his last remnants of power, Faust saw a glimpse of the future and in his vision, saw once again the near annihilation of Nevareth due to the misuse of power. Now, nearly a thousand years after the sundering, that same evil has renewed and the cycle of extinction has begun. It is up to you to face the wake of destruction that begins to envelop Nevareth, and bring about its salvation."},{"t":"Cabela's Big Game Hunter 2006 Trophy Season","p":["Windows"],"d":"Magic Wand Productions","u":"Activision Value, Zoo Digital Publishing","g":"Sports","r":"September 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabela's_Big_Game_Hunter_2006_Trophy_Season"},{"t":"Cabela's Dangerous Hunts 2","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube"],"r":"November 16","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabela%27s_Dangerous_Hunts_2"},{"t":"Cabela's Outdoor Adventures","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube"],"d":"Sand Grain Studios, Fun Labs, Magic Wand Productions","u":"Activision Value, Zoo Digital Publishing","g":"Simulation","r":"September 13, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabela's_Outdoor_Adventures_(2005_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6dlx.jpg","s":"Join Mama, Papa, Ichigo, and Ringo as they explore as a family on a tropical island.\n\nTake the Hunting & Fishing expedition of a lifetime with 22 adventures across North America and beyond. Stalk monster bucks and trophy big game or stop off and fish the local waters.\n\nExperience the sights and sounds of a true-to-life outdoor adventure where stealth, strategy and technique are of the utmost importance!"},{"t":"Call of Cthulhu: Dark Corners of the Earth","p":["Xbox"],"r":"October 24"},{"t":"Call of Duty 2","p":["Windows","Xbox 360"],"g":"Action","r":"October 25","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Call_of_Duty_2","i":"images/steam-2630.jpg","s":"Call of Duty® 2 redefines the cinematic intensity and chaos of battle as seen through the eyes of ordinary soldiers fighting together in epic WWII conflicts. The sequel to 2003's Call of Duty, winner of over 80 Game of the Year awards, Call of Duty 2 offers more immense, more intense, more realistic battles than ever before, thanks to..."},{"t":"Call of Duty 2: Big Red One","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube"],"r":"November 1"},{"t":"Capcom Classics Collection","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"September 27","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capcom_Classics_Collection"},{"t":"Capcom Fighting Evolution","p":["Xbox"],"r":"June 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Capcom_Fighting_Evolution"},{"t":"Care Bears: Care Quest","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Care_Bears:_Care_Quest"},{"t":"Care Bears: Catch a Star!","p":["Windows","macOS"],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Care_Bears:_Catch_a_Star!","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8zxg.jpg","s":"Care Bears: Catch a Star features 10 of the most popular Care Bears for rainbow-filled fun in their perfect play land."},{"t":"Castlevania: Curse of Darkness","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"November 1"},{"t":"Castlevania: Dawn of Sorrow","p":["Nintendo DS"],"u":"Konami","r":"August 25, 2005"},{"t":"Caterpillar Construction Tycoon","p":["Windows"],"d":"Gabriel Entertainment","u":"Activision Value, Zoo Digital Publishing","g":"Business simulation","r":"September 15, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caterpillar_Construction_Tycoon","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cobn7j.jpg"},{"t":"Chameleon","p":["Windows"],"r":"May 19","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chameleon_(2005_video_game)"},{"t":"Champions: Return to Arms","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Snowblind Studios","u":"Sony Online Entertainment, Ubisoft","g":"Action role-playing, hack and slash","r":"February 7, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Champions:_Return_to_Arms","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4ptj.jpg","s":"An action fantasy RPG that is the sequel to the 2004 Champions of Norrath: Realms of EverQuest, and with the same style of dungeon crawling and hack 'n' slash, Champions: Return to Arms differs from its predecessor by offering the player the ability to fight for either 'good' or 'evil'. With a variety of races and classes to create a character from, the player travels across different acts and different lands combating all sorts of enemies."},{"t":"Championship Manager 5","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Beautiful Game Studios, Gusto Games","u":"Eidos Interactive","g":"Sports","r":"March 18, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Championship_Manager_5","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/n1tf2mf8ofzlzcqrutdd.jpg","s":"The first Championship Manager title since the departure of original CM developer, Sports Interactive, Championship Manager 5 brings this soccer-oriented strategic management simulator to the PlayStation 2 for the very first time. To make the game the most authentic soccer simulation around, the company has hired a specialist agency entirely focused on the creation of player information and statistics, and has completely overhauled the game engine to compute more realistic action in real time. The team has also focused on the Training system, new Match Tactics choices for handling on-the-field gaming, and Action Zones for detailed looks at who best controls which sections of turf."},{"t":"Chaos Field","p":["GameCube"],"r":"December 20","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chaos_Field"},{"t":"Charlie and the Chocolate Factory","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"July 11","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlie_and_the_Chocolate_Factory_(2005_video_game)"},{"t":"Chibi-Robo!","p":["GameCube"],"d":"Skip Ltd.","u":"Nintendo","g":"Platform, adventure","r":"June 23, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chibi-Robo!_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cobx7s.jpg","s":"Like most families, the Sandersons bicker about money and cleaning. Unlike most families, though, they also have robotic spiders, aliens, and talking toys to worry about. Enter Chibi-Robo, a tiny robot programmed to spread happiness. Join him on his quest to restore order to the Sanderson house and SAVE THE WORLD!"},{"t":"Chicken Little","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Windows"],"r":"October 18","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicken_Little_(video_game)"},{"t":"Chuzzle","p":["Windows","macOS","Mobile phone"],"d":"Raptisoft Games","u":"PopCap Games","g":"Puzzle","r":"May 12, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chuzzle","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4k5z.jpg"},{"t":"Chłopaki Nie Płaczą","p":["Windows"],"d":"L'Art","g":"Adventure","r":"March 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ch%C5%82opaki_Nie_P%C5%82acz%C4%85_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co85db.jpg","s":"Boyz Don't Cry is a Polish adventure game with hand-drawn 2D backgrounds, and a loose sequel to the popular Polish comedy movie \"Chłopaki nie płaczą\" aka \"Boys Don't Cry\". The game focuses on two characters from the movie, Fred and Grucha, a pair of gangsters."},{"t":"Civilization IV","p":["Windows"],"u":"2K Games","g":"Strategy","r":"October 25, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civilization_IV","i":"images/steam-3900.jpg","s":"With over 6 million units sold and unprecedented critical acclaim from fans and press around the world, Sid Meier's Civilization is recognized as one of the greatest PC game franchises of all-time. Now, Sid Meier and Firaxis Games will take this incredibly fun and addictive game to new heights by adding new ways to play and win, new..."},{"t":"Classified: The Sentinel Crisis","p":["Xbox"],"d":"Torus Games","u":"Global Star Software","g":"First-person shooter","r":"June 24, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classified:_The_Sentinel_Crisis","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5b16.jpg","s":"Classified: The Sentinel Crisis is a budget video game for the Xbox. It was developed by Torus Games and published by Global Star Software. The PlayStation 2 version was cancelled due to negative reviews before release."},{"t":"Close Combat: First to Fight","p":["Xbox"],"r":"April 6"},{"t":"Cloud","p":["Windows"],"u":"USC Interactive Media Division","g":"Puzzle","r":"October 24, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloud_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5k7e.jpg","s":"A 2005 puzzle game developed by a group of Japanese students, Cloud centers upon a small boy who dreams of flight whilst sleeping in his hospital bed. The player controls the boy's dream avatar as it soars over a collection of small islands. The primary focus of the game is to gather and manipulate clouds in order to create various shapes and ward off incoming rain clouds."},{"t":"Club Penguin","p":["Browser"],"d":"New Horizon Interactive, RocketSnail Games, Disney Interactive Studios","g":"Point-and-click, Adventure, Arcade","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Club_Penguin","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2594.jpg","s":"Club Penguin was a massively multiplayer online game, involving a virtual world that contained a range of online games and activities. It was created by New Horizon Interactive. Players used cartoon penguin-avatars and played in a winter-set virtual world."},{"t":"Clubhouse Games","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"Agenda","u":"Nintendo","g":"Tabletop game","r":"November 3, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clubhouse_Games","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4ac8.jpg","s":"It's game night and everyone's invited. Play more than 20 classic board, card and party games alone, with friends or via Nintendo Wi-Fi Connection. With familiar favorites like checkers, darts and poker, Clubhouse Games is for everyone and part of the Touch Generations library. Video game newcomers will appreciate the easy-to-use interface. Players can challenge up to seven friends with one game card via Multi-Card Play or DS Download Play. Can't play checkers without shouting \"KING ME!\" across the table? The in-game (PictoChat-like) feature takes table talk to a new level. There's no need to lug around cards or boards when you want to play a quick game. Clubhouse Games is one-stop gaming that will appeal to everyone's tastes, whether they're in the mood for bowling, backgammon, bridge or billiards."},{"t":"Cluedo DVD Game","p":[],"u":"Hasbro, Parker Brothers","g":"Interactive board game","r":"October 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cluedo_DVD_Game"},{"t":"Cocoto Kart Racer","p":["PlayStation 2","GameCube"],"d":"Neko Entertainment","u":"Conspiracy Entertainment, BigBen Interactive","g":"Racing","r":"March 2, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cocoto_Kart_Racer","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3g9b.jpg","s":"Cocoto is back for this new challenge! The friendliest of imps now has a well-balanced kart and numerous powers at his disposal. Play Cocoto and his friends in devilish races! Choose among 12 characters and their crazy karts. Race with up to four players on three play modes: Championship, Simple Race, Battle. Beat your opponents with lots of devastating attacks!"},{"t":"Code Age Brawls","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Square Enix","u":"Square Enix","g":"Role-playing","r":"December 19, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Code_Age_Brawls"},{"t":"Code Age Commanders","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Square Enix","u":"Square Enix","g":"Action role-playing","r":"October 13, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Code_Age_Commanders"},{"t":"Coded Arms","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"July 6","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coded_Arms"},{"t":"Codename: Kids Next Door – Operation: V.I.D.E.O.G.A.M.E.","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"October 11"},{"t":"Codename: Panzers – Phase Two","p":["Windows"],"d":"StormRegion","u":"cdv Software Entertainment","g":"Real-time tactics","r":"July 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Codename:_Panzers_%E2%80%93_Phase_Two"},{"t":"Coffee Tycoon","p":["Windows"],"d":"Jamopolis Interactive","u":"Reflexive Arcade","g":"Business simulation","r":"April 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffee_Tycoon","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4sx2.jpg","s":"Coffee Tycoon is a game where you are the manager of a coffee store which you can run to your own liking."},{"t":"Cold Fear","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"March 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_Fear"},{"t":"Cold Winter","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"May 11","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_Winter"},{"t":"College Hoops 2K6","p":["Xbox","PlayStation 2"],"r":"November 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/College_Hoops_2K6"},{"t":"Colosseum: Road to Freedom","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"July 20"},{"t":"Combat Elite: WWII Paratroopers","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"BattleBorne Entertainment","u":"SouthPeak Interactive","g":"Shooter, Role-playing (RPG)","r":"November 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Combat_Elite:_WWII_Paratroopers","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5x7z.jpg","s":"Supported by an army of more than 17,000 US and British paratroopers, you must stop the Nazis from occupying Europe during WWII. Fight with authentic weapons and vehicles alongside brave Allied troops through rolling hills, small farms, and war-torn cities throughout France, Holland, and Belgium. More than 40 varied missions re-create the toughest battles of WWII, including D-Day, Operation Market Garden, and the Battle of the Bulge."},{"t":"Combat: Task Force 121","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Direct Action Games","u":"Groove Games, City Interactive","g":"First-person shooter","r":"March 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Combat:_Task_Force_121","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4t4r.jpg","s":"After years of simmering unrest, Marxist Rebels have obtained a foothold within the Armed Services and found sympathetic comrades to lend both a voice and weapons. While a full-blown coup d'etat is not yet underway, a few early high profile rebel victories could quickly turn the tide. US forces have been called in to put a halt to these terrorist acts. You are a member of task force 121, an elite cover unit comprised of Navy Seals, Green Berets, Army Rangers and USMC Recon personnel. Your mission is to thwart the Marxist Rebels before they can recruit allies and significantly damage US interests."},{"t":"Condemned: Criminal Origins","p":["Xbox 360"],"r":"November 22"},{"t":"Conflict: Global Terror","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Pivotal Games","u":"SCi Games, 2K, Synergenix","g":"Tactical shooter","r":"September 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conflict:_Global_Terror","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co78n6.jpg","s":"In the war on terror, the battlefield is global and only one special ops squad can protect the world's freedom. it's up to you to lead this elite group through deadly missions against and enemy fuelled by hatred."},{"t":"Conker: Live & Reloaded","p":["Xbox"],"r":"June 21"},{"t":"Conspiracy: Weapons of Mass Destruction","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Kuju Entertainment","u":"Oxygen Interactive","g":"First-person shooter","r":"May 19, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conspiracy:_Weapons_of_Mass_Destruction","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7yl6.jpg","s":"Conspiracy: Weapons of Mass Destruction is propelled by the powerful FireWarrior engine as, in first-person shooter action across five sprawling levels, gameplay spans from secret bases in Aztec ruins to military training camps in the Arctic Circle. Players assume the square-jawed role of Cole Justice, an ex government secret service agent, trained mercenary and all-round tough guy, recruited by 'the agency' for one final assignment. According to intelligence reports, a rogue government agency known as 'Hydra' has been developing weapons of mass destruction to sell to worldwide terrorist organisations. The government no longer has control over this rogue agency and it has quickly become an embarrassment in need of urgent elimination"},{"t":"Constantine","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"February 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constantine_(video_game)"},{"t":"COPS 2170: The Power of Law","p":["Windows"],"g":"Action, Adventure, Strategy","r":"January 27","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1913160","i":"images/steam-1913160.jpg","s":"COPS 2170: The Power of Law is a hybrid of RPG and tactical strategy. The central storyline unfolds in the future where the cyberpunk culture and a highly-urban oriented society have populated North America."},{"t":"Cossacks II: Napoleonic Wars","p":["Windows"],"d":"GSC Game World","u":"CDV Software","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"April 4, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cossacks_II:_Napoleonic_Wars","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1v0g.jpg","s":"Cossacks II: Napoleonic Wars is the fourth computer game in the Cossacks series of real-time strategy games, released in Spring 2005 to mixed reviews.[1] This game focuses exclusively on the Napoleonic era, meaning it has a much shorter time span than others in this series, which spanned several centuries. Therefore, fewer technologies can be researched than in other Cossacks games, and there aren't as many different unit types for each country as before. On the other hand, Cossacks II allows a large number of units to be trained and it has many tactical options and an updated graphical engine."},{"t":"Cowboy Bebop: Tsuioku no Serenade","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Chime","u":"Bandai","g":"Action","r":"August 25, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cowboy_Bebop:_Tsuioku_no_Serenade","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5bh4.jpg","s":"The Bebop crew go in search of criminal outlaws to capture for bounties when they get caught up in the story of a mysterious organization, space pirate treasure, and a song called \"Diamonds\"."},{"t":"Crash Tag Team Racing","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","PlayStation Portable"],"r":"October 19","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crash_Tag_Team_Racing"},{"t":"Crazy Frog Racer","p":["PlayStation 2","Nintendo DS","Windows","Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Neko Entertainment","u":"Digital Jesters","g":"Racing","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crazy_Frog_Racer","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3g9a.jpg","s":"Based on the ludicrously popular animated short and cellphone annoyance, this videogame features the frog-like critter that goes something like, \"A'ding ding ding ding ding d-d-ding-ding ding bing BPHACH! B'omm bdom bom d'dom dom bom d'dom bay bom b'dom bom bom b'b'bom bom booooooohm boohm bom, d'dom bomb ahem bom b'dom bom bom b'dom b'dom d'dhom-d'dhom-d'dhom-b'd'd'd'd'd brrhhhh'd'd'd'd'dd'd'd'd'd'd'd'd'd'd bhrrem'd'd'd'd'd'd'dd'd'd'd bhrim'd'd'd'd'd'd'dd'd'd bhran'd'd'd'd'd'd'd'd'd'd'd'dd'd'd'd bhram'd'd'd'd'd'd'd'd'd'd'd'd'd'd'd'd bom-bom-bom-bom bom Bom Booohm BOOOOHM BOOOOOOOHHHHHHHHM WHEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEE!!!!!!!\"\n\nCrazy Frog Racer is a high-speed, high-octane wacky racer. Players can either choose to play as 'The Annoying Thing' and D'Ding Ding their way to victory or play as one of eight other characters on 12 racetracks in single and multiplayer racing."},{"t":"Crazy Machines","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"FAKT Software","u":"Novitas Publishing, DTP Entertainment, Pepper Games, Viva Media","g":"Puzzle","r":"October 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crazy_Machines","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2pt4.jpg","s":"Turn the crank, rotate the gears, push the levers, Use the catapult, explode it, or fly it...From grilling sausages with a pulley, gears, rubberbands and a candle to firing a cannon with a basketball, these wacky brain-teasers will light up your imagination with creative and addictive fun."},{"t":"Crime Life: Gang Wars","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Windows"],"d":"Hothouse Creations","u":"Konami","g":"Action","r":"November 11, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crime_Life:_Gang_Wars","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co25l7.jpg","s":"Crime Life: Gang Wars is a free roaming crime-based beat em up. Mixing action and strategy elements within a gritty, detailed storyline to explore modern-day urban gang culture, the player is cast as a small-time homie who must work their way through the ranks to become a gang leader. Urban culture and the Hip Hop lifestyle is the focus of Crime Life: Gang Wars."},{"t":"Cross Racing Championship 2005","p":["Windows"],"d":"Invictus Games","u":"Invictus Games, Take 2 Interactive, CD Expert","g":"Racing","r":"October 4, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cross_Racing_Championship_2005"},{"t":"CT Special Forces: Fire for Effect","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Asobo Studio","u":"Hip Games","g":"Third-person shooter","r":"March 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CT_Special_Forces:_Fire_for_Effect"},{"t":"Cuban Missile Crisis: The Aftermath","p":["Windows"],"d":"G5 Software","u":"1C Company, Strategy First","g":"Real-time tactics","r":"February 4, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuban_Missile_Crisis:_The_Aftermath","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cod4s3.jpg","s":"Cuban Missile Crisis is a real-time strategy game combined with a global turn-based tactical mode, thrusting gamers into a world ravaged by the military-political confrontation between the USA and USSR in 1962."},{"t":"Cute Knight","p":["Windows","Linux","macOS"],"d":"Hanako Games","u":"IWin","g":"Life simulation, casual, role-playing, Raising simulation","r":"October 13, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cute_Knight","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7lu3.jpg","s":"A Western developed raising sim RPG."},{"t":"Daemonica","p":["Windows"],"d":"RA Images, Cinemax","u":"Cinemax, Meridian4","g":"Action-adventure game","r":"May 13, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daemonica","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1mtb.jpg","s":"Daemonica is a 3D action-adventure game with RPG elements that was developed by Czech companies RA Images and Cinemax. The game is divided into 5 acts. Cinemax and RA Images planned a sequel to the game but it was cancelled."},{"t":"Dance Dance Revolution Extreme 2","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 28","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance_Dance_Revolution_Extreme_2"},{"t":"Dance Dance Revolution Mario Mix","p":["GameCube"],"r":"October 24","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance_Dance_Revolution_Mario_Mix"},{"t":"Dance Dance Revolution Ultramix 3","p":["Xbox"],"r":"November 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance_Dance_Revolution_Ultramix_3"},{"t":"Dangerous Waters","p":["Windows"],"d":"Sonalysts Combat Simulations","u":"Strategy First","g":"Naval simulator","r":"February 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dangerous_Waters_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3o38.jpg","s":"Dangerous Waters allows you total control over multiple air, surface, and submarine platforms in a modern-day naval environment. Take direct control of individual crew stations and also plan and execute combined arms naval strategies from a top-down 'Commanders Eye' perspective."},{"t":"Danny Phantom: The Ultimate Enemy","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"September 8"},{"t":"Dark Age of Camelot: Darkness Rising","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_Age_of_Camelot:_Darkness_Rising"},{"t":"Dark Horizons Lore: Invasion","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_Horizons_Lore:_Invasion"},{"t":"Darkstalkers Chronicle: The Chaos Tower","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"March 24"},{"t":"Darkwatch","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"High Moon Studios","u":"Capcom, Ubisoft","g":"First-person shooter","r":"August 16, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darkwatch","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4oep.jpg","s":"Darkwatch mixes the Western, horror and steampunk genres, telling the story of Jericho Cross, an outlaw gunfighter in the late 19th-century American Frontier who has been turned into a vampire and forcibly recruited by the titular monster-hunting secret organization to fight against supernatural forces."},{"t":"Darwinia","p":["Windows","Linux","macOS","Steam"],"d":"Introversion Software","u":"Introversion Software, Ambrosia Software, Cinemaware Marquee/eGames, Stomp","g":"Real-time tactics, real-time strategy","r":"March 4, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darwinia_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3o5u.jpg","s":"The world of Darwinia is a virtual themepark, running entirely inside a computer network and populated by a sentient evolving life form called the Darwinians. Unfortunately Darwinia has been overrun by a computer virus which has multiplied out of control. Your task is to destroy the Viral Infection and save the Darwinians from extinction."},{"t":"Dawn of Magic","p":["Windows"],"d":"SkyFallen Entertainment","u":"1C Company","g":"Action role-playing game","r":"December 16, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dawn_of_Magic"},{"t":"Day of Defeat: Source","p":["Windows"],"d":"Valve","u":"Valve","g":"First-person shooter","r":"September 26, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Day_of_Defeat:_Source","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co610o.jpg","s":"Day of Defeat offers intense online action gameplay set in Europe during WWII. Assume the role of infantry, sniper or machine-gunner classes, and more. DoD:S features enhanced graphics and sounds design to leverage the power of Source, Valve's new engine technology."},{"t":"Day of the Figurines","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Day_of_the_Figurines"},{"t":"Dead or Alive 4","p":["Xbox 360"],"r":"December 29","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dead_or_Alive_4"},{"t":"Dead to Rights II","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Windows"],"d":"Widescreen Games, Namco","u":"Namco Hometek, Electronic Arts","g":"third-person shooter","r":"April 12, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dead_to_Rights_II","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1ou0.jpg","s":"Dead to Rights II is a third-person action video game developed by Widescreen Games, published by Namco, and released in 2005. It is a prequel to Dead to Rights. A prequel to Dead to Rights II for the PlayStation Portable, titled Dead to Rights: Reckoning, was released in June 2005."},{"t":"Dead to Rights: Reckoning","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"June 28"},{"t":"Death by Degrees","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Namco","u":"Namco, Namco Hometek, Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Action-adventure, beat 'em up","r":"January 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_by_Degrees","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co46rx.jpg","s":"As a covert operative of the CIA, Nina Williams enters an underground fighting tournament to crack Kometa, a shadowy underworld organization. Functioning as the \"sweeper\" of her cell, Nina finds herself tracking a stolen high-tech weapon through a variety of locales to reveal a conspiracy on a global scale. Nina must now face a multitude of deadly enemies, as well as her own past, in order to save the world.\n\n-Control Nina with an intuitive 360 degree combat system\n-Wield a variety of weapons including handguns, sniper rifles, swords and tonfas\n-Burst organs and shatter bones with Nina's Critical Strike\n-Deliver Nina's signature moves outside of the fighting ring"},{"t":"Death Jr.","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"August 16","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_Jr."},{"t":"Delta Force: Xtreme","p":["Windows"],"d":"NovaLogic","u":"NovaLogic","g":"First-person shooter","r":"April 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delta_Force:_Xtreme","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3oc2.jpg","s":"Powered by today's gaming technology, Delta Force: Xtreme brings the classic Delta Force game back to life to face the enemy once more. As a member of the elite Delta Force, prepare yourself to take on over 60 levels of frantic single and multiplayer FPS action, including graphically enhanced missions from the original game, new maps, improved game features, STATS and much more!\nFeatures\nOver 60 levels of combat to test your CQB and long range engagement skills as a Delta Force Operator.\nAs a member of the elite Delta Force re-deploy in over 20 graphically enhanced single player missions — the best of the best from the original game.\nAdditional new single player missions created especially for Delta Force: Xtreme add a new challenge for hardened Delta Operators.\nTake your friends into battle in over 20 co-operative missions.\nOver 20 multiplayer levels include: Deathmatch, King of the Hill, Team King of the Hill, Team Deathmatch and Capture the Flag game modes.\nSTAT tracking — you can now see how good you are compared to every other Delta Force Operator out there and watch your rankings climb as your skills improve!"},{"t":"Democracy","p":["Linux","Windows","macOS"],"d":"Positech Games, Red Marble Games","u":"Positech Games, Tri-Synergy","g":"Government simulation, social simulation","r":"April 17, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democracy_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/vnmitxfs22474wnscinv.jpg","s":"Democracy is a government simulation game that was first developed by Positech Games in 2005, with a sequel released in December 2007 and a third game in 2013. The player plays as if they are the president or prime minister of a democratic government. The player must introduce and alter policies in seven areas - tax, economy, welfare, foreign policy, transport, law and order and public services. Each policy has an effect on the happiness of various voter groups, as well as affecting factors such as crime and air quality. The player has to deal with \"situations\", which are typically problems such as petrol protests or homelessness, and also has to make decisions on dilemmas that arise each turn."},{"t":"Demon Chaos","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Genki, Now Production","u":"Genki, Konami","g":"Hack and slash, Action","r":"November 24, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demon_Chaos","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1ou1.jpg","s":"It is set in feudal Japan in the 16th century and revolves around a priestess who has been given eternal youth until she exterminates all the demons. She has been given charge of a mystical beast from the gods, Inugami, which is controlled by the player. \n \nThe game is in vein of the well known Dynasty Warriors series, in which the player battles crowd after crowd of hostile enemies. The unique aspect of the game is that up to 65,535 enemies can be on-screen at once."},{"t":"Destroy All Humans!","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"June 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Destroy_All_Humans!"},{"t":"Devil Kings","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"October 12","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil_Kings"},{"t":"Devil May Cry 3: Dante's Awakening","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"February 17"},{"t":"Devilish: Ball Bounder","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 16"},{"t":"Dig Dug: Digging Strike","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"October 18"},{"t":"Digimon World 4","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"June 2","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digimon_World_4"},{"t":"Dino Master","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"Office Create","u":"Taito, Majesco","g":"Action","r":"September 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dino_Master","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co30bz.jpg","s":"Dino Master is a game for the Nintendo DS system similar to a fusion of Pokémon and the arcade game Qix. The player takes the role of \"Dave the Digger\", who excavates fossils from various sites while avoiding enemies. The fossils can then be revived into living dinosaurs and pitted against each other in Battle Mode."},{"t":"Dinosaur King","p":["Arcade"],"g":"Fighting, Arcade","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dinosaur_King","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2zfa.jpg","s":"SEGA's second entry into the Arcade card game genre, Dinosaur king is a collectible card fighting game where you can put dinosaurs in fierce battles, with incredible graphics, and colorful and 00's accurate depictions of these prehistoric animals.\n\nIn it's story Max Taylor, his father Spike Taylor and Rex Owen found stone tablets on a fossil excavation site in Africa, the tablets suddenly bursts out voices of the past: Dinosaurs! They request that Max and Rex go back to the past to help them from the Alpha Gang who are capturing dinosaurs. Max and Rex used Dinosaurs and Move Cards and pushed back the Alpha Gang.\n\nFight with an enhanced Rock, Paper, Scissors formula where the winner can attack, and collect dinosaurs and moves to prove yourself as a Dinosaur King."},{"t":"Diplomacy","p":["Windows"],"d":"Paradox Development Studio","u":"Paradox Interactive, PAN Vision","g":"Turn-based strategy","r":"October 4, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomacy_(2005_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cobmx6.jpg"},{"t":"Disney's Herbie: Fully Loaded","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Climax Handheld Games","u":"Buena Vista Games","g":"Racing","r":"June 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disney's_Herbie:_Fully_Loaded","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1vyq.jpg","s":"Inspired by Walt Disney Pictures' feature film Herbie: Fully Loaded, the action-packed video game thrusts players into the high-octane world of 3D stock car racing. The video game offers fans a chance to slip behind the wheel of one of the world’s most beloved cars, Herbie the Love Bug, while enjoying fun power-ups, personalized racing moves, hazards and free replays of unlocked races."},{"t":"Disney's Kim Possible 3: Team Possible","p":["Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS"],"r":"July 26","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim_Possible_(video_game_series)"},{"t":"DJMax Mobile","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DJMax_Mobile"},{"t":"DK King of Swing","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"September 19","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DK_King_of_Swing"},{"t":"Domination","p":["Windows"],"d":"Wargaming","u":"DreamCatcher Games","g":"Turn-based tactics","r":"February 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domination_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cocduu.jpg","s":"Massive Assault: Phantom Renaissance is the sequel to highly acclaimed turn-based strategy game Massive Assault. Massive Assault: Phantom Renaissance features a renewed global conflict between the Free Nations Union and Phantom League in distant space colonies. The game is based on the Massive Assault’s original \"Secret Allies\" concept, acknowledged by the press and the players as innovative and easy to learn and hard to master one and in many respects rejuvenating turn-based genre."},{"t":"Donkey Kong Country 3","p":["Super Nintendo Entertainment System","Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Rare","u":"Nintendo","g":"Platform","r":"November 4, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donkey_Kong_Country_3","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2ven.jpg","s":"Donkey Kong Country 3 is the Game Boy Advance version of the SNES game \"Donkey Kong Country 3: Dixie Kong's Double Trouble!\". Although being developed as a port, the game has a different soundtrack composed by the veteran of the series David Wise, new minigames, worlds and overworld map layout."},{"t":"Donkey Kong Country 3: Dixie Kong's Double Trouble!","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 7"},{"t":"Donkey Kong Jungle Beat","p":["GameCube"],"r":"March 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donkey_Kong_Jungle_Beat"},{"t":"Donkey Konga 2: Hit Song Parade!","p":["GameCube"],"r":"May 9"},{"t":"Donkey Konga 3: Tabe-houdai! Haru Mogitate 50 Kyoku","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donkey_Konga_3:_Tabe-houdai!_Haru_Mogitate_50_Kyoku"},{"t":"Doom 3","p":["Xbox"],"r":"April 3","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doom_3"},{"t":"Doom 3: Resurrection of Evil","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"r":"April 3"},{"t":"Doom RPG","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Fountainhead Entertainment","u":"JAMDAT Mobile","g":"Role playing, first-person shooter","r":"September 19, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doom_RPG","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co901c.jpg","s":"Choose one of three different characters and get ready to battle through hordes of deadly monsters, including returning favorites such as the Pinky, Cacodemon, and Revenant, as well as new threats like the Sawcubus and Sentinel! Battle towering bosses such as the Cyberdemon, Spider Mastermind, or the Pinkinator!\n\nInteract with other survivors of the invasion to get information about your environment and solve puzzles, but beware…not all of them can be trusted!"},{"t":"Dora the Explorer: Journey to the Purple Planet","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Vicious Cycle Software","u":"Global Star Software","g":"Action-adventure","r":"October 13, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dora_the_Explorer:_Journey_to_the_Purple_Planet","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6ttm.jpg","s":"Dora the Explorer: Journey to the Purple Planet is an Adventure game, developed and published by Take-Two Interactive, which was released in 2005."},{"t":"Down in Flames","p":["Windows"],"d":"Dan Verssen Games","u":"Battlefront.com","g":"Turn-based strategy","r":"September 28, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Down_in_Flames_(video_game)"},{"t":"Dragon Ball GT: Transformation","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"August 9"},{"t":"Dragon Ball Z: Budokai Tenkaichi","p":["PlayStation 2","Wii","PlayStation Portable","Windows"],"d":"Spike, Spike Chunsoft","u":"Bandai Namco Entertainment, Atari","g":"Fighting game","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_Ball_Z:_Budokai_Tenkaichi","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1u9x.jpg","s":"Dragon Ball Z: Budokai Tenkaichi lets you play as more than 60 characters from the Dragon Ball Z TV series. You can battle using authentic special attacks of each character as you run, fly, and swim through fully destructible and free-roaming levels. Design your own character by assigning and upgrading 10 different attributes. Dragon Ball Z: Budokai Tenkaichi has multiple game modes for both one and two players."},{"t":"Dragon Ball Z: Sagas","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube"],"r":"March 22"},{"t":"Dragon Ball Z: Supersonic Warriors 2","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 20"},{"t":"Dragon Booster","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"December 7","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_Booster"},{"t":"Dragon Quest Heroes: Rocket Slime","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"Tose","u":"Square Enix","g":"Action-adventure","r":"December 1, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_Quest_Heroes:_Rocket_Slime","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8j66.jpg","s":"Dragon Quest Heroes: Rocket Slime is based in the fictional world of Slimenia, specifically in the capital city of Boingburg. It begins with four Slimes, Rocket, Hooly, Bo, and Swotsy, who are playing in front of the castle. Hooly has gotten his hands on a valuable flute, and in response to the flute being blown by Rocket, his father comes running over, forcing Hooly to stick the flute in Rocket's mouth. Afterward, an organization known as the Plob invades Boingburg, capturing 100 of its 101 inhabitants. Because he was distorted and long, the Plob mistakenly believed Rocket was not a Slime but a worm, and discarded him into Forewood Forest. There, Rocket begins his journey to rescue his fellow slimes, who have been locked up in large treasure chests."},{"t":"Dragon Quest VIII","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"November 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon_Quest_VIII"},{"t":"Dream of Mirror Online","p":["Windows"],"d":"Softstar","u":"Joypark, Gamania, Aeria Games, Goldensoft","g":"MMORPG","r":"September 9, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream_of_Mirror_Online"},{"t":"Driver 3","p":["Windows","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"March 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Driver_3"},{"t":"Driver: Vegas","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Gameloft","u":"Glu Mobile","g":"Action-adventure","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Driver:_Vegas","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7ri7.jpg"},{"t":"DT Racer","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Axis Entertainment","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment Korea, XS Games","g":"Racing","r":"September 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DT_Racer","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7ygh.jpg","s":"Extreme tuner racing just hit a whole new level of no holds barred racing. DT Racer drops you on to 22 of the slickest tracks around the globe. Completely fine tune every inch of your car's handling and performance with unlimited customization. And when you are done, put your foot to the floor and show them what you've got!"},{"t":"Duel Masters: Birth of Super Dragon","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duel_Masters:_Birth_of_Super_Dragon"},{"t":"Duel Masters: Shadow of the Code","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"g":"Turn-based strategy (TBS)","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duel_Masters:_Shadow_of_the_Code","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7jxq.jpg","s":"The third game based on the DUEL MASTERS anime. Gamers will get back in the card-game dueling with access to all 600 released cards, an in-depth storyline featuring characters from the anime, and more."},{"t":"Dungeon Fighter Online","p":["Windows"],"d":"Neople","u":"Neople, Tencent","g":"Beat 'em up","r":"August 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dungeon_Fighter_Online","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3wer.jpg","s":"Dungeon Fighter Online is a free-to-play multiplayer hack-and-slash RPG with a side-scrolling arcade style. There are currently 11 unique character classes. 3 classes have a mirrored class of the opposite gender with a 4th being added soon. Classes have Sub-classes to choose from and later has advancements of those classes to unlock upgraded skills.\nOf the 11 unique classes, 6 have 4 sub-classes, 3 have 2 sub-classes, and 2 have no sub-classes but still has advancements for new skills.\n\nDeveloped by the Korean company Neople in 2005 the game was released in Japan in 2006, China in 2007, Taiwan in 2009, and North America in 2010. The publisher Nexon shut the North American version down in 2013.\nNeople relaunched the game globally in 2016, with Season 2, adding new content and characters to the game.\n\nThe game was released on the Xbox 360 Arcade under the title \"Dungeon Fighter Live\"."},{"t":"Dungeon Lords","p":["Windows"],"d":"Heuristic Park","u":"DreamCatcher Interactive, FX Interactive, Crimson Cow, 1C, Typhoon Games","g":"Action role-playing","r":"May 5, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dungeon_Lords_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2fkm.jpg","s":"A pure Role Playing Game in every sense of the word."},{"t":"Dungeon Siege II","p":["Windows"],"g":"RPG","r":"August 16","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dungeon_Siege_II","i":"images/steam-39200.jpg","s":"It’s been a generation since you vanquished the evil that plagued the Land of Ehb, and now…a new menace has awakened. In Dungeon Siege II, the sequel to the best-selling RPG from Gas Powered Games, you will be called on to again wield sword and spell to save the world from a growing abomination many years in the making."},{"t":"Dungeons & Dragons: Dragonshard","p":["Windows"],"d":"Liquid Entertainment","u":"Atari","g":"Real-time strategy, Role-playing","r":"September 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dungeons_&_Dragons:_Dragonshard","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5yvl.jpg","s":"Dungeons & Dragons: Dragonshard is a real-time strategy role-playing video game, developed for Microsoft Windows by Liquid Entertainment, and published by Atari in 2005. It takes place in Eberron, one of the official Dungeons & Dragons campaign settings. The game combines elements of traditional real-time strategy gameplay with role-playing elements such as hero units, and questing. Dragonshard includes two single-player campaigns, single-player skirmish maps, and multiplayer support. The single-player campaign follows the struggles of three competing factions to gain control of a magical artifact known as the Heart of Siberys.\n\nAlthough Dragonshard was billed by Atari as \"the first Dungeons & Dragons real-time strategy experience,\"[2] Stronghold (1993) precedes it by over a decade.[3]"},{"t":"Dynasty Warriors","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"March 16","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynasty_Warriors_(2004_video_game)"},{"t":"Dynasty Warriors 5","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"March 29","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynasty_Warriors_5"},{"t":"Dynasty Warriors Advance","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"August 29","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynasty_Warriors_Advance"},{"t":"Eagle Eye Golf","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Telenet Japan","u":"Aksys Games, 505 GameStreet","g":"Sports","r":"June 23, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagle_Eye_Golf","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coc4kc.jpg","s":"Designed with the casual golf fan in mind, Eagle Eye Golf lets you play up to 4 players on 7 challenging courses in a variety of game modes such as Mission, Tournament, and even team-based games. The game also features a robust course editor where you can recreate some of the world's most famous courses with incredible accuracy or you can let your imagination run wild and design your own \"out-of-this-world\" fantasy courses. Also included is a mission mode featuring 100 tasks to clear and a training mode where you can choose your course and set the weather and wind. The game includes a robust character edit mode for creating your own character. You can make adjustments to clothing, hair style, body shape, voice and even shoes. Before finalizing your character, you assign points to various statistics, including power, control, impact, recovery, spin shot and fade/draw. These traits grow as you equip your character with items that you've unlocked in the mission mode."},{"t":"Earth 2160","p":["Windows","Linux"],"d":"Reality Pump Studios","u":"Zuxxez Entertainment / Deep Silver, Midway Games","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"June 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earth_2160","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co24mq.jpg","s":"Only a few thousand humans managed to escape from the Earth before its collapse in 2150 A.D. They spent the next few years on the terra forming of the red planet, developing new technologies and building up new civilisations. Somehow each of the three fractions \"Eurasian Dynasty\", \"United Civilised States\" and \"Lunar Corporation\" did this independently and separately from each other - but in the year 2160 something strange happens in this new world. Will the ED, UCS and LC join forces or continue their old war against each other?\n\nBesides the usual venues in the solar system, there are some strange looking locations: planets with moving and reflecting liquid surfaces. And beside the standard RTS - resources acquisition, base building and destruction of enemy bases, the year 2160 will have some adventure inspired tasks for the players."},{"t":"Eccky","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eccky"},{"t":"Echo: Secrets of the Lost Cavern","p":["Windows"],"d":"Kheops Studio","u":"The Adventure Company, Coladia Games","g":"Adventure","r":"June 11, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Echo:_Secrets_of_the_Lost_Cavern","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7b5d.jpg","s":"Secret of the Lost Cavern is another edutainment Myst-clone adventure in the tradition of old Cryo titles. This game attempts to take us to the Prehistoric Age.\n\nThe storyline revolves around the famed Lascaux Caverns of France, where our direct ancestors, the Cro Magnon humans, have left a significant legacy of wall paintings. The hero, Arok, is a young hunter/gatherer who is more interested in painting, however. He soon discovers that he can influence the world around him by painting on the cavern walls, as he searches for a mysterious mentor."},{"t":"Ed, Edd n Eddy: The Mis-Edventures","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 3"},{"t":"Elemental Gelade","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elemental_Gelade"},{"t":"Elite Warriors: Vietnam","p":["Windows"],"d":"nFusion","u":"Bold Games","g":"Tactical shooter","r":"March 25, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elite_Warriors:_Vietnam","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3w55.jpg","s":"Infiltrate deep into Laos with your Green Beret and Montgnard teammates, hunted by trackers and bloodhounds, outnumbered at times 100-to-1. See why SOG veterans went on to found Delta Force and in the work of secret operations, remain the stuff of legends."},{"t":"Emergency 3: Mission Life","p":["Windows"],"d":"Sixteen Tons Entertainment","u":"Take-Two Interactive, Strategy First","g":"Real-time strategy, simulation","r":"January 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emergency_3:_Mission_Life"},{"t":"Emil Chronicle Online","p":["Windows"],"d":"Headlock","u":"Gravity, BROCCOLI","g":"MMORPG","r":"November 24, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emil_Chronicle_Online","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6zw7.jpg","s":"Emil Chronicle Online was a 3D Japanese fantasy MMORPG with anime-style graphics. Set in the land of Acronia, the game featured twelve classes spread among four races, each with a particular advantage (agility, magic, or strength). Along with a series of quests and battles, the game featured a few standout modes including its marionette system, where players could transform their characters into marionettes, which were Pokémon-like surrogates. Marionettes could live in the world even when players had logged out. There was also a standard pet system outside of this. Players could also turn their characters into weapons that other people could use, gaining both experience. PvP was in RvR format, and massive battles were scheduled regularly in advance for different level groups.\n\nAs of 2024, no servers for the game are online, with GungHo Online Entertainment announcing that the Japanese server would be shut down on August 31, 2017, citing the impossible task of keeping up with modern players’ demands."},{"t":"Empire Earth","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"WonderPhone, Vivendi Games Mobile","u":"Vivendi Games Mobile","g":"Turn-based strategy","r":"October 14, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Empire_Earth_(mobile_game)"},{"t":"Empire Earth II","p":["Windows"],"d":"Mad Doc Software","u":"Vivendi Universal Games, Sierra Entertainment","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"April 26, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Empire_Earth_II","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co22ul.jpg","s":"Relive the complete span of human history! Lead the great nations of Korea, Germany and America in the base game and Egypt, Russia and the Masai in the add-on. Take part in the greatest battles in history of mankind. From quests for independence or rises to power, to the Civil and Wold War, Empire Earth 2 will show you all the faces of ancient and modern warfare. Choose your path from clear military dominance to a complicated diplomatic approach and look at the world from the perspective of famous leaders.\n\nWe are inviting you to a great journey into the history of great nations with the best instalment of this famous series. Along with small episodes of sci-fi, when the creators wanted to predict what will come in the future, it is one of the best RTS and historical game ever created. Besides this is the only way to check out what would have happened when one tank would attack XV century Heavy Cavalry!"},{"t":"Enthusia Professional Racing","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Konami","u":"Konami","g":"Sim racing","r":"March 17, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enthusia_Professional_Racing","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1oun.jpg","s":"Enthusia Professional Racing is the driving simulation that emphasizes skill behind the wheel, not under the hood. The game emphasizes pure driving skills and ensures that winning is a result of ability, not how much money you spent tuning a car. It's real-world racing at its finest. Earn the #1 ranking by competing in races scheduled throughout the entire calendar year in Enthusia Life mode Weather effects that change driving dynamics, including rain and snow."},{"t":"Espgaluda II","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Cave","u":"AMI, Cave, Live Wire","g":"Bullet hell","r":"November 25, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Espgaluda_II","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2q2f.jpg","s":"Espgaluda II is a manic shooter originally released by Cave in the arcades in 2005 as a sequel to Espgaluda."},{"t":"Europa Barbarorum","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"Europa Barbarorum Development Team","g":"Real-time tactics, Turn-based strategy","r":"December 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Europa_Barbarorum"},{"t":"EverQuest II: Desert of Flames","p":["Windows"],"r":"September 13"},{"t":"EverQuest: Depths of Darkhollow","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/EverQuest:_Depths_of_Darkhollow"},{"t":"EverQuest: Dragons of Norrath","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/EverQuest:_Dragons_of_Norrath"},{"t":"Every Party","p":["Xbox 360"],"d":"Microsoft Game Studios Japan, Game Republic","u":"Microsoft Game Studios","g":"Party","r":"December 10, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Every_Party","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/yogpdmzlwcjfyf2q5wmp.jpg","s":"One of two titles from former Capcom producer Yoichi Okamoto's new studio. The Xbox 360's first party game features characters from Sakura Momoko, over 30 mini game types, 400 types of costume items that can be freely added to the characters, and 37 types of roulettes. You can stock up to five roulettes as you work your way across a board, attempting to reach the goal before others. Up to four players can play mini games together, with full support for Xbox Live."},{"t":"Evil Dead: Regeneration","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"September 13"},{"t":"Evochron Alliance","p":["Windows"],"d":"StarWraith 3D Games","u":"StarWraith 3D Games","g":"Space simulation","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evochron_Alliance"},{"t":"EyeToy: Kinetic","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"November 8"},{"t":"EyeToy: Operation Spy","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"November 15"},{"t":"EyeToy: Play 2","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"August 16"},{"t":"EyeToy: Play 3","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"London Studio","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Party","r":"November 4, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/EyeToy:_Play_3","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2acq.jpg","s":"EyeToy: Play 3 contains a set of over 50 different games you can play with the help of a USB camera connected to Playstation 2. Amount of players can vary from 1-4 players and the game is suitable for people of all ages.\n\nEyeToy: Play 3 provides single player challenges such as Ghost Grab where you enter a ghost house and try to catch ghosts while trying to avoid objects thrown at you and Boot Camp where you try to pass the different challenges thrown at you such as running through an obstacle course or following sergeants orders. Additionally, for someone preferring slightly less intense action, there is music conducting and working in a beauty salon.\n\nHowever when two or more players are included many more games open in party mode such as Monkey Rampage, Kitty Loves Me and Athletics, with bowling, American football and such. These party games are fast-paced and usually all 4-players can play on the screen at the same time."},{"t":"F.E.A.R.","p":["Windows"],"g":"Action","r":"October 17","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F.E.A.R._(video_game)","i":"images/steam-21090.jpg","s":"Experience the original F.E.A.R. along with F.E.A.R. Extraction Point and F.E.A.R. Perseus Mandate."},{"t":"F1 Grand Prix","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Traveller's Tales","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Racing","r":"September 1, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F1_Grand_Prix_(2005_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2e70.jpg","s":"FIA licensed Formula 1 racing game including the 2005 season teams, drivers, cars, and circuits. The player controls the car on the track and tries to either complete a lap in fastest possible time, or race against either computer controlled drivers (or in multiplayer mode, against other players) and finish in top position."},{"t":"Fahrenheit","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Windows"],"r":"September 26","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fahrenheit_(2005_video_game)"},{"t":"Fahrenheit: Indigo Prophecy","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"September 20","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fahrenheit_(2005_video_game)"},{"t":"Falcon 4.0: Allied Force","p":["Windows"],"u":"Graphsim Entertainment","r":"June 28, 2005"},{"t":"Fantastic Four","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"June 27","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fantastic_Four_(2005_video_game)"},{"t":"Far Cry Instincts","p":["Xbox"],"r":"September 27","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Far_Cry_Instincts"},{"t":"FASTT Math","p":["Windows"],"d":"Tom Snyder Productions, Scholastic Corporation","u":"Scholastic Corporation, Houghton Mifflin Harcourt","g":"Mathematics","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FASTT_Math"},{"t":"Fatal Frame III: The Tormented","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"November 8"},{"t":"Fate","p":["Windows","macOS"],"r":"May 18","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fate_(video_game)"},{"t":"Fate/Hollow Ataraxia","p":["Windows"],"g":"Adventure, Visual Novel","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fate/Hollow_Ataraxia","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7p8t.jpg","s":"Fate/Hollow Ataraxia is a 2005 PC visual novel video game developed by TYPE-MOON and the sequel to Fate/Stay Night. The word \"ataraxia\" in the title is a Greek term for \"tranquility\", giving the title the combined meaning of \"empty (or false) tranquility\".\n\nThe game also was ported to PlayStation Vita, adding full-voice acting, among other enhancements. This version was released in Japan on November 27, 2014."},{"t":"Façade","p":["Windows","macOS"],"g":"Action, Indie","r":"July 5","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fa%C3%A7ade_(interactive_story)","i":"images/steam-4218870.jpg","s":"Broken Facade is an isometric metroidvania, inspired by Bullet Hell and Hack &amp; Slash games, with a post-apocalyptic cyberpunk 1920s vibe. Tear through brutal combat inspired by zero-to-hero fighting animes. Cross a shattered city and meet a small cast of colorful characters."},{"t":"FIFA 06","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube","Nintendo DS","Mobile phone","PlayStation Portable","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 4","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FIFA_06"},{"t":"FIFA 06: Road To FIFA World Cup","p":["Xbox 360"],"r":"November 22"},{"t":"FIFA Street","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube"],"r":"February 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FIFA_Street_(2005_video_game)"},{"t":"Fight Night Round 2","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube"],"r":"February 28","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fight_Night_Round_2"},{"t":"Final Fantasy IV Advance","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"December 12","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Final_Fantasy_IV"},{"t":"Final Fantasy VII","p":["Nintendo Entertainment System"],"d":"Shenzhen Nanjing Technology","u":"Shenzhen Nanjing Technology","g":"Role-playing","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Final_Fantasy_VII_(NES_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2059.jpg","s":"Final Fantasy VII is an unlicensed \"Shanzhai\" demake of SquareSoft role-playing game of the same name, originally released for PlayStation in 1997. This two-dimensional \"port\" was developed and published by Chinese company Shenzhen Nanjing Technology for Subor, a Nintendo's Family Computer clone console series (internationally known as the NES). The cartridge itself is unique, as it is structurally different from licensed Famicom cartridges in terms of hardware and programming."},{"t":"Fire Emblem: Path of Radiance","p":["GameCube"],"r":"October 19"},{"t":"Fire Emblem: The Sacred Stones","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"May 23"},{"t":"Fire Pro Wrestling Returns","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fire_Pro_Wrestling_Returns"},{"t":"Fired Up","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"d":"London Studio","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Vehicular combat","r":"September 1, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fired_Up_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2x7p.jpg","s":"Fired Up is a vehicular combat game available on the PlayStation Portable which supports up to eight players. The game features a demo of Wipeout Pure. The game features three places and five playable drivers. Fired up features game sharing and downloadable levels. It is an advancement on the 2003 PlayStation 2 game Hardware: Online Arena."},{"t":"Fist of the North Star","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Arc System Works","u":"Sega","g":"Fighting","r":"December 7, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fist_of_the_North_Star_(2005_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co63a5.jpg","s":"The famous Anime series is now the latest arcade game from Sega! Players can choose their favorite characters from the series including Kenshiro, Raoh, Toki, Shin, Rei, Juda, Thouther, Mr. Heart and Mamiya! Fist of the North Star is a 1 or 2 player game with continuous buy-in. A Boost Gauge for offensive attacks, an Aura Gauge for defensive maneuvers, and a North Star Gauge (your 7 stars of life force) have been included to enhance game play. Don't lose your stars or the Star of Death will shine, making you dangerously vulnerable to enemy attacks!"},{"t":"FlatOut","p":["Windows","Xbox","PlayStation 2"],"r":"July 12","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FlatOut_(video_game)"},{"t":"Flatspace","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flatspace"},{"t":"Food Force","p":["Windows","macOS"],"u":"United Nations World Food Programme","g":"Educational, serious","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Food_Force","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co25z5.jpg","s":"Food Force is an Educational game published by the United Nations World Food Programme in 2005. Players take on missions to distribute food in a famine-affected country and to then help the country to recover."},{"t":"Football Manager 2006","p":["Windows","macOS","PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Sports Interactive","u":"Sega","g":"Sports management","r":"October 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Football_Manager_2006","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2k73.jpg","s":"Football Manager 2006 is the second installment in the Football Manager series by Sports Interactive. The game allows the player to play the role of manager in most of the national soccer championships held around the globe, while handling as few or as many aspects of the game he wishes. It contains 270,000 personalities consisting of players, managers and team staff, and 5,000 teams from 50 different countries.\n\nNew features include:\nHalf-time Team Talks to boost the morale of your players.\nIn-game tutorial for the first time in the series.\nNew injury module.\nOne-on-one interaction with unhappy players.\nManager contracts.\nTouchline commands shouted during the game.\nHeight and weight statistics for players.\nReferee profiles to see who's harsh and who's not.\nInstant replays."},{"t":"Ford Mustang: The Legend Lives","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Eutechnyx","u":"2K, Global Star Software","g":"Racing","r":"April 19, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Mustang:_The_Legend_Lives","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9bmo.jpg","s":"Since April of 1964 the Ford Mustang has sold over 8 million vehicles and has generated a strong following of enthusiasts, aftermarket manufacturers, websites, and publications - all dedicated to this iconic vehicle. \"Ford Mustang\" provides incredible graphics and \"pick up and play\" gameplay - at a value price. Drive the hottest cars from the 40 year history of the Mustang on 22 tracks in 7 U.S. cities. The game features 40 authentically rendered production, concept and racing models from 1964 to 2005, offering arcade-style racing physics and realistic AI, from opponents as well as from obstacle traffic. Compete in \"coin-op\" style Challenges or Career Mode to unlock new cars, tracks and game modes while testing your skills to the limit. Also included: split screen Multiplayer support for Head-to-Head racing."},{"t":"Ford vs. Chevy","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Eutechnyx","u":"Global Star Software, 2K Games","g":"Racing","r":"November 10, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_vs._Chevy","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7yl3.jpg","s":"Few rivalries in American history evoke stronger emotional reactions than that of the oldest rivalry in American Motorsports – Ford vs. Chevy. This competition appeals to tens of millions of Ford and Chevy owners and NASCAR racing fans. Ford vs. Chevy takes players to the town of Westington where residents and rivals Tyrone Baker and Eddie Olson got things started way back in the earliest days of motoring by racing their Ford Model T and Chevy 490. Over the years, their rivalry grew and soon other Ford and Chevy owners started to join in the fun. Out of this rivalry, the Westington Cup was born. And so we come to today – the Westington Cup tournament is about to begin. As a driver for either the Ford or the Chevy team, it’s time to defend your pride as you battle in a variety of different races, missions and vehicles. It's furious fun as you race 48 of the hottest Ford and Chevy cars, trucks and race cars of all time."},{"t":"Formula One 05","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Studio Liverpool","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Racing","r":"July 1, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Formula_One_05"},{"t":"Forza Motorsport","p":["Xbox"],"u":"Microsoft Game Studios","r":"May 3, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forza_Motorsport_(2005_video_game)"},{"t":"Frantix","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"September 19","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frantix"},{"t":"Freedom Force vs the 3rd Reich","p":["Windows"],"d":"Irrational Games","u":"Irrational Games, Digital Jesters","g":"Real-time tactics, tactical role-playing","r":"March 8, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freedom_Force_vs_the_3rd_Reich","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co28fk.jpg","s":"Freedom is threatened yet again and only Minute Man and his heroic Freedom Force can save the day in the follow up to one of the most critically acclaimed games of 2002.\n\nFreedom Force vs. the Third Reich brings dynamic storytelling, fast-paced tactical role-play, and larger-than-life characters from the comic book pages to the computer screen. In this title, the league of heroes must travel back in time to defeat Blitzkrieg, defender of the Reich and his homicidal henchmen. With action spanning from the blasted battlefields of World War II to the dazzling depths of distant dimensions, Freedom Force vs. the Third Reich will give Freedom Fans more than they can handle."},{"t":"Friends: The One with All the Trivia","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows"],"d":"Artech Studios","u":"Warner Bros. Interactive Entertainment","g":"Trivia","r":"November 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friends:_The_One_with_All_the_Trivia","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1ovc.jpg","s":"Over 3,000 questions and 700 clips highlighting memorable moments from all 10 seasons of the sensational show\n\nPlay along with yopur hosts featuring the voice talents of Janice, Gunther and Jack & Judy Geller\n\nSingle and multi-player modes let you test your Friends knowledge solo or with a group of...friends!"},{"t":"Frog Feast","p":["Neo Geo CD","Sega CD"],"d":"Rastersoft","u":"OlderGames","g":"Action","r":"August 20, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frog_Feast","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9v5d.jpg","s":"A 16-bit remake of the game Frog Bog, which was originally released on the Atari 2600. The game has been released on a variety of platforms, but originated during the Classic Gaming Expo 2005. It is consistently being ported to new platforms."},{"t":"Frogger: Ancient Shadow","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube"],"r":"September 27"},{"t":"Frogger: Helmet Chaos","p":["Nintendo DS","PlayStation Portable"],"r":"September 29"},{"t":"Front Mission 2089","p":["Mobile phone","Nintendo DS"],"d":"Square Enix, MSF, Winds, h.a.n.d.","u":"Square Enix","g":"Tactical role-playing game","r":"March 7, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Front_Mission_2089","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4hf5.jpg","s":"Front Mission 2089 is a tactical role-playing game developed by Square Enix Co., Ltd., MSF, and Winds, and was published and released in Japan by Square Enix Co., Ltd. in 2005 and 2008 for the mobile phones. The game was released on March 7, 2005, October 27, 2005, and June 18, 2008.\n\nFront Mission 2089 borrows many of the gameplay mechanics found in Front Mission. The video game progresses in a linear manner: watch cut-scene events, complete missions, set up their wanzers during intermissions, and sortie for the next mission. Missions in Front Mission 2089 are traditional tactical RPG fare, ranging from destroying all enemy targets to protecting a particular allied target. Due to its mobile phone format, the story of Front Mission 2089 is told through episodic content; new episodes were released for download on the video game's official website on a bi-weekly basis. A returning feature in the game is the Arena. Like in Front Mission, players can fight other players to win monetary rewards. Mission rankings also make a return; based on the scoring system of Front Mission 3, players can earn new parts and wanzers by doing well during missions. Another returning feature is briefings. Lastly, players can choose to play two unique scenarios - one with the Oceania Cooperative Union (O.C.U.), and one with the United States of the New Continent (U.S.N.)."},{"t":"Front Mission 5: Scars of the War","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Square Enix","u":"Square Enix","g":"Tactical role-playing","r":"December 29, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Front_Mission_5:_Scars_of_the_War","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co398p.jpg","s":"Front Mission 5: Scars of the War is the fifth in Square's Front Mission tactical RPG series. It brings the player back to a gritty futuristic world in which conflicts are waged between five world powers: the U.S.N., O.C.U., E.C., O.A.C., and the Republic of Zaftra. Such conflicts are waged with the wanzer, Front Mission-speak for mecha.\n\nGameplay-wise, the game is a true return to Front Mission 2 roots while incorporating various features from Front Mission 1, 3, and 4. The player takes part in turn-based missions, which pit their group of wanzers against enemy forces. Old features that have returned include the ability to upgrade parts and mission branching. New features to Front Mission 5 include friendly fire and the ability to recruit new pilots."},{"t":"Front Mission: Online","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows"],"d":"Square Enix","u":"Square Enix","g":"Massively multiplayer online game, Third-person shooter","r":"May 12, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Front_Mission:_Online","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2v55.jpg","s":"A multiplayer-only arcade shooter based on Square's Front Mission universe of futuristic mecha warfare. Joining either the USN or OCU during the second Huffman conflict, you duke it out on online arenas in your Wanzer for fame and money, which you can use to further upgrade your Wanzer with new weapons and special upgrades.\n\nAll strategy elements from the series are removed save from the mechanics of damage and action, and the game is played from a 3rd person perspective similar to other 3d action titles. Registration to Square's PlayOnline service and a monthly free is required for playing. The game has built-in support for VoIP."},{"t":"Fu-un Bakumatsu-den","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Genki, From Software","u":"Genki, From Software","g":"Action","r":"January 20, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fu-un_Bakumatsu-den","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1pps.jpg","s":"Fu-un Bakumatsu-den is a 2005 PlayStation 2 action game from Genki Co. and the follow-up to Fu-un Shinsengumi. Set during Japan’s Bakumatsu era, it lets players join the Shinsengumi in stylized beat ’em up combat."},{"t":"Fullmetal Alchemist 3: Kami o Tsugu Shōjo","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Racjin","u":"Square Enix","g":"Role-playing video game","r":"July 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fullmetal_Alchemist_3:_Kami_o_Tsugu_Sh%C5%8Djo"},{"t":"Fullmetal Alchemist and the Broken Angel","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"January 18","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fullmetal_Alchemist_and_the_Broken_Angel"},{"t":"Futakoi Alternative","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Futakoi_Alternative"},{"t":"G1 Jockey 4","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Koei","u":"Koei, THQ","g":"Horse racing","r":"December 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/G1_Jockey_4","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/ov9pokvvcmazyfufn32s.jpg","s":"G1 Jockey 4 lets players take the reins and experience the feeling of being a top racehorse jockey. This fourth game in the hugely popular series introduces a new ranking system and abilities, as well a revolutionary analogue control system."},{"t":"Gakuen Heaven","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gakuen_Heaven"},{"t":"Gallop Racer 2006","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Tecmo","u":"Tecmo","g":"Alternative sports","r":"December 15, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gallop_Racer_2006","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7yf1.jpg","s":"Gallop Racer 2006, is the perennial update of the Gallop Racer series, with the standard gaming modes: Exhibition and Career, along with new modes such as Memorial Quest, where players can partake in over a 100 classic horse races from past years and Field of Legend, where players can test their created horses against actually horses from past years of horse racing. This entire setting is set in a theme park-style arena called Gallop Racing Square.\n\nNot only can players create their own horses, but they can also race classic and legendary horses from previous years in the history of horse racing. The gameplay is virtually the same as previous versions, pressing buttons at a certain point in time to urge the horse while racing, with several gauges to monitor such as the horses stamina, their position in the race as well as their mental condition. Players can also bet in races, with a true feel of betting simulation, figuring in weather conditions, the horses conditions as well as the horses stats."},{"t":"Ganbare Goemon: Tōkai Dōchū Ōedo Tengu ri Kaeshi no Maki","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"Konami Computer Entertainment Osaka","u":"Konami","g":"Action-adventure","r":"June 23, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ganbare_Goemon:_T%C5%8Dkai_D%C5%8Dch%C5%AB_%C5%8Cedo_Tengu_ri_Kaeshi_no_Maki"},{"t":"Garfield: The Search for Pooky","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 14"},{"t":"Gary Grigsby's World at War","p":["Windows"],"d":"2 by 3 Games","u":"Matrix Games","g":"Computer wargame","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gary_Grigsby's_World_at_War","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/fjyclfsk3jpundw6apow.jpg","s":"A turn based strategy game developed by the prolific strategy developer Gary Grigsby."},{"t":"Garōden","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gar%C5%8Dden"},{"t":"Gauntlet: Seven Sorrows","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"December 12"},{"t":"Geist","p":["GameCube"],"r":"August 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geist_(video_game)"},{"t":"Geneforge 3","p":["macOS","Windows"],"d":"Spiderweb Software","u":"Spiderweb Software","g":"Role-playing","r":"March 28, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geneforge_3","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2177.jpg","s":"Geneforge 3 is the next, huge installment of the Geneforge saga. In this fantasy adventure, you can explore strange, hostile lands, choose which side you will fight for, and, as always, make your own horde of completely obedient mutant monsters."},{"t":"Geniu$: The Tech Tycoon Game","p":["Windows"],"d":"Radon Labs","u":"Viva Media","g":"Business simulation","r":"November 1, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geniu$:_The_Tech_Tycoon_Game","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/habdzmgjc8prc9bqjacl.jpg","s":"Geniu$: The Tech Tycoon Game is a business simulation game in which the player operates an industrial business, making products from bicycles to aircraft. New technologies are obtained through physics questions to be solved by the player, occurring at intervals mirroring real-world innovation."},{"t":"Genji: Dawn of the Samurai","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 20"},{"t":"Geometry Wars: Retro Evolved","p":["Xbox 360"],"r":"November 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geometry_Wars"},{"t":"Ghost In The Shell:Stand Alone Complex","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"October 26"},{"t":"Ghost Online","p":["Windows"],"d":"Netgame","u":"MGame, Netgame, OurGame, GameFlier, Gemscool","g":"Fantasy, Massively Multiplayer Online Game","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost_Online","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4bl7.jpg","s":"Ghost Online also known as Ghost Soul and GO was a free fast paced action-based sidescrolling, massively multiplayer online game that is currently released in South Korea, Japanese, Chinese, Thailand and Malaysian-English. On July 8, the Global version went into Open Beta, but was closed down on June 3, 2009."},{"t":"Gift","p":["Windows"],"g":"Visual Novel","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gift_(2005_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7230.jpg","s":"Gift is a story that revolves around high school student Amami Haruhiko and his strong connection to Gift's mysterious power.\n\nThe town of Narasaki-chou, where Gift's story takes place, has two distinguishing characteristics: a rainbow that seems permanently fixed in the sky no matter the weather, and an ability known as Gift possessed by all its inhabitants. Gift's power can only be evoked by each person once in a lifetime, and is able to grant a single miracle. To be successful, a Gift must reflect the shared feelings of both the giver and the receiver. If the feelings are not mutual, the Gift is distorted and has the ability to wreak havoc on the surrounding area. When this happens, a black streak appears in the rainbow above town until Gift is used correctly."},{"t":"Girls Bravo","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girls_Bravo"},{"t":"Glimmerati","p":["N-Gage"],"d":"Bugbear Entertainment","u":"Nokia","g":"Racing","r":"July 7, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glimmerati","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co63fw.jpg","s":"In the game's story, the player is a wealthy heir who meets with another wealthy man one day, and he admires the player's skill in driving. He invites the player to compete with Club Glimmerati, an exclusive gathering of famous and rich people who race in the public streets for fun."},{"t":"Global Defence Force","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Sandlot","u":"D3 Publisher, Essential Games, Xseed Games, PQube","g":"Third-person shooter","r":"July 28, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Global_Defence_Force","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co49jt.jpg","s":"The second game in the The Chikyuu Boueigun series, renamed Global Defence Force for its English release (similarly the first game was renamed Monster Attack for its English release).\n\nIt's been two years since the invading alien menace was defeated by the Global Defence Force (the game renames the \"Earth Defence Force\" from the previous game), but like any good off-world threat, they're back for more, and they've brought new weapons and technology in their attempts to take Earth and eliminate humanity. Thankfully, the GDF has also been developing new technology to fight them.\n\nGlobal Defence Force is a third-person action shooter. Choose from either an GDF infantryman or the flight-capable Pale Wing, each with different abilities and dozens of weapons each, and set out to shoot down hordes of giant insects, enormous robots, and UFOs of incredible scale. You can choose two weapons to carry for each mission, and pickups dropped by enemies will unlock new weapons and increase your character's maximum health. You can play the game split-screen cooperatively.\n\nBeyond adding a second player class to choose from; the Pale Wing; a fragile but powerful melee centric character with a limited Jetpack and her own weapon set, to go alongside the infantry man of the first game, Global Defence Force doesn't change much of the basic game play of Monster Attack. But leaving at that would undersell the game; there are numerous new alien types, weapons and environments that add much more variety to things. The maps are larger and more detailed and missions are longer and much more scripted (where as the original game nearly always threw you into an environment against some preplaced bug's, this time you often have some simple objective(s)) to add further variety. Finally the physics have been notably enhanced.\n\nLike Monster Attack, the player in Global Defence Force fights completely by themselves despite being part of an army (unless playing offline only 2 player split screen); the original Japanese version features radio chatter from other GDF squads and your commanding officer, to give the illusion that you are fighting alongside others. This was cut from the English release."},{"t":"Go! Sudoku","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Sumo Digital","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment, Ubisoft","g":"Puzzle","r":"December 2, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Go!_Sudoku","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2e73.jpg","s":"Go! Sudoku is a sudoku puzzle game for the PlayStation Portable, released in Europe on December 2, 2005 and North America on March 21, 2006. It was later released in Japan on April 27, 2006 under the name of Kazuo (カズオ), as Nikoli holds the trademark for Sudoku. The game was mildly received by gamers and professional critics.\nThe base game features 1000 Sudoku puzzles grouped by difficulty, as well as various modes, customizable grids and multiplayer. 200 more puzzles are available for download from the Go! Sudoku official website, and players can add their own custom backgrounds to the games."},{"t":"God of War","p":["PlayStation 2"],"u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","r":"March 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/God_of_War_(2005_video_game)"},{"t":"Golden Nugget Casino DS","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"Skyworks Interactive","u":"Majesco","g":"Video game compilation","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Nugget_Casino_DS"},{"t":"GoldenEye: Source","p":["Windows"],"g":"Shooter","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GoldenEye:_Source","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3x5m.jpg","s":"GoldenEye: Source is a total conversion mod developed using Valve's Source engine. GoldenEye: Source is a multiplayer remake of the 1997 Nintendo 64 video game GoldenEye 007, itself based on the James Bond film GoldenEye. The mod's development began in 2005, and remains in active development as of 2019."},{"t":"GooBall","p":["macOS"],"d":"Over the Edge","u":"Ambrosia Software","g":"Puzzle","r":"March 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GooBall","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2yfu.jpg","s":"GooBall is a Mac video game by Over The Edge Entertainment, now Unity Technologies, and published by Ambrosia Software"},{"t":"Gran Turismo 4","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"February 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gran_Turismo_4"},{"t":"Grand Theft Auto: Liberty City Stories","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"October 24"},{"t":"Grand Theft Auto: San Andreas","p":["Xbox","Windows"],"u":"Rockstar Games","r":"June 7, 2005"},{"t":"Grand Theft Auto: The Trilogy","p":["Xbox"],"r":"October 17"},{"t":"Greg Hastings' Tournament Paintball MAX'D","p":["Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"The Whole Experience","u":"Activision","g":"First-person shooter, sports","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greg_Hastings'_Tournament_Paintball_MAX'D","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9ukq.jpg","s":"The sequel to the original Tournament Paintball game"},{"t":"Gretzky NHL 06","p":["PlayStation 2","PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Page 44 Studios","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Sports","r":"September 20, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gretzky_NHL_06"},{"t":"Gretzky NHL 2006","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 20","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gretzky_NHL_2006"},{"t":"GridWars","p":["Windows"],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GridWars","s":"GridWars is a video game inspired by Bizarre Creations' Geometry Wars by Canadian developer Marco Incitti. The first version of the game was released as freeware on December 21, 2005 on Marco Incitti's Blitz Creations website.\n\nAlthough other freeware games similar to Geometry Wars exist, GridWars eventually became so popular that Bizarre emailed Incitti and asked him to take the game down, citing that they were \"beginning to feel the Geometry Wars clone's effects on our sales via Microsoft now and are beginning a process to begin to more robustly protect our copyright and intellectual property\". The link to the download was pulled from the site on August 8, 2006. The game was subsequently released on a German website dedicated to Flash and freeware games and is available for Windows, OS X and Linux.\n\nUnlike Geometry Wars which eventually plateaus in difficulty facilitating high scores in the range of hundreds of millions of points, GridWars 2 has an exponentially increasing difficulty curve. Eventually, the enemy spawn sites become so large that they nearly envelop the entire grid.\n\nAnother important difference from Geometry Wars is the ability to \"farm\" black holes. Besides distracting and swallowing enemies, the black holes can net points (and thus bombs/lives) based on the square of the number of enemies they have swallowed."},{"t":"GripShift","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"September 13","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GripShift"},{"t":"GT Legends","p":["Windows"],"d":"SimBin Studios","u":"10tacle Publishing","g":"Sim racing","r":"October 6, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GT_Legends","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co86cd.jpg","s":"The golden age of motor sports has returned. Experience one of the world’s most exciting racing series in GT."},{"t":"GTR – FIA GT Racing Game","p":["Windows"],"d":"Simbin Studios AB","u":"10tacle Publishing","g":"Sim racing","r":"March 11, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GTR_%E2%80%93_FIA_GT_Racing_Game"},{"t":"Guild Wars","p":["Windows"],"g":"Action, Adventure, Massively Multiplayer, RPG","r":"April 26","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guild_Wars_(video_game)","i":"images/steam-4743930.jpg","s":"Guild Wars 3 is an action-adventure MMORPG, a modern evolution of the genre that blends rich action-combat, character building, and skill collection. Set in the enchanting frontier of Orr, the world brims with mystery, magic, and wonder."},{"t":"Guitar Hero","p":["PlayStation 2"],"u":"RedOctane","r":"November 7, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guitar_Hero"},{"t":"Gun","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube"],"r":"November 8","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gun_(video_game)"},{"t":"Gunstar Super Heroes","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 25","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gunstar_Super_Heroes"},{"t":"Half-Life 2","p":["Xbox"],"r":"November 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Half-Life_2"},{"t":"Half-Life 2: Capture the Flag","p":["Windows","Linux"],"d":"HL2:CTF team","g":"Action","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Half-Life_2:_Capture_the_Flag","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5iy4.jpg","s":"Half-Life 2 Capture the Flag brings the familiar Capture the Flag game to HL2. It pits the Rebels against the Combine in a fast-paced battle over the flags within the graphics rich environment of the Source engine."},{"t":"Half-Life 2: Lost Coast","p":["Windows"],"r":"October 27"},{"t":"Hammer & Sickle","p":["Windows"],"d":"Novik&Co, Nival Interactive","u":"CDV Software Entertainment, T-time Technology","g":"Tactical RPG","r":"April 29, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hammer_&_Sickle","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2x88.jpg","s":"Hammer & Sickle is a turn-based strategy game with role playing elements that uses the Silent Storm engine and universe. The year is 1949, with the Cold War between the US and Soviet Union looming and both sides uneasy at the thought of an atomic war occurring. The player takes the role of a Soviet commando on an undercover mission to meet a contact in Allied-occupied Germany. However, things go badly for this meeting, leaving the protagonist without proper support, equipment, and identification papers. Behind Allied-occupied lines, the player must attempt to stop a rogue third party intent on initiating World War III between the US and Russia.\n\nPlayers can choose to start with one of 6 player classes: Soldier, Grenadier, Scout, Sniper, Medic, and Engineer. Additionally, there are opportunities throughout the game to recruit additional characters to round out the party's abilities. The game itself features a branching plot where the player's actions and dealings with NPC's can have serious consequences later on. For example, an intelligent character may be able to talk his way out of a situation, and killing Allied soldiers may prompt more patrols later on and slide the situation towards World War III.\n\nHammer & Sickle also features heavy squad-based combat, and it inherits the turn-based engine from Silent Storm. Players spend Action Points to perform various actions in battle each turn, while the enemy does the same. The engine also models realistic looking physics that feature ragdoll animations, bullet ricochet, and destructible environments. As for available equipment, there are 90 weapons and variants that can be found or bought."},{"t":"Happiness!","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Happiness!_(video_game)"},{"t":"Hard Truck Apocalypse","p":["Windows"],"d":"Targem Games","u":"Nival Interactive, CDV Software, Buka Entertainment","g":"Vehicular combat, business simulation, post-apocalyptic science fiction","r":"December 8, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hard_Truck_Apocalypse","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coas84.jpg","s":"In a post-apocalyptic wasteland of diesel and dust, bandits and mobsters rule the last remaining cities, controlling all vital trade routes and destroying any hope of a return to a lawful world."},{"t":"Harry Potter And The Goblet Of Fire","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube","Nintendo DS","Game Boy Advance","PlayStation Portable"],"r":"November 8","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harry_Potter_and_the_Goblet_of_Fire_(video_game)"},{"t":"Harvest Moon DS","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"Marvelous Interactive","u":"Marvelous Interactive, Natsume Inc., Rising Star Games","g":"Simulation, role-playing","r":"March 17, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harvest_Moon_DS","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2xm4.jpg","s":"Help to save the Harvest Goddess, who has become trapped in another world, in the first game of the farm-simulation franchise to appear on the Nintendo DS."},{"t":"Harvest Moon: Another Wonderful Life","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harvest_Moon:_Another_Wonderful_Life"},{"t":"Harvest Moon: More Friends of Mineral Town","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"July 26"},{"t":"Haunting Ground","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"April 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haunting_Ground"},{"t":"Hauntings of Mystery Manor","p":["Windows"],"d":"Cindy Pondillo","u":"Cindy Pondillo","g":"Adventure","r":"June 15, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hauntings_of_Mystery_Manor"},{"t":"He-Man: Defender of Grayskull","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Savage Entertainment","u":"Midas Interactive Entertainment","g":"Action","r":"February 25, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/He-Man:_Defender_of_Grayskull"},{"t":"Hearts of Iron II","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"Paradox Development Studio","u":"Paradox Interactive, PAN Vision AB","g":"Grand strategy","r":"January 4, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hearts_of_Iron_II","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2qbl.jpg","s":"When Germany is defeated in 1945, the Allies and the new Soviet alliance fight for supremacy. World War III is drawing closer. Play as the ruler of one of 175 countries through World Wars II and III. As the Allies and the Soviet Union clash in Europe, the fate of the world hangs in the balance."},{"t":"Heavy Metal Thunder","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Media.Vision","u":"Square Enix","g":"Action game","r":"September 1, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heavy_Metal_Thunder_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6zy4.jpg","s":"The game pits futuristic robots against one another in wrestling matches. The player controls a robot during battles using a four-icon menu. Three actions—strike, guard and grapple—can be executed at any time and augments the player's \"beat meter\"."},{"t":"Heavy Weapon","p":["Windows","macOS","Xbox 360","PlayStation 2","PlayStation 3"],"d":"PopCap Games","u":"PopCap Games","g":"Scrolling shooter","r":"March 1, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heavy_Weapon","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5thl.jpg","s":"Heavy Weapon is a cartoonish side-scrolling action game where you control a single tank fighting waves of opponents. Driving to the right over flat terrain at a constant speed, the tank can move left or right while the sky is filled with aircraft such as jets, helicopters, zeppelins, bombers, and missiles. Projectiles need to be avoided or taken out. Some friendly planes will pass and drop power-ups to improve speed, gun power or shield, or provide nukes, rockets, a laser, rapid-fire, or spread fire. During each level, enemies will drop parts of a mega laser weapon. If the four parts are found, an extremely powerful laser beam is added to your arsenal for a short time."},{"t":"Hello Kitty: Happy Party Pals","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 11"},{"t":"Hello Kitty: Roller Rescue","p":["GameCube"],"r":"August 16"},{"t":"Heroes of the Pacific","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows","Xbox"],"d":"IR Gurus","u":"Codemasters, Ubisoft","g":"Air combat simulation","r":"September 23, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heroes_of_the_Pacific","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2jzh.jpg","s":"Heroes of the Pacific is an aerial combat simulator game set in the Pacific Theater of Operations during World War II."},{"t":"Higanjima","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"g":"Visual Novel","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Higanjima","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7237.jpg"},{"t":"High Seize","p":["N-Gage"],"d":"RedLynx","u":"Nokia","g":"Turn-based tactics","r":"October 13, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Seize","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co63fz.jpg","s":"High Seize is a pirate themed strategy game on the N-Gage."},{"t":"Hockey Rage 2005","p":["Gizmondo"],"d":"Chairman & Board","u":"Fathammer","g":"Sport","r":"April 26, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hockey_Rage_2005","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/bsursuxwgyxutswlvoni.jpg","s":"An ice hockey game for the Gizmondo. Features a 2-player mode via Bluetooth."},{"t":"Homeland","p":["GameCube"],"d":"Chunsoft","u":"Chunsoft","g":"Role-playing","r":"April 29, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homeland_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1s02.jpg","s":"Homeland is a Japanese-exclusive game for the Nintendo GameCube. Its main claim to fame is that it is the only non-Phantasy Star Online title in the system's library to officially support online multiplayer, although the implementation of it is different compared to most other games."},{"t":"Hot Shots Golf: Open Tee","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"May 3"},{"t":"Howrse","p":["Browser"],"d":"Owlient","u":"Owlient","g":"Simulation","r":"September 8, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Howrse","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3an1.jpg","s":"Breed horses, enter competitions and manage your own equestrian center!"},{"t":"Ibara","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Cave","u":"AMI, Taito","g":"Scrolling shooter","r":"July 15, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibara_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/gombjmbhznoaibvnsaib.jpg","s":"Ibara is a vertical scrolling shoot 'em up. The back story revolves around a group of sisters, led by Professor Teresa Rose, who want to destroy all technological progress in the land of Edelweiss, essentially turning it into a rose garden. Players can choose to either lead the characters Bond or Dyne and their airplanes through several levels of \"bullet hell\"-style gameplay in an attempt to defeat the sisters.\n\nThe player's weapons arsenal consists of a main gun and bombs. Bombs must be collected in fragments, and once the player has all of them, the Hadou Cannon can be used. Staying behind the cannon will make the player invincible for the duration of the effect. Additionally, enemies drop various \"options,\" up to two of which can be attached to the wings of the plane to further increase fire power.\n\nThe game has a ranking system. If the player does really well, they go up in rank and thus boss battles will be a lot harder. Rank can be strategically decreased either by dying or by collecting roses, which are created from enemy bullets when the player sets off a bomb. Scoring works by collecting gold medals dropped by destroyed enemies. They must be quickly collected to keep up a scoring chain. Once a new medal pops up, and the medals on screen already haven't been collected yet, the chain is broken."},{"t":"Ice Nine","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 28","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice_Nine_(video_game)"},{"t":"Imperia Online","p":["Windows","Browser","Linux"],"d":"Imperia Online JSC","u":"Imperia Online JSC","g":"MMORTS","r":"August 23, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperia_Online","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co43is.jpg","s":"Imperia Online is MMO strategy known for its deep gameplay. Build your capital, claim new territories by establishing provinces, trading posts and military encampments. Train your army to spy on the enemy and defend your Empire. With its pvp focus you can expect to become a part of an alliance and wage war against enemy players in competition for the title \"Lord of the Realm\"! Special weekly events, realms and tournaments are all present and further enrich your gameplay experience."},{"t":"Imperial Glory","p":["Windows"],"d":"Pyro Studios, Robosoft Technologies","u":"Eidos Interactive, Feral Interactive","g":"Real-time tactics","r":"May 17, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperial_Glory","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1rcj.jpg","s":"It is a time of war in Europe. Driven by new ideas of Enlightenment, the hearts of men and women across the continent are inflamed with dreams of freedom and glory. This is the moment for a military genius to forge himself a name to be remembered throughout all eternity. This is your moment."},{"t":"In the Groove 2","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Roxor Games","u":"RedOctane","g":"Music","r":"June 18, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_the_Groove_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/o3l8ocn5qwd3r4apb1kh.jpg","s":"In The Groove 2 is the second iteration of a dance/rhythm series made by Roxor. It's extremely similar to Konami's Dance Dance Revolution and is the center of a massive gaming community for it's ability to play custom songs."},{"t":"Indigo Prophecy","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Quantic Dream","u":"Atari","g":"Action-adventure","r":"September 16, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigo_Prophecy","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3rhh.jpg","s":"Indigo Prophecy is an action-adventure game that involves the player in making decisions to alter the narrative. The name change in North America was made to avoid confusion with Michael Moore's Fahrenheit 9/11 documentary film, which was released in 2004. Indigo Prophecy introduced elements like ethical ambiguity, romance, the inability to perish, and interactive storytelling that would endure in Quantic Dream's later games."},{"t":"Infected","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"November 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infected_(video_game)"},{"t":"InuYasha: Feudal Combat","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"August 25"},{"t":"Iron Phoenix","p":["Xbox"],"r":"March 25"},{"t":"Jade Dynasty","p":["Windows"],"d":"Beijing Perfect World","u":"Beijing Perfect World, Perfect World Entertainment, Perfect World Europe","g":"MMORPG","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jade_Dynasty_(video_game)"},{"t":"Jade Empire","p":["Xbox"],"r":"April 12","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jade_Empire"},{"t":"Jak X: Combat Racing","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"October 18"},{"t":"Jingai Makyō","p":["Windows"],"d":"Nitroplus","u":"Nitroplus","g":"Visual novel, Romance","r":"June 24, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jingai_Maky%C5%8D"},{"t":"Judge Dredd: Dredd vs. Death","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube","Windows"],"g":"Action","r":"February 24","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/3710","i":"images/steam-3710.jpg","s":"Welcome to Mega-City One, a city of over 400 million people - every one of them a potential criminal. It is the third decade of the 22nd Century, unemployment is widespread, boredom is universal and only the Judges can prevent total anarchy. Empowered to dispense instant justice, they are Judge, Jury and Executioner all in one."},{"t":"Juiced","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"g":"Action, Adventure, Indie","r":"June 13","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Juiced_(video_game)","i":"images/steam-1287310.jpg","s":"Embark on an epic journey through exotic worlds to uncover the mystery of the magic crystals! An exciting retro platform adventure in the nostalgic style of the 90's DOS platformers"},{"t":"Jump Super Stars","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"Ganbarion","u":"Nintendo","g":"Fighting","r":"August 8, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jump_Super_Stars","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9mge.jpg","s":"Jump Super Stars is a 2D fighting game for the Nintendo DS. It was developed by Ganbarion and published by Nintendo. The game was released on August 8, 2005 in Japan and accompanied the release of a red Nintendo DS. A sequel, Jump Ultimate Stars, was released in Japan on November 23, 2006."},{"t":"Kameo","p":["Xbox 360"],"r":"November 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kameo"},{"t":"Kao Challengers","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Tate Interactive","u":"Atari Europe","g":"Action-Adventure","r":"October 28, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kao_Challengers","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co292o.jpg","s":"Kao Challengers is an action-adventure video game featuring Kao the Kangaroo. Challengers is an enhanced port of Kao the Kangaroo: Round 2, released a year earlier in Europe. It includes additional racing and deathmatch multiplayer minigames."},{"t":"Kao the Kangaroo: Mystery of the Volcano","p":["Windows"],"d":"Tate Interactive","u":"Cenega, 1C Company, N3V Games","g":"Platform","r":"December 2, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kao_the_Kangaroo:_Mystery_of_the_Volcano","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6dtd.jpg","s":"Kao the Kangaroo: Mystery of the Volcano is a third instalment of the epic Kao the Kangaroo 3D platformer series where the player takes control of a brave Kao, who embarks on a journey to save his homeland from an erupting volcano. Help him succeed!"},{"t":"Kidou Senshi Gundam Seed: Rengou vs. Z.A.F.T.","p":["Arcade","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Capcom","u":"Banpresto, Bandai, Namco Bandai Games","g":"Action-adventure, Anime","r":"July 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kidou_Senshi_Gundam_Seed:_Rengou_vs._Z.A.F.T."},{"t":"Kiki the nano bot","p":["Windows"],"g":"Platform, Puzzle","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiki_the_nano_bot","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co85ba.jpg","s":"kiki the nano bot is a 3-D puzzle game, basically a mixture of the games Sokoban and Kula-World."},{"t":"killer7","p":["PlayStation 2","GameCube"],"r":"July 7","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Killer7"},{"t":"Killing Floor","p":["Windows"],"d":"Tripwire Interactive","u":"Tripwire Interactive","g":"First-person shooter","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Killing_Floor_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8efj.jpg","s":"The original iteration of Killing Floor, which was released as an Unreal Tournament 2004 total conversion mod in 2005 by Shatterline Productions.\n\nLike the future retail editions of the series, it is a co-op survival horror game against waves of specimen from the Horzine corporation...\n\nEarly versions of the mod included a short story mode, which was removed in later versions. Version 2.5 was the final version of the mod before the retail release of Killing Floor, though fans did later release up to Version 2.52."},{"t":"King Kong","p":["Mobile phone","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Windows","Xbox","Xbox 360","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS","PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Ubisoft Montpellier, Ubisoft Casablanca, Ubisoft Montreal, Gameloft","u":"Ubisoft","g":"First-person shooter, action-adventure","r":"November 14, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_Kong_(2005_video_game)"},{"t":"Kingdom Hearts II","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"December 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_Hearts_II"},{"t":"Kingdom of Paradise","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"November 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Paradise"},{"t":"Kingdom Under Fire:Heroes","p":["Xbox"],"r":"September 20"},{"t":"Kino's Journey","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kino's_Journey"},{"t":"Kirby: Canvas Curse","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"June 13"},{"t":"Klonoa 2: Dream Champ Tournament","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 23"},{"t":"Knights of the Temple II","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Cauldron","u":"Playlogic Entertainment, TDK Mediactive Europe, Evolved Games","g":"Action-adventure, hack and slash","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Temple_II","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7np5.jpg","s":"Knights of the Temple II is a 3rd Person Action-Adventure with non-linear game play, interactive dialog system, trade mode, side quests, RPG elements, alternative endings and multiplayer. KOTT2 is a game showing the player the ultimate fight of Paul de Raque, grandmaster of the Order of the Temple and hero of the first game, with the forces of Hell. Traveling the lands and kingdoms of Europe of the 13th century, he must reveal the secret of the three ancient artifacts and fight the demon armies attacking our world.\n\nAs a grandmaster of the Order of the Temple has Paul de Raque fought many battles in the eternal war between good and evil. But now he stands before his greatest challenge. Visions of evil forces invading our world, undead beings ravaging the lands of northern Europe and a dark menace opening a portal closed millennia ago. Fight your way through the forgotten Roman city, deadly dungeons of the Saracen Empire; discover long forgotten islands, ruins and catacombs on a search for a secret hidden on the ground of an ancient Underwater fortress. Test your fighting skills to overcome the hordes of darkness and to discover that the victory must be paid with blood, pain and maybe your own soul."},{"t":"Kong: King of Atlantis","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 25"},{"t":"Kong: The 8th Wonder of the World","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 21"},{"t":"Kusari","p":["Windows"],"d":"Leaf","u":"Aquaplus","g":"Visual novel, Eroge","r":"September 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kusari"},{"t":"L.A. Rush","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"October 10","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L.A._Rush"},{"t":"Land of the Dead: Road to Fiddler's Green","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Brainbox Games","u":"Groove Games","g":"First-person shooter","r":"October 20, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Land_of_the_Dead:_Road_to_Fiddler's_Green","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9r9s.jpg","s":"Based on the feature film from George A. Romero, this new chapter in the Living Dead series is a full-featured, first-person shooter video game sets players in the midst of a gruesome adventure in which they battle to save themselves – and a diminishing living population - from an army of the dead bent on spreading a zombie plague. Developed by Brainbox Games, a Digital Extremes Studio, and using the Unreal Engine, the game features terrifying zombies, frightening effects, an immersive storyline and key environments seen in the film. Gamers can also join intense, bone-chilling multiplayer battles against the dead on Xbox Live."},{"t":"Law & Order: Criminal Intent","p":["Windows"],"d":"Legacy Interactive","g":"Adventure","r":"November 15, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Law_&_Order:_Criminal_Intent_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7bqt.jpg","s":"The world of the hit television show Law & Order: Criminal Intent comes to life on the PC as players take on the role of Detective Robert Goren to investigate four all-new murder cases while taking the on the role of Detective Robert Goren. Actor Vincent D'Onofrio voices the character while you scrutinize the crime scenes, analyze evidence and interview witnesses and suspects. With beautifully rendered graphics and voices just like members of the show's cast, this thrilling 3rd person mystery adventure game will have players feeling like they've stepped into an actual episode of Law & Order: Criminal Intent."},{"t":"Legend of Kay","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 20","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Legend_of_Kay"},{"t":"Legion Arena","p":["Windows"],"d":"Slitherine Strategies","u":"Black Bean Games, Strategy First, Freeverse Software","g":"Computer wargame","r":"November 11, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Legion_Arena","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2h4o.jpg"},{"t":"Lego Star Wars: The Video Game","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance","GameCube"],"r":"April 5"},{"t":"Lexulous","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lexulous"},{"t":"LifeSigns: Surgical Unit","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"Spike","u":"Spike, DreamCatcher Games, JoWooD Productions","g":"Adventure, simulator","r":"October 20, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LifeSigns:_Surgical_Unit","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cobkwz.jpg","s":"A medical-themed adventure game for the DS. It is the sequel to the Japan-only DS launch title Kenshuui Tendo Dokuta, which inspired the more gameplay-heavy Trauma Center series."},{"t":"Lost in Blue","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"September 27","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lost_in_Blue"},{"t":"Lovely Idol","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lovely_Idol"},{"t":"Lucky Star Moe Drill","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucky_Star_Moe_Drill"},{"t":"Lugaru","p":["macOS","Linux","Windows"],"g":"Fighting, Platform, Hack and slash/Beat 'em up, Indie","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lugaru","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2yww.jpg","s":"Follow Turner, a rebel bunny rabbit with impressive combat skills in his quest to find those responsible for slaughtering his village. Uncover a far-reaching conspiracy involving the corrupt leaders of the rabbit republic and the wolves of the nearby lands.\n\nStreamlined Combat: Gone are the days of combo memorization and button mashing. Lugaru uses a context-sensitive combat system to put all the moves at your finger tips. It’s up to you to choose the right move at the right time and think your way through the fights.\n\nOpen-Ended Strategy: Each level presents you with an environment and a series of enemies. How you choose to defeat your adversaries is entirely up to you. Storm in from the front and fight everyone at once or ambush your foes one at a time with stealth attacks."},{"t":"Lula 3D","p":["Windows"],"d":"cdv Software Entertainment","u":"cdv Software Entertainment","g":"Erotic, Adventure","r":"June 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lula_3D","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2h6i.jpg","s":"Lula 3D is an adult video game. It was published and developed by CDV Software."},{"t":"Lumines","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"March 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lumines"},{"t":"Lunar: Dragon Song","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"September 27"},{"t":"Luxor","p":["macOS","Windows","Wii","PlayStation Portable"],"d":"MumboJumbo, Absolutist","u":"MumboJumbo","g":"Puzzle","r":"May 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luxor_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3plp.jpg","s":"Embark on an expedition through ancient sands in this exciting action-puzzler.\nA unique take on the match three puzzle, Luxor challenges you to think quickly and aim carefully as you explore the path of the Nile."},{"t":"Madagascar","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS"],"r":"May 24","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madagascar_(video_game)"},{"t":"Madagascar: Operation Penguin","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 7"},{"t":"Madden NFL 06","p":["PlayStation 2","GameCube","Nintendo DS","Windows"],"r":"August 8","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madden_NFL_06"},{"t":"Magna Carta: Crimson Stigmata","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"November 15"},{"t":"Major League Baseball 2K5","p":["Xbox","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Kush Games","u":"2K","g":"Sports","r":"February 23, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Major_League_Baseball_2K5","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/tkmx3qu3pyejtyexb9uk.jpg","s":"Not enhanced, not adjusted, not tweaked, and not updated. Major League Baseball 2K5 is all new and sets the standard for baseball video games. Dominate the diamond with innovative pitching and batting controls, all-new Maximum Fielding and On Command baserunning featuring active picture-in-picture display, quick select controls, and a plethora of slide options. Indulge in the true MLB atmosphere as a brand-new graphics engine brings stadiums, player models, animations, weather effects, and cut-scenes to life in breathtaking detail. With an exclusive ESPN presentation system featuring expert commentary from Jon Miller, Joe Morgan, and Karl Ravech in-studio, Major League Baseball 2K5 is your ticket to the Big Leagues."},{"t":"Makai Kingdom: Chronicles of the Sacred Tome","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"July 26"},{"t":"Manhattan Chase","p":["Windows"],"d":"Team6 Game Studios","u":"Denda","g":"Action-adventure, driving, third-person shooter","r":"June 1, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan_Chase"},{"t":"Mario and Luigi: Partners in Time","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 28"},{"t":"Mario Kart Arcade GP","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Namco, Bandai Namco Studios","u":"Namco, Nintendo, Bandai Namco Amusement","g":"Racing","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Kart_Arcade_GP","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co21z5.jpg","s":"Mario Kart Arcade GP is an arcade-only iteration of Nintendo's Mario Kart series, developed by Namco. Designed for the Triforce arcade board (also used for F-Zero AX), players can race as one of eleven characters on twenty-four tracks. On certain machines, for an additional fee, a player's data can be saved on a magnetic card which can be inserted into the machine again later to retain unlocked items and records. Nintendo's limited role of development was mainly isolated to ensuring that it was a worthy title for the established franchise.\n\nThis game's arcade cabinet houses a camera that will take a photograph of the player's face. The photo can be customized and then will be displayed above the player's character during multiplayer races.\n\nThe game is noted for being the first Mario Kart to feature playable crossover characters: Namco's Pac-Man, Ms. Pac-Man and Blinky. The game's sequel also featured Mametchi, a character from the Tamagotchi games. The third installment included Don from the Taiko no Tatsujin franchise."},{"t":"Mario Kart DS","p":["Nintendo DS"],"u":"Nintendo","r":"November 14, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Kart_DS"},{"t":"Mario Party 7","p":["GameCube"],"r":"November 7","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Party_7"},{"t":"Mario Party Advance","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"March 28","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Party_Advance"},{"t":"Mario Superstar Baseball","p":["GameCube"],"r":"August 29","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_Superstar_Baseball"},{"t":"Mario Tennis: Power Tour","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"December 5"},{"t":"Mars Daybreak","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mars_Daybreak"},{"t":"Marvel Nemesis: Rise of the Imperfects","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Nintendo DS","PlayStation Portable"],"r":"September 20"},{"t":"Massive Snowboarding","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Gameloft","u":"Gameloft","g":"Snowboarding","r":"September 10, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massive_Snowboarding"},{"t":"Master of Epic","p":["Windows"],"d":"Konami, Gonzo Rosso Online","g":"MMORPG","r":"April 1, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Master_of_Epic","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4upb.jpg","s":"An MMORPG released only in Japan."},{"t":"Medal of Honor: European Assault","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"June 7"},{"t":"Medieval Kings Chess II","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Magmic Games","u":"Magmic Games","g":"Traditional","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medieval_Kings_Chess_II"},{"t":"MediEvil: Resurrection","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"September 13"},{"t":"Mega Man Battle Network 5","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"June 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mega_Man_Battle_Network_5"},{"t":"Mega Man Battle Network 5: Double Team DS","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 1","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mega_Man_Battle_Network_5"},{"t":"Mega Man Maverick Hunter X","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Capcom","u":"Capcom","g":"Platform","r":"December 15, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mega_Man_Maverick_Hunter_X"},{"t":"Mega Man X8","p":["Windows"],"r":"September 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mega_Man_X8"},{"t":"Mega Man Zero 4","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 4","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mega_Man_Zero_4"},{"t":"Memories Off 5: Togireta Film","p":["PlayStation 2","PlayStation Portable","Windows"],"d":"KID, 5pb.","u":"CyberFront, 5pb.","g":"Visual novel","r":"October 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memories_Off_5:_Togireta_Film","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coavfm.jpg","s":"The 5th entry in the main Memories Off series."},{"t":"Memories Off After Rain","p":["PlayStation 2"],"g":"Adventure, Visual Novel","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memories_Off_After_Rain","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coavfe.jpg","s":"A three volume set of epilogue stories featuring characters from Memories Off and 2nd."},{"t":"Mercenaries: Playground of Destruction","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"January 11"},{"t":"Metal Gear Acid","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"March 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metal_Gear_Acid"},{"t":"Metal Gear Solid 3: Subsistence","p":["PlayStation 2"],"u":"Konami","r":"December 22, 2005"},{"t":"Metal Saga","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Success, Crea-Tech","u":"Success, Atlus","g":"Role-playing video game","r":"June 9, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metal_Saga","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1ox5.jpg","s":"A follow-up to the Metal Max games, Metal Saga is set in the same post-apocalyptic world as its predecessors - a world populated by bounty hunters, rangers, bandits, and mutant monsters. You take the role of a bounty hunter who has to travel the world, looking for \"wanted\" people. Accompanied by a soldier, a mechanic, and a cyborg dog, the hero must survive a journey west that will ultimately take him to remote places and lead him to battles against evil.\n\nMetal Saga has a less linear story line that one would normally expect from a Japanese RPG - a story line that develops according to the missions you decide to take, which in their turn lead to new events and finally to different endings. The combat system features traditional party management and turn-based battles, with the addition of Metal Max's trademark tank combat. When you acquire tanks for your characters, you can use them in battles. Tanks get damaged and broken, but you will be able to customize them by finding parts scattered across the world and assembling them to build new models. Based on the model of tank many different kinds of weapons, cannons, and accessories can be equipped to it, making for hundreds of different options. Tanks can even be given a custom paint job that is saved to the memory card."},{"t":"Meteos","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"June 27","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meteos"},{"t":"Metroid Prime Pinball","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"October 24","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metroid_Prime_Pinball"},{"t":"Midnight Bowling","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Gameloft","u":"Gameloft","g":"Sports","r":"November 7, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_Bowling","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7rjp.jpg","s":"Midnight Bowling is a bowling video game by Gameloft originally released for mobile phones. A version with enhanced graphics was also released for WiiWare, and under the name Midnight Bowling 3D for phones. It is part of Gameloft's Midnight series, which includes Midnight Pool, Midnight Casino and Midnight Hold'em Poker, and the game was also included in the Midnight Play! Pack compilation for the Nintendo DS. In November 2008, it was made available for the iOS via Apple's App Store."},{"t":"Midnight Club 3: DUB Edition","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","PlayStation Portable"],"r":"April 11"},{"t":"Midnight Pool","p":["Mobile phone","Windows","N-Gage"],"d":"Gameloft Montreal","u":"Gameloft","g":"Sports simulation – pool","r":"April 8, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_Pool"},{"t":"Midway Arcade Treasures 3","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Digital Eclipse, Gamestar, Midway Studios San Diego","u":"Midway","g":"Racing","r":"September 26, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midway_Arcade_Treasures_3"},{"t":"Midway Arcade Treasures: Extended Play","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"December 13"},{"t":"Mile High Pinball","p":["N-Gage"],"d":"Ideaworks3D","u":"Nokia","g":"Pinball","r":"October 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mile_High_Pinball","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6diu.jpg","s":"An N-Gage pinball game."},{"t":"Minerva","p":["Windows"],"d":"Adam Foster","g":"First-person shooter, puzzle","r":"September 2, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minerva_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5km0.jpg","s":"In Minerva, the player character is an anonymous person (who is hinted to be a renegade Overwatch Soldier in the in-game messages) who has either acquired or been provided with a stolen HEV suit. Guided by the mysterious Minerva, the player character is deployed on a tiny island occupied by the Combine - an island which hosts a huge facility - with the goal of infiltrating it and discovering its purpose."},{"t":"Mini Desktop Racing","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows"],"d":"Data Design Interactive","u":"Metro3D Europe, Data Design Interactive, Conspiracy Entertainment","g":"Racing","r":"July 20, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mini_Desktop_Racing","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4aid.jpg","s":"Mini Desktop Racing lets you loose with a crazy selection of officially licensed Minis, each accurately rendered with distinctive performance abilities. Players race in a variety of mini cars around a variety of desktop areas. The game offers reasonably interactive courses by allowing players to \"turn on fans\" and \"spill drinks\" in attempts to hinder opponents."},{"t":"Minions of Mirth","p":["macOS","Windows"],"d":"Prairie Games, Inc.","u":"Prairie Games, Inc.","g":"MMORPG","r":"December 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minions_of_Mirth","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7zh3.jpg","s":"Minions of Mirth is a role-playing game for Mac OS X and Microsoft Windows by Prairie Games, Inc. The game includes both a single-player and a massively multi-player mode. There are two editions of the game: a free version and a paid version which opens additional character abilities.\n\nThe game was released on the December 16th, 2005. Following a hard drive failure on September 18, 2017, servers were shutdown."},{"t":"MLB 2006","p":["PlayStation 2","PlayStation Portable"],"r":"March 8","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/989_Sports_Major_League_Baseball_series"},{"t":"Monster Rancher EVO","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Tecmo","u":"Tecmo","g":"Life simulation, role-playing video game","r":"December 8, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monster_Rancher_EVO","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3tsc.jpg","s":"Monster Rancher EVO introduces an evolution in monster breeding with an intricate character-driven story, a two-phase training system, three-on-three battles and the ability to raise multiple monsters at a time. Players will balance monster breeding with role-playing exploration as they join in the adventures of Julio, a young circus performer with dreams of becoming a champion monster breeder. Traveling with the circus to seven different towns, the player will meet new adventures and new friends who can help with training and breeding monsters.\n\nKeeping in tradition, Monster Rancher EVO features the series' unique media disc input system that creates monsters based on the CD, PlayStation 2 game, or DVD the player inserts into the PlayStation 2, this latest incarnation of Monster Rancher presents an evolution of the series."},{"t":"Morning's Wrath","p":["Windows"],"d":"Ethereal Darkness Interactive","u":"Ethereal Darkness Interactive","g":"RPG","r":"October 1, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morning's_Wrath","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cocko1.jpg","s":"An Action RPG heavily inspired by Diablo. Play as Princess Morning on a quest to master the ways of magic and save her kingdom from invasion."},{"t":"Mortal Kombat: Deception","p":["GameCube"],"r":"March 1"},{"t":"Mortal Kombat: Shaolin Monks","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"September 30"},{"t":"Mortal Kombat: Shaolin Monks (US)","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"September 16"},{"t":"Motocross Mania 3","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"April 27","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Motocross_Mania_3"},{"t":"MotoGP 3: Ultimate Racing Technology","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"r":"August 30"},{"t":"MotoGP 4","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Namco","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment, Namco, Namco Bandai Games","g":"Racing","r":"May 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MotoGP_4"},{"t":"MotoGP: Ultimate Racing Technology 3","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Climax Racing","u":"THQ","g":"Racing","r":"August 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MotoGP:_Ultimate_Racing_Technology_3","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1mqb.jpg"},{"t":"Musashi: Samurai Legend","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"March 15"},{"t":"Mutant Storm Reloaded","p":["Xbox 360"],"r":"November 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mutant_Storm_Reloaded"},{"t":"MVP Baseball 2005","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"February 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MVP_Baseball_2005"},{"t":"MX vs. ATV Unleashed","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"March 16","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MX_vs._ATV_Unleashed"},{"t":"MX World Tour Featuring Jamie Little","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Impulse Games","u":"Crave Entertainment, Play-It","g":"Racing","r":"April 5, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MX_World_Tour_Featuring_Jamie_Little"},{"t":"Myst V: End of Ages","p":["Windows"],"g":"Adventure, Casual","r":"September 20","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/208110","i":"images/steam-208110.jpg","s":"The Grand Finale of the greatest adventure! Decide the fate of a civilization in this triumphant final chapter to the Myst saga. Embark on an epic journey into the heart of a shattered empire as the only explorer who can still save it— or destroy it with the wrong choices."},{"t":"Namco Museum Battle Collection","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Namco","u":"Namco, Namco Hometek, Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Various","r":"February 24, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Namco_Museum_Battle_Collection"},{"t":"Namco Museum: 50th Anniversary","p":["Game Boy Advance","PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube","Windows"],"d":"Digital Eclipse","u":"Namco, Namco Hometek, Electronic Arts","g":"Various","r":"August 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Namco_Museum:_50th_Anniversary"},{"t":"Namco × Capcom","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Monolith Soft","u":"Namco","g":"Tactical role-playing","r":"May 26, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Namco_%C3%97_Capcom","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3d9n.jpg","s":"Namco X Capcom is an action tactical role-playing video game developed by and featuring characters from games produced by companies Namco and Capcom. The game centres on two original characters created for it, Reiji Arisu and Xiaomu. The two of them work for a special unit called Shinra, which is tasked with investigating spirits and other otherworldly disturbances. The game is a hybrid of action and tactical role-playing games. Movement is done on a square grid with turns being determined by figuring out which character has the highest AP. On the player's turn, he or she can move his character into position and choose to attack an enemy."},{"t":"NamCollection","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Namco","u":"Namco","g":"Compilation","r":"July 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NamCollection"},{"t":"Nancy Drew: Last Train to Blue Moon Canyon","p":["Windows"],"g":"Action, Adventure, Casual, RPG, Simulation","r":"September 15","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/31810","i":"images/steam-31810.jpg","s":"Catch this train — it’s your ticket to solving a century-old mystery!"},{"t":"Nancy Drew: Secret of the Old Clock","p":["Windows"],"g":"Adventure","r":"July 12","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/31880","i":"images/steam-31880.jpg","s":"Venture into the Past and Outwit a Criminal Before Time Runs Out!"},{"t":"Nano Breaker","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"February 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nano_Breaker"},{"t":"Nanostray","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"July 19","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nanostray"},{"t":"Narbacular Drop","p":["Windows"],"d":"Nuclear Monkey Software","u":"DigiPen Institute of Technology","g":"Puzzle-platform game","r":"April 19, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narbacular_Drop","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3bes.jpg","s":"Narbacular Drop is an environmental puzzle video game developed by Nuclear Monkey Software. It was released for free online in 2005 for Microsoft Windows. It was the senior game project of students attending DigiPen Institute of Technology. The gameplay consists of navigating a dungeon using an innovative portal system. The player controls a pair of interconnected portals that can be placed on any non-metallic surface (wall, ceiling, or floor). Gabe Newell, managing director of Valve Corporation, took interest in the team's work and employed the whole staff at Valve. The developers went on to make Portal (2007) using many of the same concepts.\n\nThe word Narbacular, which does not exist in any dictionary, was chosen primarily to aid in internet search engine results.\n\nBeing mostly a proof of applied concept, the game contains only six puzzles to solve. However, members of the Narbacular Drop forum community have created a catalog of custom maps."},{"t":"Narc","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"g":"Shooter","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narc_(2005_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8cad.jpg","s":"NARC is a 3rd-person shooter that has the player tracking the distribution of the deadly new narcotic \"Liquid Soul\" across two different cities in Asia and the U.S.A. The player controls one of two characters - Narcotics detective Jack Forezenski (voiced by Michael Madsen), or D.E.A. agent Marcus Hill (voiced by Bill Belamy). Both are led by Narcotics chief Joe Kowalski (voiced by Ron Pearlman), and the player switches between the two as the story unfolds.\n\nAs an undercover cop, players are free to roam the streets and dispense justice at their discretion. Aside from storyline missions, players can encounter 12 types of randomized street crimes and stop them to boost their \"badge rating\" (loosely, a measure of their trust within the police)."},{"t":"Narcissu","p":["macOS","Linux","Windows"],"d":"Stage-nana","u":"Insani, Sekai Project","g":"Visual novel","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narcissu","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9svk.jpg","s":"The anonymous protagonist is diagnosed with lung cancer shortly after his twentieth birthday, and is admitted to hospice care at a hospital in Mito, Ibaraki. There he meets Setsumi, a woman who is two years older than he is, who is also terminally ill. Finding that they both refuse to die in the hospital or at home with their families, they run away together in a silver Honda Integra belonging to the protagonist's father."},{"t":"Naruto: Ultimate Ninja 3","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"CyberConnect2","u":"Bandai, Namco Bandai Games","g":"Fighting game","r":"December 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naruto:_Ultimate_Ninja_3","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1u9b.jpg","s":"NARUTO: Ultimate Ninja 3 makes leaps in the franchise with a host of “firsts” for the series. Players can now live through and be a part of all the major events that defined Story Arc 1 in Heroes History mode. Also, ninja-in-training can customize their characters with the Ultimate Jutsu which gives them that extra bit of edge during battle and allows them to earn points towards upgrading their strength, defense, chakra, agility and other special abilities. Turn playable characters into more powerful ninja of unprecedented size or summon giant creatures as allies with the new Summoning mode. In addition, NARUTO fans throughout North America can experience the game in both English and original Japanese voice over. In keeping with the tradition of the series, an exclusive and original story has players exploring the massive 3D rendered Hidden Leaf Village, participating in battle royale matches and completing more than 55 missions. The experience doesn’t stop there as tons of unlockable content are available to offer loads of replay value including movies, music and cards"},{"t":"NASCAR 06: Total Team Control","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"EA Tiburon","u":"EA Sports","g":"Racing","r":"August 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NASCAR_06:_Total_Team_Control","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co313h.jpg","s":"Take command of the biggest teams in NASCAR by building a multi-car dynasty with NASCAR 06: Total Team Control. In the first-ever Squad Based Racing experience, you are not alone. Radio to teammates for assistance, while managing on-track partnerships, or take the wheel of a teammate's car in the middle of a race to fend off rivals. With all-new game controls, including real-time voice command, communicate with your crew chief, spotters, and on-track allies to help punch your team through the pack. As an owner, build your own racing empire or even buy top NASCAR Teams like Hendrick Motorsports. Earn the title of Teammate, Champion, and Hero in NASCAR 06: Total Team Control."},{"t":"NASCAR SimRacing","p":["Windows"],"d":"EA Tiburon","u":"EA Sports","g":"Simulation, Sports, Racing","r":"February 15, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NASCAR_SimRacing","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7ydk.jpg","s":"NASCAR SimRacing, abbreviated NSR, is a computer racing simulator developed by EA Tiburon and released on February 15, 2005, by EA Sports for Microsoft Windows. The game includes all of the 2004 NEXTEL Cup Series tracks including Pocono Raceway as an unlockable like in NASCAR 2005: Chase for the Cup The game cover features the vehicles of Ryan Newman, Ron Hornaday and Chad Chaffin on the cover.\n\nThe game features NASCAR's top 3 series, the Nextel Cup, Busch, and Craftsman Truck Series. The game features a single-player career mode as well as multiplayer online gameplay. The game also features many paint schemes used during the 2004 and 2005 Cup Series; however the original release featured the 2005 cars replaced with their 2004 counterparts. This game was the last NASCAR game to be released for the PC by EA; the next NASCAR game for PC would be NASCAR The Game: 2013 by Eutechnyx"},{"t":"Navy Field Online","p":["Windows"],"r":"October 20"},{"t":"NBA","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"d":"San Diego Studio","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Sports","r":"March 24, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBA_(2005_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coaarx.jpg"},{"t":"NBA 06","p":["PlayStation Portable","PlayStation 2"],"d":"San Diego Studio","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Sports","r":"October 4, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBA_06","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co726y.jpg","s":"NBA 06 deviates from other traditional NBA titles with the addition of the Life Mode. While it does include classic features such as exhibition, season, franchise, and multiplayer modes, the life mode is a take similar to the MLB: The Show.\n\nThe life mode has the player take control of an NBA rookie right out of college and just being drafted. As in the MLB Show series, the player may only control one character and cannot control others on their team or make any management decisions. The player's role of the team will be determined by their performance on and off the court. The better the player is at playing basketball and being a teammate, the more likelier they will be a huge part of the team and receive better contracts and endorsement deals.\n\nLikewise, the decisions the player makes off the court will determine who they are perceived as well, such as how they interact with teammates, what they buy or who they hang around with. The player can also train their character through a series of 20 mini-games, e.g. one-on-one, three-on-three, etc.\n\nThe game also features Showtime Gameplay, where the player may increase attributes and become a better team player with no-look alley-oops and highlight reel dunks. It also has online capabilities as well as the option of utilizing the EyeToy to put the user's face onto a created character."},{"t":"NBA 2K6","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Xbox 360"],"d":"Visual Concepts","u":"2K","g":"Sports","r":"September 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBA_2K6","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2gnf.jpg","s":"NBA 2K6 hits the hardwood with all the ingredients necessary to continue its reign as the #1 rated pro basketball game. Achieve NBA superstar status with the new 24/ mode, where created players now partake in training camps, competitions and even land endorsement deals. Elevate your game by utilizing the innovative V.I.P. System to challenge profiels of friends and other NBA 2K6 ballers across the country that match their game-play tendencies down to every minute detail. Then head over to The Crib to customize your pad, buy music and unlock mini-games with crib credits earned playing the game. With the industry leading online experience and unrivaled francise control, NBA 2K6 offers the most complete and entertaining roundball experience available."},{"t":"NBA Live 06","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Windows","Xbox","Xbox 360","PlayStation Portable","Mobile phone"],"d":"EA Canada","u":"EA Sports","g":"Sports","r":"September 26, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBA_Live_06","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1oxr.jpg","s":"NBA Live 06 is the first game in the franchise to reach next generation consoles."},{"t":"NBA Street Showdown","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"April 27","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBA_Street_Showdown"},{"t":"NBA Street V3","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"EA Canada","u":"EA Sports BIG","g":"Sports","r":"February 8, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBA_Street_V3","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3ddi.jpg"},{"t":"NCAA Football 06","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"EA Tiburon","u":"EA Sports","g":"Sports","r":"July 12, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NCAA_Football_06","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8rnb.jpg","s":"NCAA Football '06, known colloquially as College Football 2006, is a collegiate American football video game which was released on July 11, 2005. It is the successor to NCAA Football 2005 in the NCAA Football series. The product features former Michigan Wolverines standout and Heisman Trophy winner Desmond Howard on the cover. He is the only cover athlete not to have played the year before their respective game; Howard last played at Michigan in 1991. It is the only game in the series as of 2013 to have a music soundtrack, as the other games play school fight songs and general band pieces, and the last game in the series to feature FCS (Division 1-AA) teams."},{"t":"NCAA March Madness 06","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"EA Canada","u":"EA Sports","g":"Sports","r":"October 12, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NCAA_March_Madness_06","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/hhq3iolojzuqnkqdpnpw.jpg","s":"Electronic Art's NCAA Basketball franchise returns with new and improved features for the 2005 season. The new lockdown stick allows you to force opponent's to make easier turnovers and make smoother passes to teammates. You can have your senior captain get your team into the game and get your crowd fired up to rattle your rivals into mistakes. With an much more updated dynasty mode you can now recruit Junior College players with updated stats to keep you ahead of your rivals and relive some of the greatest moments with College Classics and play up to 20 great games, repeating history or completely changing it."},{"t":"Need for Speed Underground: Rivals","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"March 14"},{"t":"Need for Speed: Most Wanted","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS","PlayStation Portable","Xbox 360"],"g":"Action, Adventure, Racing","r":"November 15","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1262560","i":"images/steam-1262560.jpg","s":"The open-world action in Need for Speed Most Wanted gives you the freedom to drive your way. Hit jumps and shortcuts, switch cars, lie low or head for terrain that plays to your vehicle’s unique strengths. Fight your way past cops and rivals using skill, high-end car tech and tons of nitrous."},{"t":"Neo Geo Battle Coliseum","p":["PlayStation 2","Arcade"],"d":"SNK Playmore","u":"Sega, SNK Playmore, Ignition Entertainment","g":"Fighting","r":"July 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neo_Geo_Battle_Coliseum","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8bs7.jpg","s":"Neo Geo Battle Coliseum (abbreviated NGBC or NBC) is a 2 on 2 tag team fighting game for the Atomiswave arcade board released in 2005. The game features characters from several SNK and ADK titles. Subsequently a PlayStation 2 version of the game was released in Japan, North America, and Europe. The Xbox Live Arcade version was released worldwide on June 9, 2010."},{"t":"Neo Geo Online Collection","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"SNK Playmore","u":"SNK Playmore","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neo_Geo_Online_Collection"},{"t":"Neopets: The Darkest Faerie","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"November 15"},{"t":"Neuro Hunter","p":["Windows"],"r":"September 23","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neuro_Hunter"},{"t":"New York Nights: Success in the City","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Gameloft Montreal","u":"Gameloft","g":"Action-adventure, life simulation","r":"November 1, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_Nights:_Success_in_the_City","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9qbn.jpg","s":"New York Nights: Success in the City is an action-adventure life simulation video game developed by Gameloft Montreal and published by Gameloft."},{"t":"Nexuiz","p":["Linux","Windows","macOS","Amiga"],"d":"Alientrap","u":"Alientrap","g":"First-person shooter","r":"May 31, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nexuiz","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2hqj.jpg","s":"Nexuiz is a fast-paced quake-like fps developed and published by Alientrap in 2005"},{"t":"NFL Street 2 Unleashed","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"March 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NFL_Street_2"},{"t":"NHL 06","p":["PlayStation 2","GameCube","Windows","Xbox"],"d":"EA Canada","u":"EA Sports","g":"Sports","r":"September 6, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NHL_06","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2guy.jpg","s":"Hit the ice with EA Sports' NHL 06 for the XBOX. This entry in the NHL series builds on the 2005 version by adding new rules and an up to date rooster that includes just about every big name in the National Hockey League. NHL 06 includes everything from NHL 05, including the revamped shooting controls. New to the 2006 version is the use of the left analog stick for deking, which in hockey terms means to dodge and fake out defenders. The right analog stick is used to pull off fancy moves like a spin or between the legs pass. These fancy moves will distract goalkeepers, giving the gamer an opening to shoot. The drawback to these moves is that only superstar characters can pull them off regularly. The game includes many of the traditional hockey game modes, including dynasty mode. In dynasty mode, gamers will control their own hockey team and have to deal with outside pressures, sponsors, and more while trying to meet the team philosophy, which is different for each team. Other modes include single season, leagues and tournaments, quick game, and online play. The graphics of NHL 06 are top notch. This time, they've been tweaked to accurately show character size differences. The defense players and goalkeepers, who are traditionally larger players, actually look larger, while the smaller and faster scorers are indeed a little thinner and smaller. This is just one small change that adds to the overall amazing gameplay of NHL 06."},{"t":"NHL 2K6","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Xbox 360"],"d":"Kush Games","u":"2K","g":"Sports","r":"September 6, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NHL_2K6","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2hmn.jpg","s":"NHL 2K6 is a realistic hockey simulation in which you must take part in all aspects of running a franchise, from scheduling workouts to hitting a slap shot. The game includes revamped animations and more realistic player movement. NHL 2K6 also includes on-the-fly coaching that lets you make decisions during the game to affect your teams strategy and execution. You can even go online to challenge other gamers, track stats, or join a league."},{"t":"NHL 5-On-5 2006","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"THQ Wireless","u":"THQ Wireless","g":"Sports, ice hockey","r":"October 10, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NHL_5-On-5_2006"},{"t":"NHL Eastside Hockey Manager 2005","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"Sports Interactive","u":"Sega","g":"Sports, ice hockey","r":"May 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NHL_Eastside_Hockey_Manager_2005","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7vpe.jpg","s":"NHL Eastside Hockey Manager 2005's database features over 20 playable leagues, with more than 3000 teams and in excess of 30000 players and staff. The new 2D snapshot view allows coaches to watch the action unfold second-by-second, making key decisions on the fly. As usual, all competition rules and regulations are fully represented for the coming season. Brand new in 2005 are Training Camps. Team can now prepare for the new season, trying out new lines, different tactics, and players hoping to crack the roster.\n\nThe North American version includes the rosters from the end of August (2005) and NHL CBA. Owners of the European or digital version received this as a free season update."},{"t":"NiBiRu: Age of Secrets","p":["Windows"],"d":"Future Games","u":"The Adventure Company","g":"Adventure","r":"March 11, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NiBiRu:_Age_of_Secrets","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coaxoz.jpg","s":"During the construction of a new highway bypass, workers discover an entrance to an old tunnel. After they enter the tunnel, they find out that it was probably a German tunnel intentionally backfilled at the end of World War II. They contact an employee of the Western Bohemian Museum who then informs the superior body in Prague about their findings. The news about the discovery is published by the regional press the next day and there is tremendous buzz in the archeology community of the new find.\n\nMartin Holan, a linguistics and archeology student is contacted by his uncle to examine the mysterious World War II tunnel. A friend of Martin’s uncle is supposed to meet Martin upon his arrival to brief him on the mysterious discovery; however, when he arrives in Prague he discovers that she has been brutally murdered.\n\nAnd the Adventure Begins…"},{"t":"Nicktoons Unite!","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 26","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicktoons_Unite!"},{"t":"Night Watch","p":["Windows"],"d":"Nival Interactive","u":"CDV Software","g":"Tactical RPG","r":"August 18, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Watch_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9jfy.jpg","s":"Based on the most successful Russian-made movie ever, the Night Watch game asks players to take part in a millennia-old struggle of supernatural forces; a conflict of which ordinary humans are either completely oblivious, or in which they are unwittingly being used as pawns.\n\nIn the Night Watch universe, there are people among us who appear ordinary, but who are different; they call themselves \"Others.\" These Others can channel magical power as devastating attacks and defenses. Those who support the forces of light are known as the Night Watch, while those that fight on the side of darkness are the Day Watch. These two sides have been locked in an epic battle with the common hope of one ultimately claiming a decisive victory and a right to rule the world."},{"t":"Ninja Gaiden Black","p":["Xbox"],"u":"Tecmo","r":"September 20, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninja_Gaiden_(2004_video_game)#Ninja_Gaiden_Black"},{"t":"Ninjabread Man","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows"],"d":"Data Design Interactive","u":"Metro3D Europe, Data Design Interactive, Conspiracy Entertainment","g":"Platform, action-adventure","r":"July 13, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninjabread_Man","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3ip9.jpg","s":"Ninjabread Man is a 2005 platform game developed and published by Data Design Interactive for the PlayStation 2 and Microsoft Windows. A port for the Wii was released in September 2007 in Europe and Australia, and on 3 October 2007 in North America. Ninjabread Man was later published as part of Data Design Interactive's 'Popcorn Arcade' brand of Wii games. Ninjabread Man is an action-adventure platformer. There are three levels in the game, plus a tutorial level. In order to proceed to the next level, players must collect eight power rods to activate a teleporter. Upon release, Ninjabread Man received universally negative reviews from critics and was criticized for its camera system, graphics, lack of story, short length, and controls; the Wii version received even lower reviews for its use of motion controls and has been listed as one of the worst games of all time."},{"t":"Nintendogs","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"August 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nintendogs"},{"t":"Nintendogs: Best Friends","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"October 24","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nintendogs"},{"t":"Nursery Rhyme","p":["Windows"],"g":"Visual Novel","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nursery_Rhyme_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6948.jpg","s":"Nursery Rhyme is a Japanese adult visual novel developed by Lump of Sugar and released on November 25, 2005 for Windows.\n\nThe game, taking place 500 years after the events of Tayutama: Kiss on my Deity, is set in a fictional Japan where the existence of magic has been recognized by society, and thus has been the subject of much research. Magic is also applied to everyday life; for example, stuffed toys are able to talk. Users of magic must wear a special ring which controls their powers, and are urged to blend in with society.\n\nDespite Nursery Rhyme being set in the future, Japan's culture is depicted as unchanged for the most part. Many of the characters attend Shousei Gakuen, a prestigious all-girls school which provides its students with magic classes, as well as academic courses. Shousei Gakuen hosts a female-dominated sport event known as Sophilos."},{"t":"Oasis","p":["Windows","Mobile phone"],"d":"Mind Control Software","u":"PlayFirst, Activision","g":"Turn-based strategy","r":"April 12, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oasis_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/irxloyh61iuf8v8nohbc.jpg","s":"Oasis is a strategy/puzzle game depicting the journey of an Egyptian prince to unite the fragmented kingdoms of his father's domain. Players explore the sorcerous fog that has descended on these kingdoms, uniting lost cities to fend off barbarian hordes.\n\nSearching the kingdom uses a mechanic similar to Minesweeper, but with the difference that there are no harmful clicks. Each click removes fog from one space and reveals some information about what may be found in nearby spaces. Alternatively, once the player has removed enough fog to reveal useful terrain features, they may use a turn to instead build roads between cities, search them for hidden treasures, or take other actions to prepare for the barbarian hordes.\n\nWhen the player runs out of turns, the barbarians arrive (from where?) and attack. The player will have ten seconds to move people to the nearest city (if the player built the right roads!) and then it's out of your hands. Victory depends on having made the right preparations. So while every click on the map is good, they may not all be equally good for your current situation.\n\nThe full version of the game includes the Pharaoh's Challenge, a selection of campaign games each telling a different story, and each using different variant rules on the basic game."},{"t":"ObsCure","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"g":"Action, Adventure","r":"April 26","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ObsCure","i":"images/steam-254460.jpg","s":"For some time now, Leafmore High School has been the setting for unexplained disappearances. In this survival horror game, you take control of a group of 5 American students. With your friends, you try to unravel the mysterious happenings at this unremarkable-looking school. The night will be long and survival not will not be easy..."},{"t":"Oddworld: Stranger's Wrath","p":["Xbox"],"r":"January 25"},{"t":"One","p":["N-Gage"],"d":"Digital Legends","u":"Nokia","g":"Fighting","r":"October 13, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_(2005_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co63g0.jpg","s":"One is the first ever AAA Nokia N-Gage fighting title. You will be tested in incredible locations, against well-trained bosses with furious gangs who master different fighting techniques and styles. ONE breaks the boundaries of mobile gaming. Experience amazing 3D fighting with stunning motion-captured animations. This is the first ever mobile game with mocap, and includes real-time multiplayer fighting over bluetooth."},{"t":"One Piece","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Dimps Corporation","u":"Bandai Games","g":"Beat 'em up","r":"September 7, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_Piece_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6r8r.jpg","s":"One Piece also referred to as Shonen Jump's One Piece is a 2-D platforming adventure video game for the Nintendo Game Boy Advance based on the 4kids dub of the One Piece anime. Developed by Dimps and published by Bandai, it was released on September 7, 2005. It is the only One Piece game to be only released in the USA, and the first out of two to not see a release in Japan."},{"t":"One Piece: Grand Battle!","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Ganbarion","u":"Bandai","g":"Fighting","r":"March 17, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_Piece:_Grand_Battle!"},{"t":"One Piece: Grand Battle! Rush","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 7"},{"t":"One Piece: Pirates' Carnival","p":["PlayStation 2","GameCube"],"d":"h.a.n.d.","u":"Bandai, Namco Bandai Games","g":"Party","r":"November 23, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_Piece:_Pirates'_Carnival","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2mcb.jpg","s":"One Piece: Pirates’ Carnival brings the crazy pirate party without having to hit the ocean. Players can dominate the game board by defeating up to three friends in a series of zany games guaranteed to tickle the funny bone of the surliest of pirates. Gamers must evade bombs in a dodge ball field, locate the Pandaman, out-maneuver giant feet and more to become King of the Pirates."},{"t":"OpenArena","p":["Windows","Linux","macOS"],"g":"Shooter","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenArena","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5jgy.jpg","s":"OpenArena is a free, community-developed first-person shooter, similar to Quake III: Arena as it is based on the source code of the game along with the ioquake3 engine, and it is licensed under the GNU GPL version 2."},{"t":"Operation: Matriarchy","p":["Windows"],"d":"MADia Entertainment","u":"Buka Entertainment","g":"First-person shooter","r":"August 25, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation:_Matriarchy","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3qn4.jpg","s":"Operation: Matriarchy is a science fiction first-person shooter. In the 24th century mankind has formed itself into the Federation of Earth, and has colonized several other planets. However, around 2350 a mysterious virus ravages the colony planet of Velia, targeting only the females within the population."},{"t":"Oretachi Gēsen Zoku","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Hamster Corporation","u":"Hamster Corporation","g":"Various","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oretachi_G%C4%93sen_Zoku"},{"t":"Osu! Tatakae! Ouendan","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"iNiS Corporation","u":"Nintendo","g":"Music video game","r":"July 28, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osu!_Tatakae!_Ouendan","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co25uu.jpg","s":"Osu! Tatakae! Ouendan, or simply Ouendan, is a rhythm video game developed by iNiS and published by Nintendo for the Nintendo DS handheld game console in 2005, for release only in Japan. Ouendan stars a cheer squad rhythmically cheering for various troubled people, presented in game in the style of a manga comic. In each stage, players use the DS touchscreen to tap specifically marked spots that appear in rhythm to various Japanese pop songs, scoring points for accurate timing and avoiding a poor performance which can cause the stage to end prematurely. Though never released in Western markets, it was a popular import to these regions, leading to the development of the Westernized spiritual sequel Elite Beat Agents, as well as a direct Japanese sequel Moero! Nekketsu Rhythm Damashii Osu! Tatakae! Ouendan 2."},{"t":"Otome wa Boku ni Koishiteru","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otome_wa_Boku_ni_Koishiteru"},{"t":"Outlaw Tennis","p":["Xbox","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Hypnotix","u":"Global Star Software","g":"Sports, fighting","r":"July 26, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outlaw_Tennis","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1oy4.jpg","s":"Outlaw Tennis is a video game based on the sport of tennis published for the Xbox and PlayStation 2, and the last game in the Outlaw series to be released in 2005. Actor and political satirist Stephen Colbert provides the voice of the game's announcer."},{"t":"Outpost Kaloki X","p":["Xbox 360"],"r":"November 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outpost_Kaloki_X"},{"t":"Pac 'n Roll","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"August 16","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pac_%27n_Roll"},{"t":"Pac-Man Pinball Advance","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"May 2","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pac-Man_Pinball_Advance"},{"t":"Pac-Man World 3","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube","Nintendo DS","PlayStation Portable"],"r":"November 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pac-Man_World_3"},{"t":"Pac-Pix","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"April 26","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pac-Pix"},{"t":"Pacific Storm","p":["Windows"],"d":"Lesta Studio","u":"Buka Entertainment, CDV Software","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"November 17, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pacific_Storm","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9nh6.jpg","s":"On December 7, 1941, a major part of the U.S. Pacific navy stationed at Pearl Harbor was assaulted by Japanese planes. Japanese fighters were destroying American aircraft on land and in the air, without giving them a chance for a counterattack. The furious battle of Pearl Harbor became the first in the sequence of gory sea combats.\n\nNow you can take part in all major Pacific battles of World War II. Pacific Storm is a mixture of Real-Time Strategy, war-game and simulator. All major and important sea battles of World War II, which took place in the Pacific Ocean, are included and you can play either for the USA or Japan."},{"t":"Pariah","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"r":"May 3","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pariah_(video_game)"},{"t":"Pathway to Glory: Ikusa Islands","p":["N-Gage"],"d":"Ubisoft RedLynx","u":"Nokia","g":"Turn-based tactics","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pathway_to_Glory:_Ikusa_Islands","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/wwxn3lhcvmgjzxhgklqd.jpg","s":"Commanded by an old navy veteran McDouglas, a squad of allied soldiers take on the horrors of the Pacific Theatre. Only their strong ties to each other and to the seasoned veteran commander can keep them alive."},{"t":"Perfect Dark Zero","p":["Xbox 360"],"r":"November 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perfect_Dark_Zero"},{"t":"Perfect World","p":["Windows"],"d":"Beijing Perfect World","u":"Beijing Perfect World, Games-Masters Ltd., Arc Games, Astrum Entertainment","g":"MMORPG","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perfect_World_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6i9g.jpg","s":"Perfect World is a 3D MMORPG rooted in traditional Chinese culture and mythology. Set in the mythical realm of Pangu, it offers players an immersive adventure experience."},{"t":"Peter Jackson's King Kong: The Official Game of the Movie","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube","Xbox 360","PlayStation Portable"],"r":"November 17"},{"t":"Phantasmagoria of Flower View","p":["Windows"],"d":"Team Shanghai Alice","u":"Team Shanghai Alice","g":"Bullet hell","r":"August 14, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phantasmagoria_of_Flower_View"},{"t":"Phantom Dust","p":["Xbox"],"r":"March 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phantom_Dust"},{"t":"Phoenix Wright: Ace Attorney","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"October 12"},{"t":"Pizza Frenzy","p":["Windows"],"d":"PopCap Games","u":"PopCap Games","g":"Time management","r":"February 2, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pizza_Frenzy","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2zap.jpg","s":"The game contains three game modes based on the same principle. Shown from a top-down view, the player visits different cities where a certain number of pizzas need to be delivered. Before starting a game, the player can select the main topping to offer in that city. Each game, there are two or more pizza houses, one for each type of topping. At irregular intervals, icons with customers appear, requesting a pizza with a specific topping. The player needs to click them and take them back to the delivery house. For each delivered pizza, a tip can be picked up and after a perfect game a zeppelin dropping money appears."},{"t":"Playboy: The Mansion","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"January 25"},{"t":"Plobb!","p":["Windows"],"d":"Nothing","g":"Shoot 'em up","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plobb!"},{"t":"Pokémon Dash","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"March 13","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_Dash"},{"t":"Pokémon Emerald","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"May 1","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_Emerald"},{"t":"Pokémon Mystery Dungeon: Blue Rescue Team and Red Rescue Team","p":["Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS"],"d":"Chunsoft","u":"The Pokémon Company, Nintendo","g":"Roguelike, Role-playing","r":"November 17, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pok%C3%A9mon_Mystery_Dungeon:_Blue_Rescue_Team_and_Red_Rescue_Team"},{"t":"Pokémon XD: Gale of Darkness","p":["GameCube"],"r":"October 3"},{"t":"Polarium","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"April 18","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polarium"},{"t":"Popeye: Rush for Spinach","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"April 24"},{"t":"Postal 2: Corkscrew Rules!","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Postal_2:_Corkscrew_Rules!"},{"t":"Postal²: Share the Pain","p":["Linux"],"r":"February 4","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Postal%C2%B2"},{"t":"Power Rangers S.P.D.","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Natsume Co., Ltd.","u":"THQ","g":"Action","r":"September 6, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Power_Rangers_S.P.D._(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3g40.jpg","s":"THQ sixth game based on the Might Morphin' Power Rangers takes the team into space. POWER RANGERS: SPACE PATROL DELTA for the Game Boy Advance puts players in control of all five members of the Space Patrol Delta team as they battle the evil Emperor Gruumm and his army of robots. In the future, Earth has become home to many different alien races. While most of them are peaceful, some are not. In order to protect earth, six teens were called to form the Space Patrol Delta team. Players will control a certain ranger for each of the nine levels. While the rangers' fighting abilities are similar, each has his or her own unique power. The Red Ranger can move through objects, the Yellow Ranger can create duplicates of herself, the Green Ranger can see heat trails, the Blue Ranger can create a force field, and the Pink Ranger can replicate objects she touches. There's also a Shadow Ranger who has special abilities players will uncover as they progress through the game. Each level in this platformer has players running, jumping, and attacking enemies as they guide the chosen ranger through the many obstacles that Gruumm has created. Each of the nine levels is controlled by a boss that the Rangers must defeat to move on. After certain levels, the Rangers will summon the Megazord to do battle with giant monsters. Fans of the POWER RANGERS won't want to miss this instalment in the series. POWER RANGERS: SPACE PATROL DELTA is an out-of-this-world fighting experience."},{"t":"Predator: Concrete Jungle","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"April 27"},{"t":"Prince of Persia: Revelations","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"December 6"},{"t":"Prince of Persia: The Two Thrones","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube"],"g":"Action, Adventure","r":"November 30","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/13530","i":"images/steam-13530.jpg","s":"The Prince of Persia, a seasoned warrior, returns from the Island of Time to Babylon with his love, Kaileena. Instead of the peace that he longs for, he finds his homeland ravaged by war and the kingdom turned against him."},{"t":"Prison Tycoon","p":["Windows"],"d":"Virtual Playground","u":"ValuSoft","g":"Business simulation game","r":"July 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prison_Tycoon","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/l6zu3rvi7s45oxo33zuy.jpg","s":"Prison Tycoon lets you run your own prison, controlling the buildings, inmates, and more."},{"t":"Pro Evolution Soccer 5","p":["Windows"],"u":"Konami","r":"August 4, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pro_Evolution_Soccer_5"},{"t":"Project Gotham Racing 3","p":["Xbox 360"],"d":"Bizarre Creations","u":"Microsoft Game Studios","g":"Racing","r":"November 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Project_Gotham_Racing_3","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1uoj.jpg","s":"Project Gotham Racing 3 (PGR3 for short) is an arcade-style racing game that was released with the launch of the Xbox 360 on November 22, 2005 for the US market and December 2, 2005 in Europe, and was released on January 12, 2006 in Japan. Developed by Bizarre Creations, it is the third installment in the Project Gotham Racing series. Project Gotham Racing 3 was rated by Official Xbox Magazine (OXM) to be Xbox 360 \"Game Of The Year\" (2005). OXM also rated it \"Best 1st Person (Not Shooter) of the Year\", because of its realistic inside-car view."},{"t":"Project Reality","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Project_Reality"},{"t":"Project Snowblind","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"February 23","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Project_Snowblind"},{"t":"Protöthea","p":["Windows"],"d":"Digital Builders, Sabarasa","u":"ABC Entertainment, Ubisoft","g":"Shoot 'em up","r":"June 13, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prot%C3%B6thea"},{"t":"Psychonauts","p":["Xbox","Windows","PlayStation 2"],"u":"Majesco","g":"Action","r":"April 19, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Psychonauts","i":"images/steam-3830.jpg","s":"A Psychic Odyssey Through the Minds of Misfits, Monsters, and Madmen. This classic action/adventure platformer from acclaimed developers Double Fine Productions follows the story of a young psychic named Razputin."},{"t":"PureSim Baseball 2007","p":["Windows"],"d":"PureSim Software Studios","u":"Matrix Games","g":"Sports, Simulation","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PureSim_Baseball_2007"},{"t":"Pursuit Force","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Bigbig Studios","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Vehicular combat, third-person shooter","r":"November 10, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pursuit_Force","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2nyy.jpg","s":"You can play as a rookie cop battling five different gangs spread throughout Capital City in Pursuit Force. The game features 30 cases for you to close, using 55 different vehicles and 25 types of weapons. Each gang has a unique boss and lieutenant with their own specialized vehicles and missions. Taking down gangs fills up your justice bar, which can be used to slow down time for key stunts, fill up your life, or repair your vehicle. The game features Hollywood-style chases and gunfights to keep the action going during missions."},{"t":"Puyo Pop Fever","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"May 3","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puyo_Pop_Fever"},{"t":"Quake 4","p":["Windows","Xbox 360"],"g":"Action","r":"October 18","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quake_4","i":"images/steam-2210.jpg","s":"As part of the elite Rhino Squad, you must spearhead Earth’s military invasion of a hostile alien homeworld. But, in this desperate war for humanity’s survival against an unrelenting enemy, you may discover that the only way to defeat them...is to become one of them."},{"t":"Quraish","p":["Windows"],"d":"Afkar media Ltd.","u":"Dar al-Fiqr","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"August 2, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quraish_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4l7u.jpg","s":"Quraish: The game is a 2005 real-time strategy 3D computer video game produced by Syrian video game production, Afkar Media. It is the second Arabic language-based game and a third person strategy game based on the early battles of Islam, primarily focusing on the Rashidun Caliphate's successful campaigns against the Eastern Roman Empire and the Sassanid dynasty of Persia."},{"t":"Racing Gears Advance","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 8","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Racing_Gears_Advance"},{"t":"Radiata Stories","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 6","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radiata_Stories"},{"t":"Radirgy","p":["Arcade"],"d":"MileStone Inc.","u":"Able Corporation, MileStone Inc.","g":"Shoot 'em up","r":"October 13, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radirgy","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1w2c.jpg","s":"Radilgy is a vertical shooter with its own unique graphical design taking inspiration from anime and the look of cel-shaded graphics."},{"t":"Rag Doll Kung Fu","p":["Windows","PlayStation 3"],"d":"Qi Creations, Tarsier Studios, Another Place Productions","u":"Merscom, Zoo Digital Publishing, Sony Computer Entertainment, Another Place Productions","g":"Fighting","r":"October 12, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rag_Doll_Kung_Fu","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3tts.jpg","s":"It's a fighting computer game where you have string dolls fighting each other 1 Vs 1. You control your fighter by mouse. All moves are done by dragging your fighter body part (hand, leg or even head)\n\nRag Doll Kung Fu was the first 3rd party games to be sold on Steam."},{"t":"Raiden III","p":["Arcade","PlayStation 2"],"d":"MOSS","u":"MOSS, Taito, UFO Interactive Games, 505 Games","g":"Scrolling shooter","r":"March 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raiden_III","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8m0f.jpg","s":"This game is a port of the original Arcade release. It was released only in Japan in 2006 but it also was re-release worldwide in 2014 for digital download on the Steam platform.\n\nPlayers once again take control of the famous Raiden Supersonic Attack Fighter, red for player 1 and blue for player 2 as usual; there are no selectable ships. Two player mode is enhanced by an exclusive new attack: a beam that is usable whenever one player lines up in front of the other.\n\nIn Double play mode, both players share the live and bomb stocks, and without continue. In PlayStation 2, both players can be played from the same controller."},{"t":"Rainbow Islands Revolution","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"Marvelous Entertainment","u":"Taito, Rising Star Games, Codemasters","g":"Platform","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainbow_Islands_Revolution","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2hhi.jpg","s":"This is an updated version of Rainbow Islands, the sequel to Bubble Bobble, taking the form of a platform game where the player must ascend through vertical levels that are slowly sinking into the ocean. The objective of the source material is to reach the top of each level, taking out any enemies in the way by firing magical rainbows that can trap or eliminate foes as well as providing bridges for the player to walk on. Rainbows remain onscreen for a short amount of time but can be ?broken? by the player if they jump on them. Once broken, the rainbow will fall off the screen, taking out the first enemy it touches. The game also features a pleasing bonus item system where dispatched enemies leave behind items of food that have varying point values and power-ups that have a range of helpful effects. The major feature of this re-interpretation is shifting the entire game away from traditional controls by implementing a global touchscreen control system which radically alters the way in which the game plays. The game is also displayed across both screens of the DS. Rather than being fired by a button press, rainbows are now drawn directly onto the gameplay area using the stylus and movement is executed by dragging the player?s character around the levels. The objective is still to reach the top of the level, but the time limit has been extended to account for the player being unable to move and use rainbows simultaneously. Rainbows are now broken by pressing the stylus onto them."},{"t":"Ratchet & Clank: Going Mobile","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Handheld Games","u":"Sony Pictures Mobile","g":"Platform, shooter","r":"November 2, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ratchet_&_Clank:_Going_Mobile","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co29m1.jpg","s":"Ratchet and Clank are transported into a cell phone via the \"MCGuFIN\" and have to fight their way back out."},{"t":"Ratchet: Deadlocked","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"October 25"},{"t":"Rave Master","p":["GameCube"],"r":"March 8","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rave_Master_(video_game)"},{"t":"Rayman DS","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"March 24"},{"t":"Rayman: Hoodlums' Revenge","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"March 15"},{"t":"Raze's Hell","p":["Xbox"],"r":"April 21","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raze%27s_Hell"},{"t":"Real World Golf","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"In2Games","u":"Valcon Games, Mad Catz","g":"Sports","r":"August 26, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Real_World_Golf","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/fdb4cmamblrnx86msmy7.jpg","s":"Real World Golf was released alongside the \"Gametrak\" peripheral in 2006 by Madcatz. It approximates real golf using straps attached to the player's wrists."},{"t":"Rebel Raiders: Operation Nighthawk","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows"],"d":"Kando Games","u":"Nobilis, XS Games, Kando Games","g":"Action, Flight","r":"October 14, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rebel_Raiders:_Operation_Nighthawk","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/we5yfaasnctzizypgomc.jpg","s":"Command your squadron as you fight against one of the largest air armadas ever unleashed! Rebel Raiders: Operation Nighthawk is an intense flight shooter which emphasizes frantic dogfighting over flight simulation.\nLead the Ghost Squadron for the freedom of the Alliance! Pilot high tech aircraft and engage in non stop, arcade styled aerial combat on missions that will determine the very fate of the world.\n\nExperience a new sense of freedom using the Wii Remote to pilot your aircraft\n\nDefend the front lines with over 20 futuristic fighter and bomber aircraft\n\nUse your skills to unlock secret and powerful weapons upgrades\n\nVoiced cutscenes brings the story and immersive action to life"},{"t":"Rebelstar: Tactical Command","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"September 6"},{"t":"Red Light Center","p":["Windows"],"d":"Utherverse Digital","u":"Utherverse Digital","g":"Virtual world","r":"December 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Light_Center"},{"t":"Red Ninja: End of Honor","p":["Xbox","PlayStation 2"],"r":"March 29"},{"t":"Rengoku: The Tower of Purgatory","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"April 26"},{"t":"Resident Evil 4","p":["PlayStation 2","GameCube"],"u":"Capcom","r":"October 25, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Resident_Evil_4"},{"t":"Retro Atari Classics","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"March 16","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Retro_Atari_Classics"},{"t":"RFactor","p":["Windows"],"d":"Image Space Incorporated","u":"Image Space Incorporated","g":"Racing simulation","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RFactor","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2r4t.jpg","s":"rFactor is a computer racing simulator, designed with the ability to run any type of four-wheeled vehicle from street cars to open wheel cars of any era. rFactor aimed to be the most accurate race simulator of its time. Released in November 2005, rFactor did not have much competition in this market; however it featured many technical advances in tire modeling, complex aerodynamics and a 15 degrees of freedom physics engine."},{"t":"RHEM 2: The Cave","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"Knut Müller","u":"Got Game Entertainment and Virtual Programming","g":"Adventure game","r":"October 25, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RHEM_2:_The_Cave","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cobca1.jpg","s":"RHEM 2 is an adventure game from Knut Müller and Got Game Entertainment and the sequel to RHEM. It is distributed as a Macromedia Director file.\n\nLike Myst and Riven, Rhem 2 is a node-based first-person adventure game. The player explores a series of caverns in search of a certain artifact. The puzzles involve spatial reasoning, operating machinery, and logic."},{"t":"Ridge Racer","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"March 24","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ridge_Racer_(2004_video_game)"},{"t":"Ridge Racer 6","p":["Xbox 360"],"r":"November 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ridge_Racer_6"},{"t":"Rifts: Promise of Power","p":["N-Gage"],"d":"Backbone Entertainment","u":"Nokia","g":"Tactical role-playing","r":"October 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rifts:_Promise_of_Power","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co63ge.jpg","s":"Rifts: Promise of Power is a 2005 video game. The basic mechanics of the game are adapted from the pen-and-paper version, utilizing an Action Point turn based system."},{"t":"Rigs of Rods","p":["Windows"],"g":"Racing, Simulator, Sport","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rigs_of_Rods","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1pck.jpg","s":"Rigs of Rods is an open source vehicle simulator licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3. What makes Rigs of Rods different to most simulators is its unique soft-body physics: vehicles, machines, objects, etc. are simulated in real-time as flexible soft-body objects, giving the simulation an extremely accurate behavior which entirely depends on the physical construction of the vehicles or objects you create."},{"t":"Rise of the Kasai","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"April 5","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rise_of_the_Kasai"},{"t":"Rising Kingdoms","p":["Windows"],"d":"Haemimont Games","u":"Black Bean Games","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"June 17, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rising_Kingdoms","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3yks.jpg","s":"Rising Kingdoms is a real-time strategy game set in a fantasy world."},{"t":"River King: A Wonderful Journey","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Marvelous","u":"Natsume","g":"Fishing, role-playing","r":"January 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River_King:_A_Wonderful_Journey","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6t3v.jpg","s":"Hook, line and sinker, you're part of a long line of fishing folk. From father to son and mother to daughter, knowing where and what to fish was always part of your family mangrove tree. Only one thing is missing from the long list of accomplishments, a fish that shook hooks for generations: The River King. Perhaps today, perhaps this cast, you'll feel the strum of a tight line as the legendary giant pulls you into angling immortality. Play as one of four family members. Assist villagers and other shoreline folk. Win it all in fishing and cooking contests. Take on crafty critters in tricky trivia challenges."},{"t":"Riviera: The Promised Land","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"June 28"},{"t":"Robots","p":["Game Boy Advance","GameCube","Nintendo DS","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Windows"],"d":"Eurocom, Griptonite Games","u":"Vivendi Universal Games","g":"Platform","r":"February 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robots_(2005_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1oz9.jpg","s":"Live the adventures of a genius inventor robot named Rodney Copperbottom as he moves to the big city to work for the company founded by his childhood hero. When Rodney uncovers a villain's plot to take over the city, the brave young bot, with the help of his new friends, overcomes all obstacles to realize his dreams -- and make the world a better place for all robots. Take wild rides in fast-paced robot vehicles, upgrade your gadgets with cooler, more useful parts, and team up with your trusty Wonderbot to solve challenging puzzles, battle evil bots, and explore a highly interactive 3D universe that brings the world of Robots the Movie to life."},{"t":"Rockman EXE Battle Chip Stadium","p":["Arcade"],"u":"Capcom","g":"Real-time tactical role-playing game","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockman_EXE_Battle_Chip_Stadium","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5tsk.jpg"},{"t":"Rockman EXE The Medal Operation","p":["Arcade"],"u":"Capcom","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockman_EXE_The_Medal_Operation","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/fmhwnp5bzxke7jvxurn7.jpg","s":"Rockman EXE: The Medal Operation is a medal arcade game from the Medalusion series released in 2005 only in Japan. This is the second medal game to the Rockman.EXE series, and is themed on Rockman.EXE 5. The player moves on a board that contains different panels, some with six types of mini games, battle games, and a bonus game, some of them including a fishing mini game and a \"Super Battle Game\" against Nebula Gray. There are three slots below the screen that are used for several parts of the game to make decisions by making medals fall around, and the slot a medal falls in will be the choice, which varies from which path the player will take and which hand he will use in a rock-paper-scissors mini game. Players can win prizes like medals (arcade tokens) or packs of milk chocolate by completing the games."},{"t":"Rogue Galaxy","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Level-5","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Action role-playing","r":"December 8, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rogue_Galaxy","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co26fu.jpg","s":"Rogue Galaxy is an action role playing game set in a futuristic fantasy universe, in which the player moves through a continuous environment with no load time between overworld exploration and battles. Battles occur as random encounters, Rogue Galaxy uses a real-time hack and slash combat system in which the player fights with a party of three characters. The player has direct control over only one character, although they can change which character that is at any time. The two NPCs fight independently of the player character, based on a strategy selected prior to the battle. Available strategies include fighting especially aggressively, targeting a specific enemy or not fighting at all. The strategy can also be changed at any time during the battle. Additionally, the player can issue specific orders to the NPCs during combat, such as having them use an item or activate one of their special abilities."},{"t":"Rome: Total Realism","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"Rome: Total Realism Team; RIS Team","u":"Rome: Total Realism Team; RIS Team","g":"Real-time tactics","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rome:_Total_Realism"},{"t":"Rome: Total War: Barbarian Invasion","p":["Windows"],"d":"Creative Assembly","u":"Sega, Feral Interactive","g":"Real-time tactics, turn-based strategy","r":"September 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rome:_Total_War:_Barbarian_Invasion"},{"t":"ROSE Online","p":["MS-DOS","Windows"],"d":"Triggersoft, naROSE: Gravity Interactive, Inc., naROSE: Rednim Games, jROSE: Faith Inc.","u":"naROSE: Rednim Games, jROSE: Faith Inc., naROSE: Gravity Interactive, Inc.","g":"MMORPG","r":"July 7, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ROSE_Online"},{"t":"Rugby 2005","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Windows"],"d":"EA Canada","u":"EA","g":"Sports","r":"March 11, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rugby_2005","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8nkp.jpg","s":"Rugby 2005 is a game in the Rugby series by EA Sports. The game allows players to play as many Rugby nations, both major and minor, and includes many tournaments, such as the Rugby World Cup, the Tri Nations, the Six Nations, and the Super 12.\n\nRugby 2005 is the first EA Rugby title for Xbox, while the Windows version was canceled in the US."},{"t":"Rugby League 2","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Windows"],"d":"Sidhe","u":"Tru Blu Entertainment","g":"Sports","r":"December 8, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rugby_League_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/zp9w3c8h8zf3quunlvnw.jpg"},{"t":"S.L.A.I.: Steel Lancer Arena International","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Genki","u":"Konami","g":"Vehicular combat","r":"September 20, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S.L.A.I.:_Steel_Lancer_Arena_International","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2ypx.jpg","s":"In the year 2071, robots have become the new gladiators, and you're in the pilot's seat. Go head-to-head against other players to see who is the champion."},{"t":"Saint Seiya: The Sanctuary","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Dimps","u":"Bandai","g":"Fighting","r":"April 7, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saint_Seiya:_The_Sanctuary","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cobgbt.jpg","s":"Based on the popular anime series of the same name Saint Seiya: Chapter Sanctuary brings the legendary conflict between the Knights of Athena and the Knights of Ares home to the PlayStation 2. Battling over the Golden Cloth of Sagittarius, more than 20 different fighters square off against one another across several different modes including those of the Story, Versus, and Practice variety. As an added bonus, several of the show's most memorable moments have been recreated using the latest in CG cinematics as well, with licensed voice-overs specifically re-recorded for the videogame version of the story. Available only in Japan."},{"t":"Sakura Wars: So Long, My Love","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Sega GE2 R&D, Red Entertainment","u":"Sega, NIS America","g":"Tactical role-playing, dating sim, visual novel","r":"July 7, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sakura_Wars:_So_Long,_My_Love","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2w43.jpg","s":"Sakura Wars is a Strategy RPG that features a unique sim-based story system. An in-depth storyline exists, much like in any other RPG; however, the player's destiny in the game is not predetermined. Character interaction plays a major role, and your responses to the various characters in the game can ultimately change the story content and even the final outcome. The battle system is divided into two main parts; ground combat and air combat. Ground combat takes place using two-legged mechanized suits, which transform into jet fighters to take the fight to the sky. Every mech unit in the game can transform from battle mech mode to jet fighter mode during combat. Once transformed, weapons and movement methods will change as well. For example, the hero's ground mode utilizes a sword as his main weapon, but in jet mode he will use long-range missiles."},{"t":"Samorost 2","p":["Linux","macOS","Windows"],"d":"Amanita Design","u":"Amanita Design","g":"Graphic adventure","r":"December 8, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samorost_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8ey2.jpg","s":"Samorost2, the sequel to free browser based game Samorost1 is a short point-and-click adventure in which you must help out a little space gnome as he searches for his dog, which has been taken away by aliens."},{"t":"Samurai Shodown VI","p":["Arcade"],"d":"SNK Playmore, Yuki Enterprise","u":"SNK Playmore, Sega","g":"Fighting game","r":"September 14, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samurai_Shodown_VI","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5u76.jpg","s":"Among other series changes, aerial blocking was removed entirely, and the switch-around move, which enabled a player to shift quickly behind the other's back, as well as the dodge (evade, side-step), in which the move virtually brings a semi-3D environment to the defense in attempt to use each sword more effectively.\n\nOne can no longer charge one's own \"pow\" gauge. The off-screen delivery man was omitted entirely from the game. The \"CD combo\" was added, wherein a player can press the C and D buttons together, triggering a strike that can be followed up by a sequence of button taps.\n\nSNK also added a \"suicide\" move, wherein one's character forfeits the round. The bonus to this is that the one committing suicide will start the next round with a full \"POW\" gauge. Certain finishes also enable a \"fatality\" move in the vein of Mortal Kombat."},{"t":"Samurai Western","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Acquire","u":"Spike, Atlus, 505 Games","g":"Action role-playing","r":"January 1, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samurai_Western","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1ozo.jpg","s":"Samurai Gojiro Kiryuu comes to the American West in search of his brother. His journey takes him to a corrupt town ruled by a sinister land baron named Goldberg. Though Gojiro isn't interested in righting wrongs, he is soon caught up in the town's problems: killing highway robbers, protecting a woman from would-be rapists, and thwarting Goldberg's machinations. Focused on destroying Gojiro, Goldberg unleashes an endless stream of minions... all fodder for Gojiro's blade. But Goldberg has an ace up his sleeve...\n\nSamurai Western is a third-person action game. Gojiro's blade is more than a match for Old West weaponry as he can ably deflect or sidestep bullets. As Gojiro completes levels, he upgrades his skills, unlocks new swords and stances, and adds Western accessories to his wardrobe. Primarily a single-player game, Samurai Western has a two player co-op mode and unlockable characters for both modes."},{"t":"Sanarara","p":["Windows"],"u":"NekoNeko Soft","g":"Eroge, Visual novel","r":"April 29, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanarara"},{"t":"Save Mary","p":["Atari 2600"],"u":"Atari","r":"August 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Save_Mary","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8wdi.jpg","s":"Save Mary is an Atari 2600 action game that revolves around creating platforms to save Mary, the damsel in distress. The character is a humble construction worker who must pick up crates to use as platforms to get Mary to climb up, eventually leading to the top of the valley. The villain of the story is a mustachioed fiend who keeps Mary at the bottom of the valley for his own perverse pleasure.\n\nThe player controls a crane at the top of the valley that moves picks up crates when the button is pressed. Bonus items can be picked up for extra points. The level can be restarted in the following ways:\n\n- The water reaches above Mary's head\n- A crate is knocked into/dropped on Mary\n- Mary is dropped from a high place.\n\nThere is no definite ending, since once all the levels are completed, the game starts over. Therefore, the game loops on into eternity. Save Mary was in production for over 2 years, longer than any other Atari 2600 game."},{"t":"SBK: Snowboard Kids","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 22"},{"t":"School Days","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/School_Days_(video_game)"},{"t":"School Rumble","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/School_Rumble"},{"t":"Scooby-Doo! Unmasked","p":["PlayStation 2","GameCube","Xbox","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS"],"r":"September 13","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scooby-Doo!_Unmasked"},{"t":"Serious Sam 2","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"g":"Action, Indie","r":"October 11","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serious_Sam_2","i":"images/steam-564310.jpg","s":"Serious Sam Fusion is a central hub for several existing Serious Sam games developed by Croteam. Cool new features, engine upgrades, patches and updates will be released to existing owners for FREE!"},{"t":"Serious Sam II","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Croteam","u":"2K Games","g":"First-person shooter","r":"October 11, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serious_Sam_II","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2r9u.jpg","s":"The iconic Serious Sam brings his trademark relentless intensity to this bigger, bolder, more colorful sequel to the classic Serious Sam: First and Second Encounters! Tasked with rescuing the universe one bullet at a time against overwhelming hordes of time traveling enemies, Serious Sam must battle through thick jungles, murky swamps, frozen tundra, and futuristic cities to bring down Mental and his vile armies. Serious Sam 2 is a shot of adrenaline to the hearts of first-person shooter fans across the world. This is serious!"},{"t":"Shadow of Rome","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"February 8","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow_of_Rome"},{"t":"Shadow of the Colossus","p":["PlayStation 2"],"u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","r":"October 18, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow_of_the_Colossus"},{"t":"Shadow the Hedgehog","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube"],"r":"November 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow_the_Hedgehog_(video_game)"},{"t":"Shadowgrounds","p":["Windows"],"d":"Frozenbyte","u":"Plan 1, Meridian4, Linux Game Publishing","g":"Top-down shooter","r":"November 17, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadowgrounds","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2ra3.jpg","s":"Shadowgrounds breathes fresh air into the action genre with explosive combat sequences, an innovative weapon upgrade system, and an intriguing storyline. The adrenaline-pumping, top-down gameplay and audiovisual fireworks set the scene for this new action experience which also includes single computer (split keyboard or joystick) co-op play."},{"t":"Shaman King: Legacy of the Spirits","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Konami Computer Entertainment Japan","u":"Konami Digital Entertainment America","g":"Role-playing","r":"February 8, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shaman_King:_Legacy_of_the_Spirits"},{"t":"Shaman King: Legacy of the Spirits, Soaring Hawk","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 8"},{"t":"Shaman King: Legacy of the Spirits, Sprinting Wolf","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 8"},{"t":"Shaman King: Master of Spirits 2","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"August 2"},{"t":"Shamu's Deep Sea Adventures","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 1","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shamu%27s_Deep_Sea_Adventures"},{"t":"Sharin no Kuni: The Girl Among the Sunflowers","p":["Windows"],"d":"Akabeisoft2","u":"Akabeisoft2, 5pb., Front Wing","g":"Visual novel","r":"November 25, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sharin_no_Kuni:_The_Girl_Among_the_Sunflowers","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co865y.jpg","s":"Early summer.\n\nA society which imposes special \"Duties\" upon everyone who breaks the law.\n\nThe individuals who oversee these criminals' rehabilitation are the \"Special Elite\"ーa rank the protagonist, Kenichi Morita, hopes to attain. To do that, he must pass his final exam, for which he arrives at a certain country town.\n\nAt the school Kenichi attends, he encounters girls bound by various “Duties.” Those obligated \"to observe a 12-hour day\" are forbidden from being awake for more than 12 hours per day, and those obligated \"to remain in infancy\" cannot grow up. It is meeting Natsumi Hinata, the girl who \"cannot fall in love,\" that throws him out of gear.\n\nSoon, Kenichi makes a series of odd discoveries… his own grave, erected secretly on a clifftop; his patrimony, hidden deep inside a cavern. Kenichi finds that he must search for his own atonement in this dystopian society. What is the truth behind the Land of the Spinning Wheel? Discover for yourself through Kenichi's eyes!"},{"t":"Shattered Union","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"d":"PopTop Software","u":"2K","g":"Turn-based tactics","r":"October 17, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shattered_Union","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co410m.jpg","s":"Following a great increase in terrorism, internal strife and ultimately, the nuclear destruction of Washington, D.C., the United States shatters into a half-dozen nation-states that descend into war. Take the helm of one of these newfound sovereignties (or the 'peacekeeping' European Expeditionary Force) and struggle to reunify America... by any means necessary!"},{"t":"Shin Megami Tensei: Digital Devil Saga","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"April 5"},{"t":"Shining Force Neo","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Neverland, Pyramid","u":"Sega","g":"Action role-playing game","r":"March 24, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shining_Force_Neo","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1p02.jpg","s":"Max completes his Force military training and returns to his village to meet his family and to find news of his missing brother. Later, the village is attacked by monsters later suspected as remnants of the Legion as well as the appearance of a mysterious figure that seems to know of his brother. This reasons compel Max to seek out the Legion threat, hoping in the process to also find his missing brother."},{"t":"Shining Tears","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"March 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shining_Tears"},{"t":"Shinobido: Way of the Ninja","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Acquire","u":"Spike, Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Stealth","r":"November 10, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shinobido:_Way_of_the_Ninja","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co490q.jpg","s":"DEEP IN THE SHADOWS A NlNJA WAlTS TO STRIKE\n\nIt is the 16th century. The once peaceful province of Utakata now lies in a state of despair. The elite ninja clan who once protected the region are all but dead and with no safeguard, Utakata‘s enemies are starting to stir. War is surely near.\n\nAs the last of the Asuka Ninja you must rise up and choose a new path. Exact revenge on those who sought to end your clan and decide upon a new fate for the land.\n\n-Use Stealth or aggression to defeat your enemies\n-Combine your equipment to form over 150 weapons and items\n-Create maps and missions and transfer them to Shinobido: Tales of the Ninja on your PSP (PlayStation Portable) (sold separately)"},{"t":"Shoot the Bullet","p":["Windows"],"d":"Team Shanghai Alice","u":"Team Shanghai Alice","g":"Shoot 'em up photography","r":"December 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoot_the_Bullet"},{"t":"Shout About Music","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shout_About_Music"},{"t":"Shrek SuperSlam","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS"],"r":"October 25","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shrek_SuperSlam"},{"t":"Sigma Star Saga","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"August 16","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sigma_Star_Saga"},{"t":"Silent Hunter III","p":["Windows"],"u":"Ubisoft","g":"Simulation","r":"March 15, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silent_Hunter_III","i":"images/steam-15210.jpg","s":"The king of submarine simulations returns with an all-new 3D engine, new crew command features, and more realistic WWII naval action than ever before. The movie-like graphics and simple, tension-filled gameplay make this the perfect game for the realism fanatic and the casual gamer."},{"t":"Silkroad Online","p":["Windows"],"d":"Joymax","u":"Yahoo! Korea, Joymax1.310","g":"MMORPG","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silkroad_Online","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8d3p.jpg","s":"Silkroad Online is a free MMORPG made by Joymax that is based on the silkroad trading routes in ancient China."},{"t":"Singles 2: Triple Trouble","p":["Windows"],"d":"Rotobee","u":"Deep Silver","g":"Social simulation","r":"June 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singles_2:_Triple_Trouble","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/dk6leggnmsms0sitsv5q.jpg"},{"t":"SingStar The Dome","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"SCEE Studio London","u":"SCEE","g":"Karaoke","r":"June 1, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SingStar_The_Dome"},{"t":"Sly 3: Honor Among Thieves","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 26"},{"t":"Smart Bomb","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Core Design","u":"Eidos Interactive","g":"Strategy, puzzle","r":"May 10, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smart_Bomb_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co72f7.jpg","s":"Smart Bomb test your skills, the puzzle game for the PSP developed by Core Design Ltd."},{"t":"Snakes","p":["N-Gage"],"d":"IOMO","u":"Nokia","g":"Arcade","r":"January 25, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snakes_(N-Gage_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6q7e.jpg","s":"The N-Gages \"Killer App\", Snakes is an upgrade to the flash legend Snake. The game can also be transferred between handhelds and stored via Blue Tooth."},{"t":"Sniper Elite","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Rebellion Developments","u":"Namco Hometek, MC2 France","g":"Tactical shooter, stealth","r":"September 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sniper_Elite_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1p0u.jpg","s":"Sniper Elite is a third-person action strategy game with a focus on sniping. The player takes on the role of an American agent working for the OSS (the organization that later became the CIA) stationed in Berlin at the end of World War II, tasked with preventing the Russian troops from getting hold of the research Germany had been conducting into nuclear weaponry. As an elite sniper, the style of play is much less run-and-gun and much more about finding good positions, lining up shots and taking out the enemy before he even knows where you are.\n\nThe single-player campaign takes place over 28 missions set in and around Berlin. Players use stealth tactics, and things like wind and background noise can be a factor when lining up shots. When a shot is performed particularly well, players are rewarded with a 'bullet cam' which follows the bullet in slow-motion from gun barrel to target."},{"t":"Snood 2: On Vacation","p":["Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS","Mobile phone"],"d":"Gravity-i Ltd","u":"Destination Software, Cybiko","g":"Puzzle","r":"October 31, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snood_2:_On_Vacation","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8ced.jpg","s":"We have arrived at Snoodville and the action is all go, go, go! Classic Snood turned sideways is a massive issue as all the snoods fall to the floor. Once they meet up with three of their own color, all the action starts to happen. Clear the board of all the snoods in time limit and other play modes. No more snoods available !! What do we do now? We fire a grappling hook to hook the snoods and pull them back to snood central! Then fire them to where we want them to be to make them fall from the board. Circular snood will also get you in a spin! Fire the snoods up to the highest levels, but watch out -- there are no straight sides to bounce off! You are in a circular tube and the snoods will bounce and fly everywhere if your angles are wrong. Just when you think you have the game beaten the whole world rotates and leaves you fighting to stay in the game!"},{"t":"SOCOM 3","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"October 11","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SOCOM_3"},{"t":"SOCOM 3 U.S. Navy SEALs","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Zipper Interactive","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Third-person shooter, tactical shooter","r":"October 11, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SOCOM_3_U.S._Navy_SEALs","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1vue.jpg","s":"The Socom series continues with a single player campaign. 32 player capability is added to the online experience. The series is still about protecting America against urban and rural warfare. Three new AOs are included in this game: Morocco, Poland, and Bangladesh. Maps are 5 to 6 times larger than the last game. Multiple save points have been included. Vehicles can be driven by players and AI. The new weapon customization allows 30 different weapons and attachments. The new TCA system allows the player to quickly give a command."},{"t":"SOCOM U.S. Navy SEALs: Fireteam Bravo","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"November 8"},{"t":"Software Tycoon","p":["Linux"],"r":"January 10"},{"t":"Sonic Gems Collection","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Sonic Team","u":"Sega","g":"Various","r":"August 11, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonic_Gems_Collection"},{"t":"Sonic Jump","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Sonic Team, AirPlay, Hardlight","u":"Sega","g":"Platform","r":"February 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonic_Jump","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9jse.jpg","s":"The original version of Sonic Jump. It the game, you control Sonic jumping while avoiding enemies and obstacles. It has a remake with the same name for smartphones."},{"t":"Sonic Rush","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonic_Rush"},{"t":"Soul Calibur III","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"October 25","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soul_Calibur_III"},{"t":"Soul Ride","p":["Linux"],"r":"June 24"},{"t":"Space Battleship Yamato: Nijū Ginga no Hōkai","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Bandai","u":"Bandai","g":"Action","r":"July 4, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Battleship_Yamato:_Nij%C5%AB_Ginga_no_H%C5%8Dkai"},{"t":"Space Invaders Evolution","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Invaders_Evolution"},{"t":"Space Invaders Pocket","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Invaders_Pocket"},{"t":"Space Invaders Revolution","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"September 20","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Space_Invaders_video_games#Space_Invaders_Revolution"},{"t":"Space Invaders X Pac-Man","p":["Mobile phone"],"g":"Arcade","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Space_Invaders_X_Pac-Man","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cocmox.jpg","s":"Space Invaders x Pac-Man was an limited-time action game available on the i-mode platform. This game showcases a collaboration between Namco's Pac-Man and Taito's Space Invaders characters. This game was available for a limited time from September 1st to October 31st, 2005."},{"t":"Spartan: Total Warrior","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Creative Assembly","u":"Sega","g":"Hack and slash","r":"October 7, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spartan:_Total_Warrior","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1pej.jpg","s":"An action game spin-off in the Total Warrior series. Play as a mighty Spartan trooper, and battle through hordes of enemies in large environments, while working with allies. Use ultra-violent special attacks to mow down entire groups of foes at once, with ridiculously bloody effect.\n\nThe game has a fast-paced, arcade-like, mission-based gameplay. In each mission, you must succeed in minor goals like killing the generals of the opposition, escorting sappers to blow up enemy siege weaponry and preventing the enemy from making to behind your borders. The storyline progresses through cutscenes, shown in-between each mission.\n\nDepending on how you succeed in your mission, you get \"tokens\", which you can use to upgrade the health, damage or power of your character. The player is capable of doing special moves, which can be learned throughout the game. Some of the special moves gain their powers through the spartan gods, that aid the player in his battle. During the game, you can find different weapons like swords, bows and spears, and of course, shields."},{"t":"Spider-Man 2","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"March 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spider-Man_2_(2004_video_game)"},{"t":"Spikeout: Battle Street","p":["Xbox"],"r":"March 29"},{"t":"Splat Magazine Renegade Paintball","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Cat Daddy Games","u":"Global Star Software","g":"First-person shooter","r":"October 11, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Splat_Magazine_Renegade_Paintball","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/kzcw4metgrf66lmufung.jpg","s":"Splat Magazine Renegade Paintball challenges players with over 25 white-knuckle single player Tournament and Fieldball matches. For those who want more than single player competition, the game offers online multiplayer action via Xbox Live and System Link as well as Two Player Split Screen, and Internet and LAN play for PC."},{"t":"SpongeBob SquarePants: Lights, Camera, Pants!","p":["Xbox","PlayStation 2","GameCube","Game Boy Advance","Windows"],"d":"THQ Studio Australia, WayForward Technologies, AWE Games","u":"THQ","g":"Party","r":"October 19, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SpongeBob_SquarePants:_Lights,_Camera,_Pants!","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6stu.jpg","s":"SpongeBob SquarePants: Lights!, Camera!, Pants!, the city of Bikini Bottom is producing a show called \"The Adventures of Mermaid Man & Barnacle Boy\" in which the titular SpongeBob wishes to play as the starring role. SpongeBob must compete with the other characters in the series – including Patrick Star, Sandy Cheeks, Squidward Tentacles, Mr. Krabs and Sheldon J. Plankton – in order to impress the talent scouts and land the lead role of the villain."},{"t":"SpongeBob SquarePants: Lights, Cameras, Pants!","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"October 21"},{"t":"Spy vs. Spy","p":["Xbox","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Vicious Cycle Software","u":"Global Star Software","g":"Platform","r":"April 7, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spy_vs._Spy_(2005_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4vdz.jpg","s":"The black Spy and the white Spy are out to beat each other before the time bell rings. Find the needed objects by digging through drawers, closets and furniture in the house. Foil your opponent by setting creative booby traps in the various rooms (a bomb in a dresser drawer, for instance).\n\nFights ensue when both spies enter the same room. Find hidden weapons in the rooms to help with those fights, since one of you will die if you run into each other."},{"t":"Spyro: Shadow Legacy","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"October 18"},{"t":"SpyToy","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"London Studio","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Action","r":"October 14, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SpyToy","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4sn8.jpg","s":"Use the EyeToy camera to play out the role of a spy. Mission include stealthy sky diving, code breaking, face matching, and more.\n\nThe main objective of the game is to guard a room from an intruder. Unique features include new face recognition technology, new video messaging, and interactive missions. If an intruder is caught, the next time the player returns to the room they can watch the recorded video of who came in. The concept for EyeToy: Operation Spy was derived from a game within EyeToy: Play 2, which also had similar security features."},{"t":"SSX on Tour","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","PlayStation Portable"],"r":"October 11","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SSX_on_Tour"},{"t":"SSX Out of Bounds","p":["N-Gage","Gizmondo"],"d":"EA Sports Big","u":"Nokia, Gizmondo Games","g":"Snowboarding","r":"January 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SSX_Out_of_Bounds"},{"t":"Stalingrad","p":["Windows"],"d":"DTF Games","u":"BlackBean Games, 1C Games","g":"Real-time tactics","r":"March 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stalingrad_(2005_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co90kq.jpg","s":"Stalingrad is a real-time strategy title that places gamers in the middle of the most dramatic periods of World War II, covering major events from June 1942 till January 1943. Built-up upon the enhanced Enigma Engine, the game offers faithful historical recreation of the Stalingrad area, vast tactical options and more than 150 units at your command."},{"t":"Star Fox Assault","p":["GameCube"],"r":"February 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Fox_Assault"},{"t":"Star Heritage 1: The Black Cobra","p":["Windows"],"g":"Adventure","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Heritage_1:_The_Black_Cobra","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coc9eo.jpg"},{"t":"Star Wars Battlefront 2","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox","PlayStation Portable"],"r":"November 1"},{"t":"Star Wars Episode III: Revenge of the Sith","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS","Mobile phone"],"r":"May 5"},{"t":"Star Wars: Battlefront II","p":["PlayStation 2","PlayStation Portable","Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Pandemic Studios","u":"LucasArts","g":"Action, third-person shooter, first-person shooter","r":"October 28, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_Wars:_Battlefront_II_(2005_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cob1g4.jpg","s":"Star Wars: Battlefront II is the sequel to Star Wars: Battlefront. It is a high-selling Star Wars video game following the many adventures of several characters. The two games are very similar, as both revolve around troopers from various factions fighting in different locales. Battlefront II, however, includes elements and missions from Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith, as well as enhanced aspects of gameplay including space combat and the ability to play as Jedi characters or other heroes.\n\nWith brand new space combat, playable Jedi characters, and over 16 all new battlefronts, Star Wars Battlefront II gives you more ways than ever before to play the classic Star Wars battles any way you want."},{"t":"Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic II The Sith Lords","p":["Windows"],"g":"RPG","r":"February 8","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/208580","i":"images/steam-208580.jpg","s":"5 years after the events of the award winning original, the Sith are on the verge of crushing the Old Republic. As a lone Jedi, will you follow the light side or succumb to the dark?"},{"t":"Star Wars: Republic Commando","p":["Xbox","Windows"],"g":"Action","r":"February 28","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/6000","i":"images/steam-6000.jpg","s":"You are the leader of an elite squad of Republic Commandos, your mission is to infiltrate, dominate, and ultimately, annihilate the enemy. Your squad will follow your orders and your lead, working together as a team - instinctively, intelligently, instantly. You are their leader. They are your weapon."},{"t":"Starry Sky","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starry_Sky"},{"t":"Starship Troopers","p":["Windows"],"d":"Strangelite","u":"Empire Interactive, Destineer","g":"First-person shooter","r":"October 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starship_Troopers_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3gx0.jpg","s":"Would you like to know more? Jump into epic battles featuring over 300 bugs on the screen at once, each with their own AI -- 19 different types of bugs to encounter\nChoose from 9 futuristic weapons, each with dual function attacks - From the standard-issue Morita rifle (as seen in the film) and shotgun to the plasma rifle and nuke launcher\n12 single player levels with real-time battles and solo infiltration missions\nVaried combat environments - indoor and outdoor levels, including the wide-open battlefields, a secret laboratory, claustrophobic bug nests, abandoned mines and lonely outposts\nLAN and online modes, including death match and co-op missions"},{"t":"Sticky Balls","p":["Gizmondo"],"d":"Gizmondo Studios Manchester","u":"Gizmondo Studios","g":"Puzzle","r":"May 24, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sticky_Balls","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7yty.jpg","s":"Sticky Balls is an action puzzle game published by Gizmondo Studios and developed in Manchester and designed by John and Ste Pickford. Sticky Balls uses a pool-like interface where the player utilizes a spring-loaded rod to shoot brightly colored balls at each other. Bouncing the balls against the table walls doubles the score of the shot but hitting a ball of a different color, or failing to hit anything causes the player to lose a turn."},{"t":"Still Life","p":["Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Microids Canada","u":"MC2, The Adventure Company","g":"Adventure","r":"April 14, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Still_Life_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co222h.jpg","s":"Two separate murder cases, in two separate lifetimes - so similar in the smallest of details that one could believe they were performed by the same person. Impossible! One of the crimes took place 75 years ago, while the other just happened! Is someone copying an old serial killer? Or is it remotely possible that the same murderer is still alive and committing more crimes?\n\nIn this thriller adventure, you'll play as Victoria, an FBI agent, in modern Chicago as well as her grandfather, Gustav, P.I. in Prague in the 1920s. Explore Chicago and Prague and solve puzzles while preforming investigations in two time periods."},{"t":"Stolen","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Blue52","u":"Hip Games","g":"Stealth, platform","r":"April 1, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stolen_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coc3z6.jpg","s":"Stolen is a third-person stealth action game in which you play as a female thief. After your everyday job turns sour, you enter a web of conspiracy that threatens to destroy the entire city. With your stealth and agility, you'll break into and out of various locations (including museums, prisons, and satellite arrays) in an effort to steal priceless items. You'll have access to different high-tech gadgets and tools that will help you achieve your objectives."},{"t":"Strawberry Marshmallow","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strawberry_Marshmallow"},{"t":"Street Fighter III: 3rd Strike","p":["Xbox"],"r":"February 22"},{"t":"Street Racing Syndicate","p":["Windows","Game Boy Advance"],"g":"Racing","r":"January 18","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Street_Racing_Syndicate","i":"images/steam-292410.jpg","s":"The raw, high-stakes world of illegal street racing comes to life in Street Racing Syndicate. Trick out over 40 authentic licensed cars with parts from over 15 real-world manufacturers, then turn your customized ride loose on the streets of 3 cities across the USA."},{"t":"Street Supremacy","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Genki","u":"Genki, Konami","g":"Racing","r":"April 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Street_Supremacy","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coahb6.jpg","s":"Unlike other Shutokou Battle series titles, the objective of Street Supremacy is to join a team, level up to become the team leader, recruit other rivals to join your team, and to take control of the various highways in Tokyo.\n\nThe map area consists of the areas featured in Tokyo Xtreme Racer 3, including the C1 Loop, Shinkanjou, Wangan Line, Yokohane, and Yokohama routes. Each route is broken up into several zones, which are controlled by the rival teams.\n\nRival teams in Street Supremacy include Rolling Guy, Fine Drive, Galaxy Racers, The Road of Justice, Departures, No Loser, Highway Outlaw, Free Way, Another Star, Unlimited, Neo Limited, Speed Masters R, and Wanderers (much like other Shutokou Battle titles, Wanderers have certain requirements that need to be met before challenging the player). Some bosses from the other titles appear in Street Supremacy as Wanderers by default. Street Supremacy is the only Shutokou Battle series title where rivals can change teams during the game and teams can disband during the game."},{"t":"Stronghold 2","p":["Windows"],"d":"Firefly Studios","u":"2K, Firefly Studios","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"April 19, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stronghold_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7nr5.jpg","s":"Tax, torture or treat your peasants! Rehabilitate criminals or sentence them to death? Decide as you joust over a lavish banquet, all while under siege from the warmongering Lord Barclay. Will you entertain with medieval tournaments or rule with an iron fist and dispense feudal justice to overworked and malnourished peasants? With powerful barons jostling for power over a disintegrating kingdom, it is up to you to stem the tides of ambition and unite the land under the one true King!\n\nBuilding on the sim gameplay of the original Stronghold, Stronghold 2 allows players to rule as they please and still conquer each skirmish. Unhappy peasants turn to crime and must be punished, rival lords can raise entire armies on their title alone and sieges must be fought tooth and nail, with close combat taking place inside castle structures. Stronghold 2 Online extends this gameplay to competitive multiplayer for up to eight players, with offline skirmish mode also available against computer-controller opponents.\n\nThe online services used GameSpy which was shutdown. The Steam Edition is the only version of Stronghold 2 that still features multiplayer using Steam Multiplayer."},{"t":"Stubbs the Zombie in Rebel Without a Pulse","p":["Xbox"],"r":"October 18","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stubbs_the_Zombie_in_Rebel_Without_a_Pulse"},{"t":"Sudden Attack","p":["Windows"],"d":"Nexon GT","u":"Nexon","g":"First-person shooter","r":"April 11, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudden_Attack","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2hvp.jpg","s":"Sudden Attack is a fast paced game with speed and user battlefield And that seems to provide tension. In addition, the ease of operation and user-friendly Interface that you can enjoy the FPS for Everyone Pursued."},{"t":"Sudeki","p":["Windows"],"g":"Action, Adventure, RPG","r":"March 25","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudeki","i":"images/steam-233350.jpg","s":"Sudeki, a world torn apart into light, shadow and dark. Rent asunder by deceit and betrayal, the land cries out for a peace that only four united heroes can bring. Beyond the protective walls of Illumina Castle lie miles of pastoral, rolling countryside, though once a serene landscape, the Aklorian forces have transformed the countryside..."},{"t":"Suikoden Tactics","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"November 8","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suikoden_Tactics"},{"t":"Summer","p":["Windows"],"g":"Adventure, Visual Novel","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summer_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/iil8k4ninecy495jqzse.jpg","s":"A visual novel from Hooksoft."},{"t":"Summon Night Swordcraft Story 3: Stone of Beginnings","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Flight-Plan","u":"Banpresto","g":"Action role-playing game","r":"December 8, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summon_Night_Swordcraft_Story_3:_Stone_of_Beginnings","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2wje.jpg","s":"Summon Night Craft Sword Monogatari: Hajimari no Ishi is a Role-Playing game, developed by Flight-Plan and published by Banpresto, which was released in Japan in 2005."},{"t":"Super Army War","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 23","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Army_War"},{"t":"Super Columbine Massacre RPG!","p":["Windows"],"g":"Role-playing","r":"April 20, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Columbine_Massacre_RPG!","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3lyw.jpg","s":"Super Columbine Massacre RPG! is a role-playing video game created by Danny Ledonne and released in April 2005. The game recreates the 1999 Columbine High School shootings near Littleton, Colorado. Players assume the roles of gunmen Eric Harris and Dylan Klebold and act out the massacre, with flashbacks relating parts of Harris and Klebold's past experiences. The game begins on the day of the shootings and follows Harris and Klebold after their suicides to fictional adventures in perdition."},{"t":"Super Mario Strikers","p":["GameCube"],"r":"December 5","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Mario_Strikers"},{"t":"Super Monkey Ball Deluxe","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"March 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Monkey_Ball_Deluxe"},{"t":"Super Princess Peach","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"Tose","u":"Nintendo","g":"Platform","r":"October 20, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Princess_Peach","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1wsg.jpg","s":"Princess Power!\nBowser's up to no good again...but this time, it's Princess Peach to the rescue! When Mario, Luigi, and the Mushroom Castle Toads get kidnapped it's up to Peach and her magical umbrella to save them."},{"t":"Super Robot Wars J","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"A.I","u":"Banpresto","g":"Tactical role-playing game","r":"September 15, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Robot_Wars_J","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4ykv.jpg","s":"Super Robot Taisen J is a tactical role-playing video game released for the Game Boy Advance by Banpresto."},{"t":"Super Robot Wars OG 2","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Banpresoft","u":"Banpresto, Atlus, 505 Games","g":"Tactical role-playing","r":"February 3, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Robot_Wars_OG_2"},{"t":"Supreme Ruler 2010","p":["Windows"],"d":"BattleGoat Studios","u":"Strategy First, Black Bean Games","g":"Strategy","r":"May 10, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Ruler_2010","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/sz5unumwqq6ulawqfh6m.jpg","s":"Supreme Ruler 2010 was the first PC title from BattleGoat Studios launching their critically acclaimed Supreme Ruler series."},{"t":"Surviving High School","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Centerscore, EA Mobile","g":"Interactive fiction","r":"April 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surviving_High_School","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/flmre3pgck3xwtzstvzt.jpg","s":"Experience high school drama at Centerscore High in this text-based game."},{"t":"SWAT 4","p":["Windows"],"r":"April 5","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SWAT_4"},{"t":"Swords and Sandals","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swords_and_Sandals"},{"t":"System Rush","p":["N-Gage"],"d":"Ideaworks Game Studio","u":"Nokia","g":"racing game","r":"September 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/System_Rush","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co63gj.jpg","s":"Futuristic racing game on the N-Gage."},{"t":"Tabloid Tycoon","p":["Windows"],"d":"Black Lantern Studios","u":"ValuSoft, Global Software Publishing","g":"Business simulation","r":"April 25, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tabloid_Tycoon","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cobkpt.jpg","s":"In Tabloid Tycoon you become the head of a newspaper company. You must manage staff and budget to create a successful newspaper empire. The game simulates different weekly aspects of running a newspaper company including finding leads, putting photographers and reporters on a job, planning sabotage on rivals, settling lawsuits and making stories. Along the way you can encounter special shortcuts, win awards, buy things from vehicles to gadgets to improve your paper. With more money, prestige and public praise you can make your newspaper bigger and upgrade your facilities.\n\nThe news stories can range from funny, weird, to plain bizarre and can be randomly generated and edited. The game also comes with a custom story editor to make your own stories with custom photos. You can save your newspapers to html. Modes of gameplay include scenarios, enterprise, and freeplay."},{"t":"Taito Legends","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Empire Interactive","u":"Empire Interactive, Sega","g":"Various","r":"October 14, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taito_Legends"},{"t":"Tak: The Great Juju Challenge","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS","PlayStation Portable"],"r":"September 19"},{"t":"Tales of Mobile","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tales_of_Mobile"},{"t":"Tales of the World: Narikiri Dungeon 3","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Alfa System","u":"Namco","g":"Tactical RPG","r":"January 6, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tales_of_the_World:_Narikiri_Dungeon_3","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6sw5.jpg","s":"The third in the \"Narikiri Dungeon\" series of Namco's \"Tales of\" franchise. It includes a number of crossovers with previous Tales games, including Tales of Symphonia and and Tales of Eternia."},{"t":"Talkman","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Sony Computer Entertainment Japan","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Edutainment","r":"November 17, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talkman","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2rjh.jpg","s":"Thanks to TalkMan - and a large blue multilingual bird called Max PSP (PlayStationPortable) is on a mission to break the ice and tear down those barriers that keep nationalities apart. Bring the art of language to your gestures, put words behind the shrugs, turn Spanglish into perfecto Espanol, make the move on the girl or guy in that foreign bar who catches your eye - in short, become a jetsetter able to communicate in six languages with more than 3000 crucial phrases at your fingertips.\n\nFollowing the recent success of the Asian version in Japan and Korea, Talkman is coming to Europe and Australasia this spring on PSP, courtesy of Sony Computer Entertainment Europe. TalkMan is the portable language entertainment tool and interactive phrasebook that makes sure you are ready to talk - wherever you are and comes packed with the phrases that count in six languages: French; English; German; Spanish; Italian and, of course, Japanese"},{"t":"Tears to Tiara","p":["Windows"],"g":"Role-playing (RPG), Strategy, Tactical, Visual Novel","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tears_to_Tiara","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cob5ds.jpg","s":"Tears to Tiara is a Japanese adult tactical role-playing game."},{"t":"Tecmo Classic Arcade","p":["Xbox"],"r":"September 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tecmo_Classic_Arcade"},{"t":"Teen Titans","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 16","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teen_Titans_(GBA_game)"},{"t":"Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles 3: Mutant Nightmare","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Nintendo DS"],"d":"Konami Computer Entertainment Studios","u":"Konami Digital Entertainment","g":"Action","r":"November 1, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teenage_Mutant_Ninja_Turtles_3:_Mutant_Nightmare","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2deu.jpg","s":"TMNT3 puts more of a focus on teamwork, character development and control than any other console Turtles game to date. Gamers can play as their favorite Turtle alone or with up to three friends, earning experience points along the way as they slash and bash Foot Ninjas and powerful, well-known bosses from the TMNT universe. These experience points allow players to improve and evolve their Turtles' traits and abilities for more varied, powerful attacks and moves. The Ninja Scroll System is another new feature on TMMT3. Being able to select which ninja scrolls to use allows the Turtles to use various special abilities strategically. Cooperative play lies at the heart of TMNT3 and gamers who team up with friends for multiplayer action are rewarded with exclusive features such as Cooperative Attack for even more shell shocking damage to enemies. The effect of this attack changes depending on the number of players working together (between 2-4 players). For even greater control, TMNT3 features a new combat system called the Target Attack system that lets gamers play more instinctively and strategically. With the Target Attack system, players will be able to lock onto specific enemies and block, dodge or counter attack accordingly for smoother and more maneuverable combat. Story Mode can be played with 1-4 players. Even when you have less than 4 players to play, the other Turtles will be at your side, controlled through AI. All the Turtles can participate in Cooperative Attack to beat enemies and players can give commands to the AI."},{"t":"Tekken 5","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"February 24","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tekken_5"},{"t":"Telltale Texas Hold'em","p":["Windows"],"d":"Telltale Games","u":"Telltale Games","g":"Card game","r":"February 11, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telltale_Texas_Hold'em","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1riv.jpg","s":"Join poker's most outspoken players for a hand of Telltale Texas Hold'em, the card game stacked high with personality. Quips will fly, chips will fall, and you may just end up rolling in the aisles."},{"t":"Tenchu: Time of the Assassins","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"d":"K2","u":"FromSoftware, Sega","g":"Action-adventure, stealth","r":"July 28, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tenchu:_Time_of_the_Assassins","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2nzx.jpg","s":"The Assassins are back...\nTenchu: Time of the Assassins sees the return of Rikimaru, Ayame, Rin and Tesshu in their most impressive Ninja adventure to date.\n\n-Create new storylines with scenario mode\n-Create and share your own missions\n-Play story mode or any of 50 standalone missions"},{"t":"Tennis Titans","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"Skunk Studios","u":"Skunk Studios","g":"Sports","r":"March 16, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tennis_Titans","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/npmlfmqf9aggxefzd4lw.jpg","s":"Hit the courts for some rowdy tennis fun with seven flavorful tennis characters! Featuring simple, easy-to-learn hitting and aiming, Tennis Titans brings together a crazy crew of colorful cartoon characters who all want the same thing - to be Court Champion. Plus, two great game modes means there's more ways to win! Charming, delightful, and beautifully rendered, Tennis Titans is a challenging treat for the entire family."},{"t":"The 25th Ward: The Silver Case","p":["Mobile phone"],"d":"Grasshopper Manufacture","u":"Genki, Liveware, Nippon Ichi Software, NIS America","g":"Adventure","r":"October 3, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_25th_Ward:_The_Silver_Case"},{"t":"The Adventures of El Ballo","p":["macOS"],"d":"ProRattaFactor","u":"Ambrosia Software","g":"Platform","r":"September 19, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Adventures_of_El_Ballo","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2yfv.jpg","s":"The Adventures of El Ballo is a 2D side-scrolling platform game for Mac OS 9 and X released by Ambrosia Software on September 19, 2005."},{"t":"The Bible Game","p":["Game Boy Advance","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Mass Media, Alpine Studios","u":"Crave Entertainment, 505 GameStreet","g":"Christian, party","r":"October 18, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Bible_Game","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5rp8.jpg","s":"The Bible Game is a Christian-themed party and trivia game for PlayStation 2 and Xbox. The console version is structured around a game show format, with players answering Old Testament trivia questions and competing in short mini-games based on biblical stories. It supports up to four players and includes separate modes for the main game show and individual challenge games. The Game Boy Advance version is different, using an isometric adventure format rather than the console version’s party-game structure."},{"t":"The Chronicles Of Narnia: The Lion, The Witch and The Wardrobe","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube","Nintendo DS","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 14"},{"t":"The Con","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"October 18","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Con_(video_game)"},{"t":"The Endless Forest","p":["Windows"],"r":"December 9","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Endless_Forest"},{"t":"The Fairly Oddparents! Clash with the Anti-World","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"October 18"},{"t":"The Getaway: Black Monday","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"January 11"},{"t":"The Hidden","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Hidden_(video_game)"},{"t":"The House of the Dead 4","p":["Arcade","PlayStation 3"],"d":"Sega AM1, Sega Shanghai Studio","u":"Sega","g":"Rail shooter, light gun shooter, horror game","r":"July 2, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_House_of_the_Dead_4","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2iti.jpg","s":"The House of the Dead 4 is a light gun arcade game with a horror theme and the fourth installment of the House of the Dead series of video games, developed by Sega. The game takes place between the events of The House of the Dead 2 and The House of the Dead III, and introduced several new gameplay concepts. Players can control characters James Taylor, from The House of the Dead 2, or Kate Green, a new character to the series.\n\nThe House of the Dead 4 is the first game to run on the Sega Lindbergh arcade system board. A PlayStation 3 version featuring support for PlayStation Move and the two stages from The House of the Dead 4 Special was released on April 17, 2012 on the PlayStation Network."},{"t":"The Idolmaster","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Metro","u":"Namco, Namco Bandai Games","g":"Raising simulation, Rhythm","r":"July 26, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Idolmaster_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7ksr.jpg","s":"The Idolmaster is a popular Japanese rhythm and simulation game that focuses on the management and training of virtual pop idols. Developed by Namco (later Bandai Namco Entertainment), the game places players in the role of a producer working with a talent agency to nurture and guide aspiring idols towards stardom, and the first title in the 1st Vision era.\nIt was released as the second installment of the \"Rewritable Stage\" touchscreen cabinet."},{"t":"The Incredible Hulk: Ultimate Destruction","p":["PlayStation 2","GameCube","Xbox"],"r":"August 23"},{"t":"The Incredibles: Rise of the Underminer","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube","Nintendo DS","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 1"},{"t":"The King of Fighters XI","p":["Arcade"],"d":"SNK Playmore, G1M2","u":"Sega, SNK Playmore, Ignition Entertainment","g":"Fighting","r":"October 26, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_King_of_Fighters_XI","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1p2o.jpg","s":"The eleventh game in the KOF series following The King of Fighters 2003.\nAccording to Sega: 'For over 10 years, the King of Fighters series has been the choice of game players around the world. The 11th team of fighters continues this tradition. KOF11 is suited for one to two players, with continuous buy-in. Choose from 33 fighters, including 4 new characters. A fifth control button was added to enhance your skills by delivering a devastating blow to your opponent, if hit at the right time. A New Skill Gauge performs a variety of tag-off moves and new attacks. A player can also custom construct a Three-Fighter Tag-Team by selecting three choice combatants.'"},{"t":"The Legend of Zelda: The Minish Cap","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"January 10"},{"t":"The Lord of the Rings: Tactics","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"November 8"},{"t":"The Matrix Online","p":["Windows"],"r":"March 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Matrix_Online"},{"t":"The Matrix: Path of Neo","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"November 7"},{"t":"The Movies","p":["Windows"],"g":"Video Production","r":"November 8","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Movies_(video_game)","i":"images/steam-922540.jpg","s":"The largest collection of categorized and rated 360°/ VR movies on the internet."},{"t":"The Nightmare Before Christmas: Oogie's Revenge","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"October 10"},{"t":"The Nightmare Before Christmas: The Pumpkin King","p":["Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS"],"r":"October 10"},{"t":"The Proud Family","p":["Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 13","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Proud_Family"},{"t":"The Punisher","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"January 16","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Punisher_(2005_video_game)"},{"t":"The Rumble Fish 2","p":["Arcade"],"d":"Dimps","u":"Sammy","g":"Fighting","r":"March 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Rumble_Fish_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4zii.jpg","s":"The Rumble Fish 2 is a sequel to Dimps' 2004 fighting game, The Rumble Fish. After developing many licensed fighters, The Rumble Fish series was Dimps' first real foray into a 2D competitive fighter which paved the way for their eventual hand in Street Fighter IV & V's development. The game has never seen an official console release and was originally only available on Atomiswave hardware, but in 2012 an updated version was released on the NesicaxLive distribution system in arcades. In November 2020 the Atomiswave version was unofficially ported to the Dreamcast by yzb, allowing players to play the game on physical hardware without having to acquire an actual arcade board.\n\nThe game features unique vector animations, many complex and engaging system mechanics, and a strong cast of characters with varied and interesting playstyles. Combined with its open-ended chain combo system, The Rumble Fish 2 a fun game to pick up and learn but has enough intricacies to entice those looking for something deeper."},{"t":"The Sims 2","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"December 7","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sims_2"},{"t":"The Sims 2: Nightlife","p":["Windows"],"d":"Maxis","u":"Electronic Arts, Aspyr Media","g":"Social simulation","r":"September 15, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sims_2:_Nightlife"},{"t":"The Sims 2: University","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"Maxis","u":"Electronic Arts, Aspyr Media","g":"Social simulation","r":"March 1, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sims_2:_University"},{"t":"The Stalin Subway","p":["Windows"],"d":"G5 Software","u":"Buka Entertainment","g":"First-person shooter","r":"September 29, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Stalin_Subway","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2gia.jpg","s":"\"The Stalin Subway\" is a First Person Shooter-style game where the events take place in post-war Moscow. The game allows to plunge into the depressing atmosphere of the Stalin's period and to play as a Soviet officer."},{"t":"The Suffering: Ties That Bind","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Surreal Software","u":"Midway Games","g":"First-person shooter, third-person shooter, survival horror","r":"September 26, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Suffering:_Ties_That_Bind","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4pwh.jpg","s":"The Suffering: Ties That Bind follows in the footsteps of its predecessor by combining a disturbing horror atmosphere with action/shooter gameplay. Players can switch between third person and first person depending on their preference, and will shoot a lot of hideous demonic manifestations of evil before the game is done. The player is also able to transform into a hideous creature at key times in the game, which allows him to engage in intense melee combat. The game includes a morality system which records the player's actions during gameplay and changes the story accordingly, and also alters the player's creature form. Everything from the first The Suffering has been refined and turned up a notch for the sequel."},{"t":"The Sword of Etheria","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Konami Computer Entertainment Tokyo","u":"Konami","g":"Action role-playing, hack and slash","r":"June 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sword_of_Etheria","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4pte.jpg","s":"The Sword of Etheria is an action, hack and slash and role-playing video game developed and published by Konami Computer Entertainment Tokyo.\n\nSet in an alternate world; humans, gods, and spiritual beings known as \"Katenas\" coexist. Katenas are powerful warriors with the ability to encase themselves in full suits of armor called \"Lexes\". The Katenas are the envoys of the gods. The three great Katenas, chosen by the gods, are collectively referred to as \"Oz\".\n\nBoth humans and Katenas are overseen by the gods. As in Greek mythology, the gods are described as omnipotent, ambitious, self-serving, and power-hungry. The major source of their power is light; as they consume light, they cast parts of the world into darkness for centuries. The gods seek to destroy humanity and drain the planet's energy source, \"Etheria\"."},{"t":"The Three Musketeers","p":["Windows"],"d":"Legendo Entertainment","u":"Legendo Entertainment","g":"Platform","r":"November 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Three_Musketeers_(2006_video_game)"},{"t":"The Tower SP","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"d":"Vivarium","u":"Nintendo, Sega","g":"Construction and Management Simulation","r":"April 28, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Tower_SP","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cobxkz.jpg","s":"Based on a hit PC game, players manage a tower and all tenants who reside within. Your goal is to make your tenants happy, collect greater investment funds and expand your tower upwards. This isn't as easy as it seems, as you have to keep your tenants' stress level down or they'll take flight and leave you with vacancies and unpaid dept. As the building manager, you have lots of responsibilities. You have to make sure elevator access is smooth, perhaps making use of more funds to install new elevators. You even have to clean the toilets by pressing the A button real fast. Listening to your tenant's opinions is also important, and the game offers a quick way of viewing complaints and comments from your tenants in real time."},{"t":"The Warriors","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"October 17","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Warriors_(video_game)"},{"t":"The White Chamber","p":["Windows"],"d":"Studio Trophis","g":"Adventure","r":"March 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_White_Chamber","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5zc0.jpg","s":"White Chamber is an anime-style space-horror downloadable adventure game available for free. It contains multiple endings."},{"t":"Tick! Tack!","p":["Windows"],"d":"Navel","u":"Navel, MangaGamer","g":"Visual novel, Eroge","r":"October 16, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tick!_Tack!"},{"t":"Tiger Woods PGA Tour 06","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"September 26","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger_Woods_PGA_Tour_06"},{"t":"TimeSplitters: Future Perfect","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"March 21"},{"t":"TMNT: Mutant Melee","p":["GameCube","Windows","Xbox","PlayStation 2"],"d":"Konami Computer Entertainment Hawaii","u":"Konami","g":"Fighting","r":"March 15, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TMNT:_Mutant_Melee","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2z46.jpg","s":"Run with the Turtles as they trash, smash and bash their way to victory in the ultimate 4 player Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles action game!\n\n-Over 20 playable characters\n-Unpredictable obstacles around every corner\n-Melee and Adventure Mode\n-A wide range of mini games including Last Man Standing, King of the Hill and more!"},{"t":"Togainu no Chi","p":["Windows"],"g":"Visual Novel","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Togainu_no_Chi","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9s75.jpg","s":"Togainu no Chi is a Japanese BL visual novel. Can you help Akira, numb from a lifetime of violence and isolation, forge the bonds he needs to survive a ruined Tokyo's deadly underworld?"},{"t":"Tokobot","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"December 5","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokobot"},{"t":"Tokyo Xtreme Racer: Drift 2","p":["PlayStation 2"],"u":"Genki, Konami, Crave Entertainment","g":"Racing","r":"July 28, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokyo_Xtreme_Racer:_Drift_2"},{"t":"Tom Clancy's Ghost Recon 2: Summit Strike","p":["Xbox"],"r":"August 3"},{"t":"Tom Clancy's Rainbow Six 3: Iron Wrath","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom_Clancy's_Rainbow_Six_3:_Iron_Wrath"},{"t":"Tom Clancy's Rainbow Six: Lockdown","p":["GameCube"],"r":"September 27"},{"t":"Tom Clancy's Splinter Cell: Chaos Theory","p":["Xbox","Windows","PlayStation 2","GameCube"],"u":"Ubisoft","g":"Action","r":"March 28, 2005","l":"https://store.steampowered.com/app/13570","i":"images/steam-13570.jpg","s":"Experience one of the most critically acclaimed stealth-action games of all time. Uncover a conspiracy that hits close to home and stop World War III."},{"t":"Tomoyo After: It's a Wonderful Life","p":["Windows"],"d":"Key","u":"Visual Arts, Prototype","g":"Eroge, visual novel","r":"November 25, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomoyo_After:_It's_a_Wonderful_Life","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cobt8i.jpg","s":"Tomoyo After: It's a Wonderful Life is a Japanese adult visual novel developed by Key. Key later released versions of Tomoyo After without the erotic content. The story follows the lives of Tomoya Okazaki, a young man who recently graduated from high school, and his close friend Tomoyo Sakagami as they start to see more of each other in a romantic relationship."},{"t":"Tony Hawk's American Sk8land","p":["Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS"],"d":"Vicarious Visions","u":"Activision","g":"Sports","r":"October 18, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tony_Hawk's_American_Sk8land","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2hg8.jpg","s":"Tony Hawk's American Sk8land is the handheld version of American Wasteland, the seventh entry in the Tony Hawk's series. It is the first entry in the series for the Nintendo DS.\n\nAmerican Sk8land uses cel shaded visuals and it was developed by Vicarious Visions, the developer of the Game Boy Advance Tony Hawk games. The game is based on its console counterpart, American Wasteland, featuring the same soundtrack, many of the same environments, characters.\n\nThe top screen is used to display the main gameplay, while the touch screen displays an overhead map of the area the player is currently skating, as well as icons for easily performing tricks. The touch screen is also used to create Skateboard art. Furthering the use of the DS's functions is the ability to record, with the DS microphone, your own sound clips for use in the game.\n\nAmerican Sk8land was the first Nintendo DS game released by a third party to support the Nintendo Wi-Fi Connection, the online service for the Nintendo DS. Players are able to play Trick Attack, Score Challenge, Combo Mambo and The Price is Wrong. Players are also able to upload or download graffiti, board art, highscores, and replays to one of the servers, and can periodically download new goals to complete."},{"t":"Tony Hawk's American Wasteland","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Xbox 360","Mobile phone"],"d":"Neversoft","u":"Activision","g":"Sports","r":"October 18, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tony_Hawk's_American_Wasteland","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1p3c.jpg","s":"You are a new skater in the city of L.A.. The main drive of the game is that your hanging around with a skating group and its leader, who also happens to be a skating legend, at their skate park in Beverly Hills called Skate Ranch. Throughout the game you must help your friends by getting skate pieces for Skate Ranch.\n\nThe game marks the third reinvention of the series, with Pro Skater being the first, and Underground being the second. It comes with brand new features like the ability to change your personal appearance in game, as well as the ability to get off of the skateboard and use a BMX. For the first time all of levels are strung together into one big environment, which gets rid of loading times and menu selection.\n\nOld features were also kept like Create-a-park, which dates back to the Pro Skater series. Missions are still acquired by going up to random people or friends and accepting the mission they want you to run.\n\nThe game also includes a multiplayer mode and co-op for up to 2 players for added replay value."},{"t":"Tony Hawk's Underground 2: Remix","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"March 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tony_Hawk%27s_Underground_2"},{"t":"Top Spin","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 26","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Top_Spin_(video_game)"},{"t":"Tork: Prehistoric Punk","p":["Xbox"],"d":"Tiwak","u":"Ubisoft","g":"Platform","r":"January 12, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tork:_Prehistoric_Punk","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coa5hp.jpg","s":"Not even time can stand in the way of Tork. This cave boy must travel through time to find those responsible for kidnapping his father and destroying his village. Not your ordinary hero, Tork can change into three spirit animals: a yeti, an armadillo, or a flying squirrel. As Tork, you must face dinosaurs, gargoyles, robots, and more as you fight your way from the Stone Age to the Age of Fantastical Machines. Dodge avalanches, volcanoes, and machines in a variety of fantastic environments."},{"t":"Total Overdose","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Deadline Games","u":"SCi Games","g":"Third-person shooter","r":"September 16, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Total_Overdose","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1p3i.jpg","s":"Take control of Ramiro Cruz, a man on a crazy mission through Mexico's drug-fueled underworld. An amazing combat system keeps the action intense, mixing third person action with an incredible combo system for maximum carnage - and maximum replayability. Hilarious special moves and a huge amount of weaponry makes Total Overdose as frantic and fun an adventure as you could ever hope to find, and a red-hot latin soundtrack fits the action perfectly. This can be the perfect Latino gangsta sandbox game you were looking for all your life!"},{"t":"Totally Spies!","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Totally_Spies!_(video_game)"},{"t":"Touch Dictionary","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"YBM Sisa","u":"Daiwon C&A Holdings","g":"Dictionary","r":"July 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Touch_Dictionary","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co314o.jpg","s":"A Korean dictionary for the Nintendo DS. The original title (Touch Dic) caused mild controversy due to its name sounding perverse to native English speakers. It was later renamed to \"Touch Dictionary\"."},{"t":"Tower Bloxx","p":["Mobile phone","Browser","Windows Mobile","BlackBerry OS"],"d":"Digital Chocolate Helsinki","u":"Digital Chocolate","g":"Puzzle, casual","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tower_Bloxx","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3t02.jpg","s":"Build a skyscraper by stacking floors on top of each other. You do this by dropping them from a crane."},{"t":"Toy Golf","p":["Gizmondo","Windows"],"d":"Ninai Games","u":"Fathammer, Zoo Digital Publishing","g":"Golf","r":"May 4, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toy_Golf","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/rudid8jlpugcanwfrkq9.jpg","s":"Toy Golf is a fantasy golf game for the Gizmondo."},{"t":"TrackMania Sunrise","p":["Windows"],"d":"Nadeo","u":"Focus Home Interactive, Digital Jesters, Enlight","g":"Racing","r":"April 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TrackMania_Sunrise","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1v1p.jpg","s":"TrackMania Sunrise is the sequel to TrackMania and featured 3 new environments and new game modes."},{"t":"Trainz Railway Simulator 2006","p":["Windows"],"d":"Auran","u":"Auran, Just Trains, Merscom, Nordic Softsales","g":"Train simulation, strategy","r":"August 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trainz_Railway_Simulator_2006"},{"t":"Trapt","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Tecmo","u":"Tecmo","g":"Action-Strategy","r":"June 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trapt_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co51ki.jpg","s":"Tecmo presents TRAPT for the PS2, a puzzle-based game that contains a number of horror elements in its interesting storyline. The game is a continuation of the KAGERO: Deception series that began on the Playstation, but players aren't required to play the original games to understand TRAPT. The storyline begins when Princess Allura is framed for killing her father. As she flees the castle, players learn her dark secret: she's possessed by a demon known as Fiend. Fiend allows Allura to set a number of different traps to kill people, giving Fiend souls to survive off of. As the storyline progresses, players learn more about Fiend and how he came to possess the princess. The gameplay in TRAPT is very unique. As Allura, players run around the room setting traps while avoiding enemies. Once up to nine traps are set, they can be activated once an enemy is near. The traps come in a number of different types, including floor traps like bombs, wall traps like spikes, and ceiling traps like metal balls. Once players understand the system, they can start laying out traps in a way that an enemy will be hit by several at once to create a combo. Of course, it isn't quite that simple: some enemies are immune to certain traps, and some rooms contain areas where traps can't be placed. TRAPT weaves together unique characters, horror elements, and a fun, different gameplay style to create a unique game that will provide hours of challenge."},{"t":"Trash","p":["Windows"],"d":"Inhuman Games","u":"Inhuman Games","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"September 20, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trash_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cobn4a.jpg","s":"Trash is a real-time strategy computer game developed by Inhuman Games for the Microsoft Windows operating systems. It was released on September 20, 2005."},{"t":"Trauma Center: Under the Knife","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"October 4"},{"t":"Tribal Trouble","p":["Windows","macOS","Linux"],"d":"Oddlabs","u":"GarageGames","g":"Real-time strategy","r":"March 31, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tribal_Trouble"},{"t":"True Crime: New York City","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox","GameCube"],"r":"November 15"},{"t":"Tsuyokiss","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsuyokiss"},{"t":"TT Superbikes Real Road Racing","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Jester Interactive","u":"Jester Interactive, Valcon Games","g":"Racing, simulation","r":"April 29, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TT_Superbikes_Real_Road_Racing","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/h9wmdsgvstmlnimizsyl.jpg","s":"Suzuki TT Superbikes features more than 50 vehicles from all over the world, and includes the world famous 37.73 mile Isle of Mann racetrack. For the highest level of realism possible, the course itself has been mapped using data supplied by the government and data captured by the development team. In addition to the traditional racing, the game also features a \"Mad Sunday\" mode that brings riders from all over the world to test their chops on the mountain. Supplementary modes, such as two-player split-screen and sidecar multiplayer are also included, as are bikes from all classes -- from 125cc all the way to the F1 1000ccs!"},{"t":"Tumblebugs","p":["macOS","Windows","Wii"],"d":"Wildfire Studios","u":"GameHouse, Big Fish Games","g":"Puzzle","r":"May 18, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tumblebugs","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5npm.jpg","s":"Tumblebugs is a casual game of the match-3 genre. Players are required to shoot different coloured balls into a existing queue to make groups of three or more of the same colour, scoring points for larger groups and activating powerups.\n\nThe game takes place across over 30 distinct backgrounds and over 70 different levels which are divided into 12 stages and 5-8 rounds per stage.\n\nThe story is based around the hero, Tumble, who is saving her tumblebug friends from the evil Black Bug Empire. Tumble is the mechanism by which the player shoots the balls to make matches."},{"t":"Twisted Metal: Head-On","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"March 24"},{"t":"TY the Tasmanian Tiger 3: Night of the Quinkan","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"November 1"},{"t":"UFO: Aftershock","p":["Windows"],"d":"Altar Interactive","u":"Cenega Publishing, Tri Synergy","g":"Real-time tactics, Strategy video game","r":"October 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UFO:_Aftershock","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2cqc.jpg","s":"UFO: Aftershock is the second in a three-game squad-based tactical strategy-RPG series clearly inspired by the original X-COM games, with similar themes and gameplay, but with its own post-apocalyptic horror spin on the concept. The game is rendered in isometric 3D and, unlike its turn-based predecessor, features tactical combat in real-time with pause.\n\nIt is the year 2054. Fifty years after the disaster. Fifty years after the surface of Earth became uninhabitable. Retreating to the flying haven of the Laputa the remnants of humankind clung onto existence. Then a revolt against the increasingly rigid and corrupt human leadership of the Laputa escalated into a conflict that destroyed the colony. Now, the remaining survivors flee once again. Can they reclaim the Earth from the unknown forces that chased them into the skies?"},{"t":"Ultima V: Lazarus","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"Team Lazarus","u":"Team Lazarus","g":"Role-playing","r":"December 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultima_V:_Lazarus"},{"t":"Ultimate Block Party","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"December 13","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultimate_Block_Party"},{"t":"Ultimate Spider-Man","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","Game Boy Advance","Nintendo DS"],"r":"September 22","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultimate_Spider-Man_(video_game)"},{"t":"Ultraman Fighting Evolution Rebirth","p":["PlayStation 2"],"g":"Fighting","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultraman_Fighting_Evolution_Rebirth","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co8yqt.jpg","s":"Ultraman Fighting Evolution Rebirth is the 4th game in the Ultraman Fighting Evolution series. This game was released in the PlayStation 2 console.\n\nIts Story Mode involves Alien Mephilas launching a massive invasion using EX monsters (more powerful versions of the originals) and sending three 'Chaosroids' (dark versions of Ultraman, Ultraseven, and Ultraman Taro) to the Land of Light. Eventually, Mephiles fuses with his final monster, Neo Chaos Darkness. With the combined effort between Cosmos and the other Ultras, they managed to defeat him and stop his invasion."},{"t":"Uncharted Waters Online","p":["Windows","PlayStation 3"],"d":"Koei Tecmo","u":"Netmarble→OGPlanet→Papaya Play, Koei→Koei Tecmo, Netmarble, Softstar→Cayenne Tech","g":"MMORPG","r":"March 3, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uncharted_Waters_Online","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4hrc.jpg","s":"Discover yourself in the “Age of Discovery” where you’ll sail out into the uncharted waters! Discover real historical artifacts and mystical legends! Start a company and make enormous fortunes! Fight in fierce sea battles! Whatever your play style, you can play who you want and how you want in UWO!"},{"t":"Under Defeat","p":["Arcade"],"d":"G.rev","u":"Sega, G.rev","g":"Shoot 'em up","r":"October 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Under_Defeat","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2pog.jpg","s":"Under Defeat is a shoot 'em up arcade game by G.rev. It was released for the Sega Dreamcast in March 2006. The game takes place in an alternate reality based on World War II, and, in a controversial twist, players control German-speaking characters (under the banner of \"the Empire\"), fighting against enemies (\"the Union\") that speak English and possess weapons patterned after those of both real-life Allied and Axis powers (for example, naval units in Level 2 bear heavy resemblance toward the Imperial Japanese warships). The game was released very late in the life of the Dreamcast, but sold much better than expected, probably because there were no other home ports planned in the foreseeable future.\n\nPlayers assume control of a helicopter, which can be rotated like a more limited version of the mechanism in Zero Gunner 2. Gameplay is largely very traditional, and bears a strong resemblance to some older Toaplan games, especially Twin Cobra. It uses 3D graphics, and a slightly angled perspective to give the game more depth than most other titles in the genre.\n\nOn October 27, 2011, G.rev announced a remake titled Under Defeat HD to be released for the PlayStation 3 and Xbox 360.[1] The game is released by Rising Star Games on February 23, 2012 in Japan, November 9, 2012 in the UK and set to be released on November 28, 2012 in North America for PlayStation 3 only and January 25, 2013 in Europe. The Xbox 360 version for North America was released on August 26, 2014 as a downloadable game-only under Games on Demand. An upgraded version of Under Defeat HD (PS3, Xbox 360) was made on Sega Ring Edge 2 arcade System, named Under Defeat HD+. Now that version is coming to arcades with some improvements via Sega’s ALL.NET. Among the enhancements this will have is a horizontal orientation mode, more detail in the battlefield and a “New Order” mode where apparently you can choose from different types of aircraft."},{"t":"Under Siege","p":["Windows"],"d":"Afkar Media","u":"Dar al-Fikr","g":"First-person shooter","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Under_Siege_(2005_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4hw4.jpg","s":"The game begins at the 1995 Cave of the Patriarchs massacre. The player takes on the role of Ahmed, who must incapacitate the shooter Baruch Goldstein, and subsequently fight Israeli forces. The player then takes the role of a 13 year old boy named Mann. Mann steals a flag from the back of a Merkava tank, and is killed by the enraged tank crew."},{"t":"Unreal Championship 2: The Liandri Conflict","p":["Xbox"],"r":"April 18"},{"t":"Untold Legends: Brotherhood of the Blade","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Sony Online Entertainment","u":"Sony Online Entertainment","g":"Action role-playing","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Untold_Legends:_Brotherhood_of_the_Blade","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1poh.jpg","s":"Untold Legends is a hack'n'slash game for the PSP."},{"t":"Urban Dead","p":["Browser"],"d":"Kevan Davis","g":"Survival horror MMORPG","r":"July 3, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urban_Dead","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/znpm5igsmfmt8b6hrdg8.jpg","s":"A free text based zombie themed MMO, with player classes involving military, citizens, scientists, and zombies."},{"t":"Urban Jungle","p":["Windows"],"d":"Urban Development","u":"Autoklub Rijeka, Talented Programmers Association of Rijeka","g":"Educational driving game","r":"December 6, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urban_Jungle"},{"t":"Urban Reign","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Namco","u":"Namco, Namco Hometek, Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Beat 'em up","r":"September 13, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urban_Reign","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4lbo.jpg","s":"Urban Reign is a Namco-produced 3D brawler, done in the tradition of Double Dragon and Final Fight."},{"t":"Ururun Quest: Koiyuuki","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Vingt-et-un Systems","u":"D3","g":"Love Simulation+RPG","r":"July 28, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ururun_Quest:_Koiyuuki","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5j91.jpg","s":"Ururun Quest - Koiyuuki is a fully voiced Japanese PS2 videogame classified as an 'Onna no Ko Senyou (Girl-targeted) Love Simulation+RPG' by its developer. It was released in 2005 and marketed as the first 'RPG targeted towards girls'. The player acts as the main character, Ruri, while she adventures around her world with her friends and finding new companions."},{"t":"Vega Strike","p":["Linux","Windows","macOS"],"d":"The Vega Strike Team","g":"Space simulation","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vega_Strike"},{"t":"Vespers","p":["Windows","Linux","Browser","macOS"],"g":"Simulator","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vespers_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/yp7k0lqqnsudacoqlgml.jpg","s":"A piece of interactive fiction written by Jason Devlin."},{"t":"Vietcong 2","p":["Windows"],"d":"Pterodon, Illusion Softworks, a.s.","u":"2K","g":"First-person shooter, tactical shooter","r":"October 26, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietcong_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2xfl.jpg","s":"Vietcong 2 is the next installment in the million+ selling Vietcong franchise, set against the background of the 1968 Tet Offensive during the Vietnam War. Brought to life through a gritty story written by well-known authors, compiled from first-hand accounts of Special Forces and Infantry servicemen stationed in Hue during the assault. Based on these historical accounts, the player will take the role of a US Captain tasked with escorting a war reporter covering the traditional New Year (Tet) festivities during a ceasefire. Follow the progress of the infamous Tet Offensive from joyous New Year celebrations in the US compound, through bloody conflict across 14 distinct locations, to the final push to reclaim the Imperial Palace and the city of Hue."},{"t":"Viewtiful Joe: Double Trouble!","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"November 8"},{"t":"Viewtiful Joe: Red Hot Rumble","p":["GameCube"],"r":"November 8"},{"t":"Virtua Quest","p":["PlayStation 2","GameCube"],"r":"January 18","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtua_Quest"},{"t":"Virtua Tennis: World Tour","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"October 7"},{"t":"Virtual Magic Kingdom","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"Walt Disney Parks and Resorts, Sulake Corporation","u":"Walt Disney Parks and Resorts","g":"Massively multiplayer online game","r":"May 23, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtual_Magic_Kingdom"},{"t":"Virtual Pool: Tournament Edition","p":["Xbox"],"d":"Celeris","u":"Global Star Software","g":"Sports simulation – snooker & pool","r":"May 11, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtual_Pool:_Tournament_Edition","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/e9mee56l1b7pm2p8qqjc.jpg","s":"The leader in video game billiards chalks up for console with Virtual Pool: Tournament Edition. Virtual Pool offers 18 different pool games on tables from chic Monte Carlo to a dirty biker bar. Shoot some stick with the most advanced billiard physics ever experienced as you bank, angle, and English the trickiest shots imaginable. Virtual Pool: Tournament Edition is widely recognized as the most realistic pool simulator ever developed!\nFeatures:\n\nMultiple locations: a suburban garage, dusty biker bar, and a beachside mansion\n18 varieties of pool: 8-ball, 9-ball, Snooker, and 1- and 3-Cushion Billiards\nEasy to play: as quick as setting up a shot on a real pool table\nAuthentic gameplay: most accurate table and ball physics ever--balls roll, fly, and bounce off the table\nLibrary of artistic trick shots: or set up your own to become a true shark"},{"t":"Vivisector: Beast Within","p":["Windows"],"d":"Action Forms","u":"1C Company","g":"First-person shooter","r":"September 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vivisector:_Beast_Within","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co7k1j.jpg","s":"An FPS retelling of 'The Island of Doctor Moreau', this game pits you against an army of heavily armed genetically engineered half-man half-animal soldiers."},{"t":"Voyage: Inspired by Jules Verne","p":["Windows"],"d":"Kheops Studio, Microids","u":"The Adventure Company, Microids","g":"Adventure","r":"August 16, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voyage:_Inspired_by_Jules_Verne","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co221h.jpg","s":"Make fantastic discoveries and dare to go into the deepest depths of the moon to solve puzzles that will allow you to go back to Earth."},{"t":"Wallace & Gromit: The Curse of the Were-Rabbit","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"October 7"},{"t":"War World","p":["Windows"],"d":"Third Wave Games","u":"Third Wave Games, Flashman Studios, Lighthouse Interactive","g":"Action, First-person Shooter","r":"August 2, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_World_(video_game)"},{"t":"Warhammer 40,000: Dawn of War: Winter Assault","p":["Windows"],"r":"September"},{"t":"WarioWare: Touched!","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"February 14"},{"t":"WarioWare: Twisted!","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"May 23"},{"t":"WarTech: Senko no Ronde","p":["Arcade"],"d":"G.rev","u":"Sega, G.rev, Ubisoft","g":"Fighting/Shooter","r":"April 26, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WarTech:_Senko_no_Ronde","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co5jah.jpg","s":"WarTech: Senko no Ronde thrusts the player into a distant future where humanity has colonized countless new galaxies and Earth has become a planet mined for its natural resources. A violent war has erupted as nations struggle for world domination. Rounder Mechs fill the skies as the fate of the world is determined through aerial combat."},{"t":"We Love Katamari","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"September 20","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/We_Love_Katamari"},{"t":"Whac-A-Mole","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"September 20","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whac-A-Mole"},{"t":"Wild Arms 4","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Media.Vision","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment, Xseed Games, 505 Game Street","g":"Role-playing","r":"March 24, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wild_Arms_4","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co61vm.jpg","s":"You play as a young teenager named Jude Maverick. You live in a quiet village that floats high above the ground, unaware of the world that lies beneath it. But one day, your world is shattered to pieces, and you descend onto the earth to face the terrible reality: the world of Filgaia was devastated by wars. A few settlements amidst rusty tanks is all that is left of civilization. The democratically elected government has some plans for improving the conditions of the world, but as you meet a young girl whom they used as a tool for their purpose, you realize you must find a better plan to save her, and the world, from complete destruction.\n\nThe fourth installment of the Wild Arms series abandons its traditional Wild West theme and is set in a post-apocalyptic world. The gameplay system introduces hex-based battles. Battle screens are divided into seven hexes, each one of which can hold several party members or foes. You navigate your characters on the battle field, trying to force the enemy into an uncomfortable position. There is also a variety of skills you can learn and apply in battles to get benefits. As in previous Wild Arms games, the dungeons contain many environmental puzzles to solve."},{"t":"Wild Arms Alter Code: F","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"November 15"},{"t":"Wildlife Tycoon: Venture Africa","p":["Windows","macOS"],"d":"Pocketwatch Games","u":"Pocketwatch Games, MumboJumbo","g":"Simulation","r":"October 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wildlife_Tycoon:_Venture_Africa","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co697h.jpg","s":"From the back-catalog of Pocketwatch Games, 2005's Wildlife Tycoon: Venture Africa was the game that started this indie's journey.\n\nExpect the unexpected out of this unique Tycoon game -- There are no people to please, there is no money to horde, there are only animals. Packs of hungry lions, families of chattering baboons, and epic herds of wildebeests fill the ecosystems that players create and control."},{"t":"Winnie the Pooh's Rumbly Tumbly Adventure","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2","Game Boy Advance"],"r":"February 8","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winnie_the_Pooh%27s_Rumbly_Tumbly_Adventure"},{"t":"Wipeout Pure","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"March 24","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wipeout_Pure"},{"t":"Without Warning","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Circle Studio","u":"Capcom","g":"Third-person shooter","r":"October 28, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Without_Warning_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1rwz.jpg","s":"Without Warning is a third-person, arcade-style shooter video game set in a vast chemical plant. In the midst of a brutal terrorist plot, the game follows the actions of the six playable characters; three Special Forces members, a security guard, a secretary, and a cameraman. Set over twelve hours, the feel of the game, storywise, is similar in style to the TV series 24.\n\nWithout Warning was developer Circle Studio's only video game, before the company began focusing on DVD games as opposed to console games. It was also the first game that Capcom published that was developed by a Western company. Despite relatively high expectations during development, given the developers' previous work on the hugely successful Tomb Raider series, upon release, it received generally negative feedback by most game critics and players due to an evidently rushed release. Most complaints centred on the glitchy AI and numerous other technical inadequacies, coupled with a poor storyline and characters."},{"t":"Wizard","p":["Atari 2600"],"d":"Atari, Inc.","u":"Atari, Inc.","g":"Maze","r":"October 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wizard_(2005_video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co38sz.jpg","s":"Wizard was to be the last of Atari's 2600 games, but went unreleased in favor of the new 5200 games. Chris Crawford puts it this way:\n\n\"Wizard was spec'd as a 2K game, but just four months later, when it was ready, the marketing people had decided that everything should be 4K, so they asked me if I could expand it to 4K. To be honest, I really didn't want to work on the 2600 -- I was eager to get going on the 800. So I told them that you don't just expand a 2K game to 4K: you start from scratch and design it for 4K from the ground up. That was true, and marketing lost interest, so I got to move to the 800.\"\n\nSince Wizard was never advertised in any Atari catalogs and it was never assigned a part number, most people don't even know if its existence.\n\nWizard can best be described as a cross between Berzerk and Wizard of Wor. You control a wizard (at least I think he's a wizard), who must attempt to destroy the swirling star shaped creature. The board layout is a giant maze, which makes it hard to run from the creature and to get a clean shot off. Unfortunately the creature can move through the maze walls, but thankfully it can't shoot through them. Once you take a shot you'll notice that your wizard dims a bit, this means you are recharging, and cannot shoot. Once your wizard is done recharging he will light back up again, and you can take another shot. You don't have to worry about aiming you shots, as you will automatically shoot in the direction of the creature. This makes it easy to run away but still take shots at the creature."},{"t":"Wonderland Online","p":["Windows"],"u":"IGG Inc., Chinese Gamer Intl.","g":"Massively Multiplayer Online Role-playing Game","r":"December 14, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wonderland_Online"},{"t":"World Poker Tour","p":["Game Boy Advance","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Backbone Emeryville, Coresoft","u":"2K","g":"Card game","r":"October 18, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Poker_Tour_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co6fl6.jpg","s":"Bet, raise and bluff your way to the top as you make your mark in the virtual poker world by creating your very own character and controlling the destiny of your career. Gain experience points at every table, bump up career earnings with every win and even flaunt your poker prowess by decking out your player with accessories available for purchase with your earnings. Then, take your stack online to compete against players across the country, set up poker nights with your friends, and chat live. An exclusive presentation system featuring graphics and camera angles modeled after the popular World Poker Tour television show and insightful commentary by WPT commentators Mike Sexton and Vince Van Patten, turn your living room into seat at a WPT table."},{"t":"World Racing 2","p":["PlayStation 2","Windows","Xbox"],"d":"Synetic","u":"Playlogic Entertainment, Evolved Games, TDK","g":"Racing","r":"September 29, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Racing_2","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9bsh.jpg","s":"Compared to its predecessor, where players could only drive different Mercedes Benz cars, this sequel allows them to control over 90 different cars from 17 different manufacturers, such as Alfa Romeo, Morgan, and others.\n\nThe core of the game is the career-mode with 120 races which take players all around the globe, from Italy to Florida, where players can earn their 'Speedbucks' to buy new cars and tuning options.\n\nThe game also features oncoming traffic and a detailed damage model including realistic driving physics. Players can also customize their cars with vinyls, alloy rims and many other extras."},{"t":"World Rally Championship","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Traveller's Tales","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment, Namco Bandai Games","g":"Racing","r":"November 18, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Rally_Championship_(2005_video_game)"},{"t":"World Series of Poker","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Windows","GameCube","PlayStation Portable"],"r":"August 31","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Series_of_Poker_(video_game)"},{"t":"World Snooker Championship 2005","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox","PlayStation Portable"],"d":"Blade Interactive","u":"Sega","g":"Sports","r":"April 15, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Snooker_Championship_2005_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4eoi.jpg","s":"Part of the World Snooker Championship Franchise developed by Blade Interactive."},{"t":"World Tour Soccer: Challenge Edition","p":["PlayStation Portable"],"r":"March 14"},{"t":"Worms 4","p":["Windows","PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"r":"July 29","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Worms_4"},{"t":"Worms 4: Mayhem","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox","Windows"],"d":"Team17","u":"Codemasters, Majesco","g":"Artillery, strategy","r":"July 29, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Worms_4:_Mayhem","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/coagzr.jpg","s":"The Worms series continues with Worms 4: Mayhem. You can engage in the turn-based combat that the series has become known for across predesigned or random 3D maps. Worms 4: Mayhem delivers new weapons as well as more customization options, allowing you to design your teams and the arsenal that they use. You can unlock bonuses in the 25-mission story mode or play online against up to four other players."},{"t":"WRC: Rally Evolved","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"Evolution Studios","u":"Sony Computer Entertainment","g":"Racing","r":"October 27, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WRC:_Rally_Evolved","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co50bg.jpg","s":"Taste the physical extremes of rally driving and battle your way past your opponents in grueling multi-car wheel-to-wheel racing. Prepare for the unexpected as driver and co-driver negotiate on-track dangers - evade the wreckage of rival cars, navigate through flooded stages, and dodge crumbling walls and tumbling rocks. More cars than ever before from rally's past, present and future are brought to life in realistically interactive surroundings - drive over 40 awesome vehicles through rivers, raging fires, dense smoke and debris strewn terrain."},{"t":"Wrestle Kingdom","p":["Xbox 360"],"d":"Yuke's","u":"Yuke's","g":"Fighting","r":"December 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wrestle_Kingdom_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/cocckb.jpg","s":"FIGHT! The greatest pro wrestling organizations fight for domination! Create your own wrestler and become the legend of your league! Take on your rivals and dominate the opposition. Wrestle Kingdom is here!"},{"t":"WWE Aftershock","p":["N-Gage"],"d":"Exient Entertainment","u":"THQ Wireless","g":"Professional wrestling, fighting","r":"May 19, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WWE_Aftershock","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co63gl.jpg","s":"A WWE game for the N-Gage. Poorly received because of its limited choice of characters and long loading times."},{"t":"WWE Day of Reckoning 2","p":["GameCube"],"r":"August 29","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WWE_Day_of_Reckoning_2"},{"t":"WWE SmackDown! vs. Raw 2006","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"November 15","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WWE_SmackDown!_vs._Raw_2006"},{"t":"WWE WrestleMania 21","p":["Xbox"],"r":"April 20","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WWE_WrestleMania_21_(video_game)"},{"t":"X-Men Legends II: Rise of Apocalypse","p":["Windows","GameCube","PlayStation 2","Xbox","PlayStation Portable"],"r":"September 20"},{"t":"X-Moto","p":["Linux","Windows","macOS"],"g":"Racing","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X-Moto","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co9tlb.jpg","s":"X-Moto is a free and open source 2D motocross platform game developed for Linux, FreeBSD, Mac OS X and Microsoft Windows, where physics play an all important role in the gameplay. The basic gameplay clones that of Elasto Mania, but the simulated physics are subtly different."},{"t":"X3: Reunion","p":["Windows"],"d":"Egosoft","u":"Deep Silver, Enlight, Linux Game Publishing","g":"Space simulation","r":"October 28, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X3:_Reunion","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1rkd.jpg","s":"The Sequel to the award winning X2: The Threat introduces a new 3D engine as well as a new story, new ships and a new gameplay to greatly increase the variety in the X-universe. The economy of X3: Reunion is more complex than anything seen in the X-universe before. Factories are being built by NPCs, wars can affect the global economy, NPCs can trade freely and pirates behave far more realistically.\n\nSpace just got a whole lot bigger with the addition of two new sectors and the introduction of the gargantuan Player HQ which allows many exciting new features including the ability to build your own ships and even give them customized space paint finishes. In addition to the new M7 battleship, there is an assortment of new weapons and onboard ship devices to use and explore."},{"t":"Xanadu Next","p":["N-Gage","Windows"],"d":"Nihon Falcom, ScriptArts","u":"Nihon Falcom, Xseed Games, Nokia","g":"Action role-playing","r":"June 20, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xanadu_Next","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3l8l.jpg","s":"Xanadu Next is an exploration-centric action RPG from Nihon Falcom, the acclaimed creators of the Ys and The Legend of Heroes RPG franchises. A late entry in their immensely popular Dragon Slayer series and a spiritual follow-up to the late ‘80s cult classic Faxanadu, Xanadu Next puts players in the shoes of a gravely injured knight given a new lease on life through ancient magic who must now seek a legendary sword called “Dragon Slayer” to ensure his survival."},{"t":"Xenosaga Episode II: Jenseits von Gut und Böse","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"February 15"},{"t":"Yakuman DS","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"Nintendo SPD, MediaKite","u":"Nintendo","g":"Puzzle","r":"March 31, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yakuman_DS","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2why.jpg","s":"Yakuman DS is a Nintendo developed and published Nintendo DS game released early in 2005. The game is a DS variant of Mahjong that features Mario characters"},{"t":"Yakuza","p":["PlayStation 2"],"r":"December 8","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yakuza_(video_game)"},{"t":"Yo-Jin-Bo","p":["Windows"],"d":"Two-Five","u":"Two-Five, Hirameki International","g":"Visual novel, Otome game","r":"July 29, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yo-Jin-Bo","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4p9c.jpg","s":"Yo-Jin-Bo: The Bodyguards is a Japanese visual novel produced by Two-Five."},{"t":"Yoake Mae yori Ruriiro na","p":[],"l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoake_Mae_yori_Ruriiro_na"},{"t":"Yogurting","p":["Windows"],"d":"NTIX Soft, Neowiz, REDDUCK Inc.","u":"GungHo","g":"MMORPG","r":"May 10, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yogurting","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3r73.jpg","s":"Yogurting was a massively multiplayer online role-playing game. It was set in a modern-day setting with supernatural elements, and focused on the events occurring in the high schools Estiva and So-weol Academy. A mysterious event known as \"Endless Vacation\" caused teachers and entire schools disappear, and the students must discover who or what stands behind that phenomenon."},{"t":"Yoshi Topsy-Turvy","p":["Game Boy Advance"],"r":"June 13","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoshi%27s_Universal_Gravitation"},{"t":"Yoshi Touch & Go","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"March 14","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoshi_Touch_%26_Go"},{"t":"Yoshitsune Eiyūden: The Story of Hero Yoshitsune","p":["PlayStation 2"],"d":"FromSoftware","u":"FromSoftware","g":"Hack and slash, real-time strategy","r":"January 13, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoshitsune_Eiy%C5%ABden:_The_Story_of_Hero_Yoshitsune"},{"t":"Ys: The Oath in Felghana","p":["Windows"],"d":"Nihon Falcom","u":"Xseed Games, Nihon Falcom","g":"Action role-playing","r":"June 30, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ys:_The_Oath_in_Felghana","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4kwe.jpg","s":"Ys: The Oath in Felghana is a 3D reimagining of Ys III: Wanderers from Ys. It is an action role-playing game featuring real-time combat, interconnected areas, platforming elements, and large boss encounters. This version is based on the original 2005 PC release and includes an English localization, achievements, and cloud saving."},{"t":"Yu-Gi-Oh! Nightmare Troubadour","p":["Nintendo DS"],"d":"Konami Computer Entertainment Japan","u":"Konami","g":"Digital collectible card game","r":"July 21, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yu-Gi-Oh!_Nightmare_Troubadour","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co3dfn.jpg","s":"Yu-Gi-Oh! Duel Monsters: Nightmare Troubadour is the first time that the Yu-Gi-Oh dueling card game has appeared on the Nintendo DS. You can build a deck out of more than 1000 cards, including three exclusive trading cards that come with each game. The bottom screen represents the card game area, utilizing full touch capabilities, and the upper levels displays characters as they battle in full 3D. Yu-Gi-Oh! Duel Monsters: Nightmare Troubadour also supports wireless play, letting you challenge your friends to a duel or trade cards wirelessly."},{"t":"Yume Miru Kusuri: A Drug That Makes You Dream","p":["Windows"],"d":"Rúf","u":"Rúf, Peach Princess","g":"Eroge, visual novel","r":"December 22, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yume_Miru_Kusuri:_A_Drug_That_Makes_You_Dream"},{"t":"Zatch Bell! Mamodo Battles","p":["GameCube","PlayStation 2"],"r":"October 19","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zatch_Bell!_Mamodo_Battles"},{"t":"Zathura","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"High Voltage Software","u":"2K","g":"Action-adventure game, platformer","r":"November 3, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zathura_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co1rvw.jpg","s":"The intergalactic journey begins when a mysterious board game thrusts the house of two young brothers, Walter and Danny, into outer space. Battle deadly aliens, menacing robots and other celestial hazards in this space journey filled with action-packed adventure!"},{"t":"Zill O'll Infinite","p":["PlayStation 2"],"g":"Role-playing (RPG)","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zill_O'll_Infinite","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co4o37.jpg","s":"Zill O’ll Infinite is a remastered and expanded version of the original PS1 JRPG Zill O’ll, released for the PlayStation 2. It features updated graphics and audio, new characters, dungeons, scenarios, and multiple endings. Set in the open world of Vyashion, players create a customizable character and complete missions through an adventurer’s guild. The game offers turn-based combat and a flexible story path shaped by player choices and relationships with various NPCs, leading to over 50 possible endings.\n\nAn enhanced PSP version, Zill O’ll Infinite Plus, added even more content and story elements."},{"t":"Zoo Keeper","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"January 18","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zoo_Keeper_(2003_video_game)"},{"t":"Zoo Tycoon 2: Endangered Species","p":["Windows"],"r":"October 18"},{"t":"Zoo Tycoon DS","p":["Nintendo DS"],"r":"October 11","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zoo_Tycoon_DS"},{"t":"Æon Flux","p":["PlayStation 2","Xbox"],"d":"Terminal Reality","u":"Majesco","g":"Action-adventure","r":"November 15, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%86on_Flux_(video_game)","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co2g3w.jpg","s":"This is the 2005 release, not to be confused with the other two prior cancelled attempts at an adaptation.\n\nIn order to coincide with the release of the upcoming film, developer Terminal Reality was tasked with creating a game to tie-in with the film. The team was only given ten months to finish the game, a relatively short time for a non-sequel console game (especially in 2005), as it had to be out in time for the movie's theatrical premier. Still, Terminal Reality rose to the task and managed to create a complete Æon Flux game in less than a year, due in part to the fact that the developer created much of the game using an engine they had already built for their previous title, BloodRayne 2, which cut down on development time dramatically. Nine years after the first ill-fated attempt and five years after the second, an Æon Flux game was finally completed and released to the market in November 2005."},{"t":"ÜberSoldier","p":["Windows"],"d":"Burut Creative Team","u":"Russobit-M, CDV","g":"First-person shooter","r":"November 18, 2005","l":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%9CberSoldier","i":"https://images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_cover_small/co21i4.jpg","s":"UberSoldier is a World War II-based first person shooter, developed by Burut and released in 2006.\n\nUberSoldier follows the journey of the fictitious Karl Stolz, a Nazi soldier who has, through the process of being killed in duty, then being resurrected, acquired supernatural powers which aid him in combat. Just before he was indoctrinated by the Nazis, a member of the German Resistance rescued him and effectively changed his loyalties. Karl Stolz now became the UberSoldier of the German Resistance helping them destroy the \"UberSoldier fabrication\" infrastructure."}];
